E["npc:baron-revilgaz"] = {t="npc",n="Baron Revilgaz",z="stranglethorn",s="Baron Revilgaz is the cunning goblin leader of Booty Bay and the Blackwater Raiders, ruling the pirate haven on behalf of the Steamwheedle Cartel. Perched high on the balcony of the Salty Sailor Tavern, he balances fragile trade neutrality with ruthlessly pragmatic opportunism. He hires passing mercenaries to secure his investments, undermine rivals like the Bloodsail Buccaneers, and retrieve ancient relics of the jungle.",h="Baron Revilgaz is the cunning goblin leader of Booty Bay and the Blackwater Raiders, ruling the pirate haven...",sec={{t="Master of Booty Bay",b="From his vantage atop the Salty Sailor Tavern, Baron Revilgaz watches the bustling docks of Blackwater Cove through a custom enchanted spyglass. Flanked by his trusted advisor, the tauren Fleet Master Seahorn, Revilgaz exercises firm control over the town's cutpurses, merchants, and privateers. Originally a human settlement overwhelmed by trolls before the First War, the port was claimed and fortified by goblins, eventually evolving into the pirate-leaning commercial nexus of the Blackwater Raiders. Revilgaz ensures the port remains officially open to both Alliance and Horde travelers, strictly enforcing neutrality within harbor limits so that trade continues uninterrupted.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Ambition",b="Revilgaz's influence extends far past the harbor docks. When business stagnated following recent wars elsewhere in Azeroth, he seized upon the discovery of tastyfish to establish the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza, drawing crowds back to his shores. Across Stranglethorn Vale, he keeps a sharp eye on competitors and potential threats: he commissions sabotage against the Venture Company at Lake Nazferiti, closely monitors Nesingwary's hunting expedition and rogue human military camps in the north, and maintains racing trade ties with Monte Gazlowe and Pozzik at the Mirage Raceway.",sp=0},{t="The Stone of the Tides",b="Behind Revilgaz's mercantile front lies an obsession with ancient power and wealth. Investigating rumors of a haunted island off the coast, Revilgaz dispatches adventurers to uncover the legendary Stone of the Tides. The search requires consulting ancient tomes in the Stormwind Library, studying elemental residues with Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver, and recovering an ancient troll dagger from the Bloodsail Buccaneers to shatter the coastal altar shielding the stone. In doing so, Revilgaz breaks a deadly elemental curse to secure the priceless relic for his own vaults.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Baron Revilgaz?",a="Baron Revilgaz is the ruler of Booty Bay and the leader of the Blackwater Raiders. Operating on behalf of the neutral Steamwheedle Cartel, he governs the pirate haven with a mix of ruthless greed and diplomatic pragmatism.",al={"who is revilgaz","revilgaz backstory","booty bay boss","leader of booty bay"}},{q="Where can Baron Revilgaz be found?",a="He stands on the top balcony of the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay, overlooking the cove alongside his trusted advisor, Fleet Master Seahorn.",al={"where is revilgaz","revilgaz location","how to find revilgaz"}},{q="What is Revilgaz's relationship with the Bloodsail Buccaneers?",a="They are bitter enemies. The Bloodsail Buccaneers operate outside the rules of the Steamwheedle Cartel and actively raid Booty Bay shipping. In fact, Bloodsail leadership regularly plots assassinations against Revilgaz and Seahorn.",al={"revilgaz bloodsail","bloodsail vs revilgaz","why hate bloodsail"}},{q="What is Revilgaz's stake in the Mirage Raceway?",a="Revilgaz sponsors the goblin racing team led by Pozzik against the gnomes in the Shimmering Flats. He uses adventurers to steal proprietary fuel regulator blueprints from the Venture Company at Lake Nazferiti and delivers them to the raceway.",al={"revilgaz racing","revilgaz shimmer flats","revilgaz pozik"}},{q="What is the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza?",a="When trade dipped due to regional wars elsewhere in Azeroth, Revilgaz backed an angler named Riggle Bassbait after sampling the local 'tastyfish.' Revilgaz turned the catch into a weekly competitive tournament along the Stranglethorn coast to revitalize Booty Bay's economy.",al={"fishing tournament lore","who started the fishing contest","tastyfish revilgaz"}},{q="What is the Stone of the Tides?",a="It is an ancient, cursed magical stone hidden at the Vile Reef. Revilgaz unearths its legend through Stormwind records and employs Dalaran scholar Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver to help adventurers dismantle its elemental wards and claim the relic.",al={"stone of the tides quest","vile reef stone","altar of the tides"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Revilgaz respects thieves, spies, and opportunists. He frequently hires rogues for high-stakes theft, sabotage against rival cartels, and covert retrieval of rare jungle artifacts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Booty Bay rests on the ruins of the pre-First War Stormwind enclave of Blackwater Cove, and Revilgaz routinely coordinates with human scholars and librarians in Stormwind when ancient lore translates to profit.",["profession:Engineering"]="Revilgaz stays involved in goblin engineering rivalries, leveraging underhanded tactics to secure advanced blueprints and fuel regulators from the Venture Company."},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","lake nazferiti","revilgaz","salty sailor tavern","seahorn","steamwheedle cartel","stone of the tides"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","npc:fleet-master-seahorn","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","subzone:vile-reef","npc:archmage-ansirem-runeweaver","npc:monte-gazlowe","quest:764"},src={"Baron Revilgaz"}}
E["npc:colonel-kurzen"] = {t="npc",n="Colonel Kurzen",z="stranglethorn",s="Colonel Conrad Kurzen was once a decorated and noble officer of the Stormwind Army, sent to lead an expedition into northern Stranglethorn Vale. After descending into sudden madness and tyranny, he turned his force into a rogue jungle militia operating out of an armed compound. Today, his former subordinates at the nearby Rebel Camp actively seek his death to end his reign of terror.",h="Colonel Conrad Kurzen was once a decorated and noble officer of the Stormwind Army, sent to lead an...",sec={{t="A Fall from Grace",b="Before his downfall, Colonel Conrad Kurzen was regarded in Stormwind as an exceptionally capable and noble officer. Trusted by the kingdom's leadership, he was granted command of an expeditionary unit dispatched south into the dense jungles of Stranglethorn Vale. However, deep within the humid wilds, Kurzen began to exhibit erratic behavior and extreme megalomania, declaring absolute sovereignty over the surrounding wilderness and abandoning his allegiance to Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="The Rebellion",b="Kurzen's sudden transformation divided his ranks. While many soldiers succumbed to blind loyalty or twisted zealotry, others grew appalled by his madness and brutality—including his act of throwing Emerine Junis into the compound's prison simply for spurning his advances. Led by Lieutenant Doren, a group of conscience-stricken soldiers broke away to establish the Rebel Camp along the northern road. These loyalist defectors now wage a desperate war against Kurzen to stop his rampaging force.",sp=0},{t="The Ogre Behind the Curtain",b="Kurzen's madness was not born of jungle fever or natural exhaustion. The colonel fell victim to dark sorcery wrought by Mai'Zoth, a cunning ogre mage of the Mosh'ogg clan. By possessing Kurzen's mind, Mai'Zoth turned a disciplined detachment of Stormwind soldiers into violent pawns, manipulating Kurzen to exert regional control without the ogres having to wage open warfare themselves.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Why did Colonel Kurzen turn against Stormwind?",a="Sometime during his expedition into Stranglethorn Vale, Kurzen began showing erratic behavior and megalomania, abandoning his allegiance to Stormwind. What drove the once-noble colonel to madness is a mystery his former soldiers at the Rebel Camp are still trying to unravel.",al={"why is kurzen evil","what happened to kurzen","kurzen backstory"},sp=2},{q="Where is Colonel Kurzen located?",a="He commands his militia from deep within Kurzen's Compound, situated in the hills of northern Stranglethorn Vale. He resides inside the fortified Stockpile building at the back of the encampment.",al={"where to find kurzen","kurzen location","colonel kurzen compound"}},{q="Who are the rebels at the Rebel Camp?",a="The rebels are former soldiers under Kurzen's command who refused to follow his descent into madness. Led by Lieutenant Doren, they remain loyal to Stormwind and operate from the Rebel Camp near the northern border, seeking to put an end to Kurzen's rogue army.",al={"rebel camp lore","who is lieutenant doren","why rebel camp"}},{q="Who is Emerine Junis?",a="Emerine Junis was a woman attached to the expedition who rejected Kurzen's unwanted advances. In his growing cruelty and delusion, the colonel locked her away in the compound's prison cages.",al={"emerine junis","kurzen prisoner"}},{q="Is Kurzen acting alone in the jungle?",a="No. He commands the human mercenaries, soldiers, and jungle fighters who remained loyal to him after the rebels broke away to the Rebel Camp.",al={"who does kurzen work for","kurzen allies"},sp=2},{q="What happens if Colonel Kurzen is slain?",a="Lieutenant Doren asks Alliance adventurers to sever Kurzen's head to definitively prove the colonel's demise, shatter his militia's chain of command, and salvage the honor of the Stormwind Army.",al={"kurzen quest end","doren kurzen head"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Kurzen represents a severe military scandal and a tragic loss of Stormwind troops, prompting Alliance command and local loyalists to authorize his elimination.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Kurzen was once a peer and respected leader, making his brutal descent into tyranny a grim reminder of the jungle's hazards.",["class:Warrior"]="Kurzen stands as a cautionary example of disciplined martial might entirely subverted and twisted when stripped of will and honor."},kw={"colonel kurzen","conrad kurzen","doren","kurzen","kurzen's compound","rebel camp","stockpile","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:kurzen-s-compound","subzone:rebel-camp","npc:doren","zone:stranglethorn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Colonel Kurzen"}}
E["npc:doren"] = {t="npc",n="Doren",z="stranglethorn",s="Lieutenant Doren commands the Rebel Camp nestled in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Once an officer under Colonel Kurzen, Doren led a mutiny after his superior and fellow expeditionaries descended into madness. Now, he directs a guerrilla resistance determined to uncover the source of the affliction and eliminate Kurzen.",h="Lieutenant Doren commands the Rebel Camp nestled in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="A Mutiny in the Jungle",b="Lieutenant Doren initially deployed to Stranglethorn Vale under the banner of Stormwind and the command of Colonel Kurzen. The expedition was meant to establish a foothold in the wild southern jungle, but it quickly soured as Kurzen and his inner circle succumbed to an erratic, violent insanity. Refusing to abandon their sanity or their honor, Doren and a cadre of loyalists broke rank. They fled north and carved out the Rebel Camp along the road, choosing defection over servitude to a madman.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Truth",b="From their precarious outpost, Doren oversees operations against Kurzen's Compound. He maintains supply lines with neutral parties, including goblin contacts like Krazek down in Booty Bay, to keep his dwindling troops fed and armed. Beyond mere survival, Doren seeks answers: he deploys spies such as Private Thorsen behind enemy lines to discover what cursed the Colonel and to root out traitors and collaborators like Bookie Herod. Ultimately, Doren believes the only way to save what remains of their expedition's honor is to put an end to Kurzen himself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Doren?",a="Lieutenant Doren is the leader of the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Formerly second to Colonel Kurzen on an expedition from Stormwind, Doren led a breakaway faction of soldiers who refused to follow the Colonel after he went mad.",al={"who is doren","doren lore","rebel camp leader"}},{q="Why is Doren considered a rebel?",a="Doren and his troops mutinied against their commanding officer, Colonel Kurzen. Because Kurzen was the officially commissioned head of the expedition, breaking away and taking up arms against him technically made Doren and his followers rebels, even though they defected to preserve their sanity and oppose Kurzen's tyranny.",al={"why is it called rebel camp","why did doren rebel","kurzen mutiny"}},{q="What drove Colonel Kurzen mad?",a="The exact source of the madness that afflicted Kurzen and his inner circle remains a mystery that Doren actively seeks to solve. Doren uses reconnaissance and infiltrators to uncover what corrupted his former commander deep within the jungle.",al={"why did kurzen go crazy","kurzens madness"}},{q="How does Doren keep the Rebel Camp supplied?",a="Cut off from official Stormwind support, Doren relies on covert supply runs and trade arrangements with third parties. Notably, he coordinates with goblin merchants such as Krazek in the southern pirate haven of Booty Bay to keep his troops outfitted.",al={"rebel camp supplies","doren supplies"}},{q="Who is Bookie Herod and what is his connection to Doren?",a="Bookie Herod is an associate within Kurzen's forces. Doren suspects Herod was involved in uncovering the true loyalties of Doren's undercover agent, Private Thorsen, while Thorsen was infiltrating the compound.",al={"bookie herod","herod rebel camp"}},{q="Does Doren answer to Stormwind?",a="Doren remains loyal to the ideals of the Alliance, but because he broke ranks against a commanding officer in the field, he operates autonomously. He welcomes Alliance adventurers to help clean up the disastrous expedition.",al={"doren alliance","doren stormwind allegiance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance soldiers, Doren represents the tragic fallout of Stormwind's jungle expedition, offering a chance to right Kurzen's wrongs and restore order to the wild frontier.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers will recognize Doren's military discipline, a reminder of the toll that isolated duty far from the Kingdom of Stormwind can take on mind and morale."},kw={"bookie herod","colonel kurzen","doren","kurzen","kurzen's compound","lieutenant doren","rebel camp","stranglethorn","thorsen"},rel={"subzone:rebel-camp","npc:colonel-kurzen","subzone:kurzen-s-compound","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:booty-bay"},src={"Doren"}}
E["npc:fleet-master-seahorn"] = {t="npc",n="Fleet Master Seahorn",z="stranglethorn",s="Fleet Master Seahorn is a seasoned tauren mariner who serves as the naval commander of the Blackwater Raiders in Booty Bay. Stationed on the upper balcony of the Salty Sailor Tavern alongside Baron Revilgaz, he oversees the goblin port's maritime defenses. His primary duty is protecting the harbor from the looming threat posed by their sworn enemies, the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",h="Fleet Master Seahorn is a seasoned tauren mariner who serves as the naval commander of the Blackwater Raiders...",sec={{t="A Bull on the High Seas",b="While tauren are renowned across Kalimdor as plains-dwellers, Fleet Master Seahorn chose a vastly different life upon the ocean. Clad in pirate regalia, he commands the fleet of the Blackwater Raiders, the private naval arm of the Steamwheedle Cartel's operation in Stranglethorn Vale. Stationed atop the Salty Sailor Tavern, Seahorn works shoulder-to-shoulder with Baron Revilgaz, coordinating shipping routes, crew deployments, and coastal defenses for the lawless yet strictly managed port of Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="Defending the Bay",b="Seahorn's greatest ongoing concern is the Bloodsail Buccaneers, who have established fortified camps along the southern Wild Shore and anchored warships off the coast. When reports reveal that Fleet Master Firallon and the Bloodsail leadership intend to launch a direct assault to sack Booty Bay, Seahorn takes aggressive action. By dispatching mercenaries to seize enemy correspondence and neutralize Firallon, Keelhaul, and Stillwater aboard their flagship, Seahorn successfully shields the port from outright devastation.",sp=1},{t="Eyes Across the Seas",b="Beyond repelling pirate raids, Seahorn manages varied commercial and salvage ventures across the Eastern Kingdoms. He coordinates recovery efforts for lost sunken treasures off the Arathi coast near Faldir's Cove, working with salvage divers to secure elven relics. He also keeps Revilgaz informed of lucrative opportunities passing through town, such as competitive angling and local trade, ensuring the Blackwater fleet stays well-funded and ahead of rival operations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fleet Master Seahorn located?",a="He is located on the top floor and balcony of the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay, standing right beside Baron Revilgaz overlooking the docks.",al={"where is seahorn","seahorn location","find seahorn"}},{q="Why is a tauren serving as a pirate fleet master?",a="Though most tauren remain closely tied to the plains and spiritual traditions of Mulgore, Seahorn took to seafaring and mercenary naval life. His nautical skill and commanding presence earned him leadership of the Blackwater Raiders under Baron Revilgaz.",al={"tauren pirate","why is seahorn a pirate","tauren in booty bay"}},{q="What is Seahorn's relationship with Baron Revilgaz?",a="Seahorn is Baron Revilgaz's second-in-command and the naval commander of his Blackwater Raiders. While Revilgaz manages politics, trade, and finances, Seahorn oversees the fleet, tactical intelligence, and defensive military operations for Booty Bay.",al={"seahorn and revilgaz","is seahorn revilgaz bodyguard","who works for revilgaz"}},{q="Who are the Blackwater Raiders?",a="The Blackwater Raiders are a private fleet of corsairs loyal to the Steamwheedle Cartel, based out of Booty Bay. Unlike outlaw raiders who plunder indiscriminately, they act as the sanctioned navy protecting goblin merchant interests and maintaining order in the southern seas.",al={"blackwater raiders","what faction is seahorn","booty bay pirates"}},{q="Why does Seahorn want to stop the Bloodsail Buccaneers?",a="The Bloodsail Buccaneers are the bitter rivals of the Blackwater Raiders. Led by Fleet Master Firallon, the Bloodsail have set up camps along the Wild Shore and intend to conquer Booty Bay itself. Seahorn works constantly to preempt their invasion plans.",al={"seahorn vs bloodsail","bloodsail conflict","why fight bloodsail"}},{q="Does Seahorn have dealings outside of Stranglethorn Vale?",a="Yes. Seahorn works with salvage agents like Doctor Draxlegauge and Shakes O'Breen to recover lost cargo and elven treasures sunken near Faldir's Cove off the Arathi Highlands, having valuable artifacts delivered back to his post in Booty Bay.",al={"faldirs cove seahorn","seahorn sunken treasure","arathi quests seahorn"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Seahorn is one of the extremely rare tauren who has abandoned the inland plains of Kalimdor to master the open ocean, serving as fleet master for a neutral goblin port.",["faction:Horde"]="Although Seahorn is a tauren, his allegiance belongs strictly to the Steamwheedle Cartel and the Blackwater Raiders, maintaining a neutral stance toward Horde and Alliance travelers alike.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues operating in Booty Bay find Seahorn at the heart of coastal espionage, organizing covert raids against Bloodsail warships and intercepting enemy orders."},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail","booty bay","faldir's cove","firallon","fleet master seahorn","revilgaz","salty sailor tavern","seahorn","wild shore"},rel={"npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","subzone:wild-shore","subzone:faldir-s-cove","zone:stranglethorn","topic:pirate","topic:tauren"},src={"Fleet Master Seahorn"}}
E["npc:kin-weelay"] = {t="npc",n="Kin'weelay",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay is a renowned Darkspear witch doctor stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale. Dispatched directly from Orgrimmar, he offers mystical aid and counsel to the Horde vanguard in the jungle. His spiritual expertise is vital in unravelling dark mojo and aiding the rescue of young Yenniku.",h="Kin'weelay is a renowned Darkspear witch doctor stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="A Master of Darkspear Mojo",b="Recognized among the Darkspear as one of their most powerful practitioners of traditional witchcraft, Kin'weelay commands deep knowledge of spirits, hexes, and soul magic. When matters involving ancestral spirits or hostile troll enchantments arise, Horde scouts in Stranglethorn Vale look to him to pierce the magical veil.",sp=0},{t="The Mission to Grom'gol",b="Kin'weelay was sent south from the dusty streets of Orgrimmar specifically to support Nimboya at Grom'gol Base Camp. His purpose extends beyond simple military support; he focuses on breaking the sinister bindings placed upon Yenniku, the abducted son of Chieftain Vol'jin's trusted bloodline. To undo such dark craft, Kin'weelay seeks powerful reagents—most notably the Mind's Eye—to fashion a soul gem capable of freeing captured spirits.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kin'weelay?",a="Kin'weelay is an esteemed Darkspear troll witch doctor stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Known for his mastery of spiritual and soul magic, he was dispatched by the Horde leadership from Orgrimmar.",al={"kinweelay lore","who is kin'weelay","gromgol witch doctor"}},{q="Why is Kin'weelay in Stranglethorn Vale?",a="He was sent to Grom'gol Base Camp to lend his mystical talents to Nimboya and the local Darkspear expedition, particularly in finding and restoring young Yenniku from the grip of hostile jungle trolls.",al={"why is kinweelay in gromgol","kinweelay purpose"}},{q="What is Kin'weelay trying to create?",a="Kin'weelay seeks to acquire a relic known as the Mind's Eye. With his witchcraft, he intends to refine it into a soul gem that can capture and safely preserve the soul of Yenniku, severing the dark control holding the boy.",al={"kinweelay minds eye","what does kinweelay make"}},{q="Where does Kin'weelay come from?",a="He traveled from Orgrimmar, where the Darkspear tribe has maintained strong ties and presence since joining the Horde and settling the Echo Isles.",al={"kinweelay background","where did kinweelay come from"}},{q="How does he view the other troll tribes of Stranglethorn?",a="He views hostile jungle tribes, like the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter, as dangerous rivals steeped in violent, corrupted rituals. He actively uses his craft to counter their charms and recover stolen Darkspear youth.",al={"kinweelay other trolls","kinweelay and bloodscalp"}},{q="What kind of items does Kin'weelay study?",a="Kin'weelay investigates local curiosities possessing natural or hexed resonance, including the mysterious singing crystals and bone necklaces worn by hostile jungle trolls, studying their mojo to devise countermeasures.",al={"kinweelay items","singing crystals kinweelay"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Kin'weelay represents one of the tribe's most respected spiritual authorities, dedicated to undoing the cruel curses of their jungle kin.",["faction:Horde"]="Kin'weelay demonstrates the value of troll spiritualism to the Horde war effort, providing magical counter-strategies against threats that pure strength cannot break."},kw={"darkspear","grom'gol","kin'weelay","kinweelay","mind's eye","stranglethorn","witch doctor","yenniku"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","topic:horde","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:vile-reef"},src={"Kin'weelay"}}
E["quest:1127"] = {t="quest",n="Fool's Stout",z="stranglethorn",s="Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay brews batches of Fool's Stout for travelers looking to return to the Shimmering Flats raceway. To concoct another serving, he requires twelve flasks of Zanzil's mixture.",h="Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay brews batches of Fool's Stout for travelers looking to return to the Shimmering...",sec={{t="A Second Batch",b="For travelers whose initial supply of Fool's Stout has expired before reaching the gnomes at the raceway, Crank Fizzlebub offers to brew a replacement. The goblin Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay requires twelve flasks of Zanzil's mixture to prepare the potent beverage once more, compensating anyone willing to fetch the ingredients while offering a little extra to keep the transaction discreet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers to brew Fool's Stout?",a="Crank Fizzlebub, found inside Booty Bay in southern Stranglethorn Vale, prepares the stout.",al={"who gives fools stout","fools stout questgiver","crank fizzlebub"}},{q="What ingredients does Crank Fizzlebub need?",a="He requires twelve flasks of Zanzil's mixture to brew another batch of the stout.",al={"what items needed fools stout","fools stout ingredients","zanzils mixture requirement"}},{q="Why would someone need another batch of Fool's Stout?",a="The concoction evaporates after two hours, so travelers who miss that window must gather fresh ingredients for a replacement.",al={"why do fools stout again","fools stout expired","fools stout duration"}},{q="Where is the brew intended to go?",a="The brew is meant for the gnomes at the raceway.",al={"where does fools stout go","who drinks fools stout","fools stout destination"}}},kw={"booty bay","crank fizzlebub","fools stout","raceway","stranglethorn vale","zanzils mixture"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:gnome"},m={start="Crank Fizzlebub",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="44",id=1127},src={"Fool's Stout (quest)"}}
E["quest:185"] = {t="quest",n="Tiger Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="At the northern safari camp in Stranglethorn Vale, the hunter Ajeck Rouack offers to train adventurers in the discipline of big cat stalking. She starts newcomers against the younger tigers prowling near the camp to test basic hunting and tracking prowess.",h="At the northern safari camp in Stranglethorn Vale, the hunter Ajeck Rouack offers to train adventurers in the...",sec={{t="First Lessons in the Jungle",b="Having learned the art of hunting tigers from her father when she was a girl, Ajeck Rouack shares his craft with travelers who reach Nesingwary's Expedition following Welcome to the Jungle. She insists that tracking and slaying the youngest felines is the essential foundation before any hunter can advance to greater quarry.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Prowlers",b="Young Stranglethorn tigers are often found in the jungle close to the expedition camp. Rouack demands that ten of these beasts be hunted down to prove sufficient skill before she agrees to provide any further training.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers to train you in tiger hunting?",a="Ajeck Rouack, a seasoned hunter stationed at Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, offers the training.",al={"who gives tiger mastery","ajeck rouack quest","tiger quest giver"}},{q="Why does Ajeck Rouack target young tigers first?",a="Rouack considers the younger felines far easier to track and slay, making them an ideal initial trial to test a hunter's tracking skills before attempting more dangerous quarry.",al={"why young tigers","why start easy tiger mastery"}},{q="Where are the young tigers found?",a="Young Stranglethorn tigers can commonly be found stalking the jungle grounds right near the expedition's camp.",al={"where are young stranglethorn tigers","young tiger location"}},{q="What comes before this hunt?",a="This hunting trial follows the arrival quest Welcome to the Jungle, which introduces travelers to the safari camp.",al={"tiger mastery prerequisite","tiger mastery previous quest"}}},kw={"ajeck rouack","hunting","nesingwary","stranglethorn vale","tiger mastery","young stranglethorn tiger"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Ajeck Rouack",["end"]="Ajeck Rouack",level="31",id=185},src={"Tiger Mastery (Classic)"}}
E["quest:186"] = {t="quest",n="Tiger Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="At Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Ajeck Rouack escalates his hunting trials. Having seen your early promise with young stalkers, he now sends you into the jungle to fell mature Stranglethorn Tigers.",h="At Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Ajeck Rouack escalates his hunting trials.",sec={{t="Hunting the Mature Cats",b="Following your initial success against younger predators, Ajeck Rouack seeks to test your growing skills against more seasoned beasts. She directs you back out into the wilds of Stranglethorn Vale to hunt down ten mature Stranglethorn Tigers before you can pursue even greater challenges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this hunt?",a="Ajeck Rouack, a hunter stationed at Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, issues the trial.",al={"who gives tiger mastery","ajeck rouack location","who gives this quest"}},{q="What beasts are you tasked with hunting?",a="You are challenged to track and slay ten mature Stranglethorn Tigers roaming the surrounding jungle.",al={"what tigers do i kill","which cats","tiger mastery targets"}},{q="Where does this trial fit in the hunt?",a="This trial follows the initial Tiger Mastery hunt and leads directly into a third stage under Ajeck Rouack's guidance.",al={"what comes before tiger mastery 2","what is next","tiger mastery chain"}}},kw={"ajeck rouack","nesingwary's expedition","stranglethorn tigers","stranglethorn vale","tiger mastery"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Ajeck Rouack",["end"]="Ajeck Rouack",level="33",id=186},src={"Tiger Mastery (2)"}}
E["quest:187"] = {t="quest",n="Tiger Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Deep in the jungle at Nesingwary's Expedition, Ajeck Rouack raises the stakes of his hunting trials. He demands the death of ten elder Stranglethorn tigers to prove your prowess before the final test.",h="Deep in the jungle at Nesingwary's Expedition, Ajeck Rouack raises the stakes of his hunting trials.",sec={{t="A Test of Skill",b="Following the earlier hunts, Ajeck Rouack asks you to pursue ten elder Stranglethorn tigers across the wilds. He considers these beasts both the most elusive to track and the fiercest to overcome. Felling ten of them serves as the prelude to a concluding trial, after which he promises to proclaim you a master tiger hunter before Master Nesingwary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this trial?",a="Ajeck Rouack offers this trial from the camp of Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who gives tiger mastery","ajeck rouack quest","quest giver"}},{q="What quarry are you tracking?",a="You must hunt down ten elder Stranglethorn tigers.",al={"what do i kill","which tigers","tiger mastery targets"}},{q="Why are elder Stranglethorn tigers singled out?",a="Ajeck Rouack notes that elder Stranglethorn tigers are the hardest to find and the most ferocious to defeat among the local cats.",al={"why elder tigers","elder tiger difficulty"}},{q="What comes before this hunt?",a="This trial directly follows the second stage of Ajeck Rouack's Tiger Mastery series.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite"}}},kw={"ajeck rouack","big game hunting","elder stranglethorn tiger","nesingwary","stranglethorn vale","tiger mastery"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter"},m={start="Ajeck Rouack",["end"]="Ajeck Rouack",level="35",id=187},src={"Tiger Mastery (3)"}}
E["quest:188"] = {t="quest",n="Tiger Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Ajeck Rouack offers the ultimate challenge in his series of hunts within northern Stranglethorn Vale. After weeks of tracking an elusive beast, he challenges you to seek out the tiger Sin'Dall and bring back her paw.",h="Ajeck Rouack offers the ultimate challenge in his series of hunts within northern Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="The Final Tiger",b="Having completed the earlier trials against Stranglethorn's tigers, you are offered one last challenge by Ajeck Rouack at Nesingwary's Expedition. The hunting camp has tracked an extraordinarily elusive tiger known as Sin'Dall across the jungle for weeks. Ajeck challenges you to track her down, fell the beast, and claim her paw as indisputable proof.",sp=0},{t="Master Tiger Hunter",b="Returning to Nesingwary's camp with the paw of Sin'Dall proves your tracking prowess beyond question. Ajeck Rouack acknowledges your accomplishment, declaring you a true Master Tiger Hunter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt?",a="Ajeck Rouack, a seasoned huntsman stationed at Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, presents this final feline challenge.",al={"quest giver","who gives tiger mastery","ajeck rouack location"}},{q="What is Sin'Dall?",a="Sin'Dall is an elusive tiger that the hunters of Nesingwary's Expedition have been pursuing for weeks across the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"what is sindall","sindall lore","who is sin dall"}},{q="What proof does Ajeck Rouack require?",a="Ajeck Rouack requires you to return with the Paw of Sin'Dall to prove that the beast was truly bested.",al={"what do i bring back","tiger mastery proof","paw of sindall"}},{q="What precedes this hunt?",a="This hunt is the fourth and culminating step of Ajeck Rouack's series, following the third Tiger Mastery trial in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"prerequisites","tiger mastery chain","previous quest"}}},kw={"ajeck rouack","master tiger hunter","nesingwary's expedition","paw of sin'dall","sin'dall","stranglethorn vale","tiger mastery"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter"},m={start="Ajeck Rouack",["end"]="Ajeck Rouack",level="37",id=188},src={"Tiger Mastery (4)"}}
E["quest:189"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodscalp Ears",z="stranglethorn",s="Kebok in Booty Bay is losing guards and agents to jungle clashes with the Bloodscalp tribe. Worried about climbing expenses and answering to Baron Revilgaz, he offers coin to any adventurer willing to hunt down the trolls and return with proof of the kill.",h="Kebok in Booty Bay is losing guards and agents to jungle clashes with the Bloodscalp tribe.",sec={{t="Mounting Costs",b="In the bustling port of Booty Bay, Kebok faces a serious operational dilemma. The local trolls in Stranglethorn Vale have been killing his agents in the jungle, and he has lost many of his best guards in skirmishes with them. With the casualties mounting, so too are the costs, leaving him frantic over how to explain them to Baron Revilgaz.",sp=0},{t="A Bounded Bounty",b="Rather than allowing the losses to accumulate further, Kebok turns to outside help. He offers monetary compensation to travelers who head into the jungle, cull the Bloodscalp trolls, and bring back fifteen of their severed ears as undeniable confirmation of their demise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kebok?",a="Kebok is a goblin in Booty Bay who has agents and guards out in the jungle, and he has to answer to Baron Revilgaz for what they cost.",al={"kebok","who is kebok","who gives bloodscalp ears"}},{q="Why does Kebok want Bloodscalp ears?",a="Bloodscalp trolls have been killing his agents in the jungle and costing him many of his best guards in skirmishes. The costs are piling up and he has no good way to explain them to Baron Revilgaz.",al={"why ears","why bloodscalp ears","why collect ears"}},{q="How many ears are required?",a="Kebok requires fifteen Bloodscalp ears before he will hand over your payment.",al={"how many ears","ear count"}},{q="Where does this bounty lead next?",a="Once Kebok compensates you for the Bloodscalp ears, he shifts his attention to another local threat in Skullsplitter Tusks.",al={"what comes next","bloodscalp ears follow up","next quest"},sp=1}},kw={"bloodscalp","booty bay","ears","kebok","revilgaz","stranglethorn","troll"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","npc:baron-revilgaz","topic:troll","quest:209","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kebok",["end"]="Kebok",level="35",faction="Neutral",id=189},src={"Bloodscalp Ears","In-game quest text: Bloodscalp Ears"}}
E["quest:190"] = {t="quest",n="Panther Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition offers a trial to those seeking to prove their prowess as big-game stalkers in Stranglethorn Vale. To join Hemet's hunting company, adventurers must first demonstrate their basic tracking ability by taking down ten young panthers.",h="Sir S.",sec={{t="A Crack Group of Hunters",b="Within the wild expanse of northern Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary has assembled a seasoned band of big-game huntsmen. Sir S. J. Erlgadin tells anyone who wants a part of the hunt that they must first prove themselves an able panther hunter.",sp=0},{t="Tracking the Prowlers",b="Before Erlgadin entrusts anyone with greater game, he issues an entry test: finding and slaying ten young panthers. Simply finding the beasts is only half the challenge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this hunting challenge?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin gives this challenge from the camp of Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, testing newcomers who want to join Hemet's hunting party.",al={"panther mastery quest giver","who starts panther mastery","erlgadin quest"}},{q="What quarry must be hunted?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin directs hunters to track down and slay ten young panthers roaming the surrounding jungle brush.",al={"what do i kill for panther mastery","panther mastery target","young panthers"}},{q="Why does Sir S. J. Erlgadin assign this test?",a="Hemet Nesingwary has gathered a seasoned hunting crew, and Erlgadin wants newcomers to prove themselves able panther hunters before they join the hunt.",al={"why kill young panthers","purpose of panther mastery"}},{q="What comes next after completing this hunt?",a="Completing this opening trial leads directly to Panther Mastery (2), where Sir S. J. Erlgadin increases the difficulty of the quarry.",al={"panther mastery next quest","what comes after panther mastery"}}},kw={"hemet","nesingwary","panther mastery","sir s. j. erlgadin","stranglethorn vale","young panthers"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter"},m={start="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",["end"]="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",level="31",faction="Neutral",id=190},src={"Panther Mastery (Classic)"}}
E["quest:191"] = {t="quest",n="Panther Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Sir S. J. Erlgadin demands that you prove yourself worthy of the big game hunters at Nesingwary's Expedition. Following your initial cull of younger beasts, he challenges you to track down and slay ten fully grown panthers in the wilds of Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Sir S.",sec={{t="A Higher Standard",b="After dispatching the young panthers around the jungle, Sir S. J. Erlgadin asks you to raise your sights. To show that you deserve to keep company with seasoned big game hunters, you are sent out to hunt ten mature panthers, which are far tougher and more dangerous than their younger kin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this trial?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin, a hunter stationed at Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale, oversees this stage of the hunt.",al={"who gives panther mastery","erlgadin quest","quest giver"}},{q="What quarry are you asked to hunt?",a="You are asked to track down and defeat ten mature panthers in the surrounding jungle, which are tougher than the younger specimens previously targeted.",al={"what panthers to kill","which beasts","panther mastery target"}},{q="What comes before this challenge?",a="This follows an earlier trial, also titled Panther Mastery, in which Erlgadin tested your mettle against younger jungle panthers.",al={"previous quest","prior step","panther mastery prerequisite"}},{q="What is the purpose of hunting these panthers?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin requires you to prove you have the skill and fortitude to socialize and hunt alongside the seasoned big game hunters of the expedition.",al={"why kill panthers","erlgadin motive","nesingwary purpose"}}},kw={"big game","erlgadin","hunting","mastery","nesingwary","panther","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","quest:208","topic:hunter"},m={start="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",["end"]="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",level="33",id=191},src={"Panther Mastery (2)"}}
E["quest:192"] = {t="quest",n="Panther Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition challenges big game hunters to track and bring down the deadliest panthers in Stranglethorn Vale. Following your earlier trials, you must now seek out and slay ten Shadowmaw Panthers.",h="Sir S.",sec={{t="The Deadliest Quarry",b="Sir S. J. Erlgadin considers Shadowmaw Panthers to be the most dangerous cats prowling the jungles of Stranglethorn. Proving your mettle as a true stalker requires crawling through the dense underbrush to track down ten of these elusive beasts, whose ferocity makes them far harder to kill than to find.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin offers this challenge from the Nesingwary Expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who gives panther mastery","panther mastery quest giver","who gives this quest"}},{q="What beasts are you hunting?",a="You are to hunt down ten Shadowmaw Panthers, which Erlgadin calls the deadliest panthers in all of Stranglethorn.",al={"what do i kill","target of panther mastery","which panthers"}},{q="Where does this fit in the hunting trials?",a="This is the third trial in the panther hunting series, following directly after the second Panther Mastery trial and preceding the fourth.",al={"what quest comes before this","panther mastery chain","prerequisite quest"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Erlgadin challenges you directly on your reputation as a big game hunter, expecting you to master the stalking and slaying of the jungle's fiercest predators."},kw={"big game","nesingwary","panther mastery","shadowmaw panther","sir s. j. erlgadin","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter"},m={start="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",["end"]="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",level="38",faction="Neutral",id=192},src={"Panther Mastery (3)"}}
E["quest:193"] = {t="quest",n="Panther Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Sir S. J. Erlgadin has set the final trial of his panther hunt before you in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Having proven your skill against the region's panthers, you are challenged to seek out Bhag'thera, an elusive predator that has so far eluded the expedition's party. Bringing back the beast's fang will establish your standing as a true master of the hunt.",h="Sir S.",sec={{t="The Elusive Prowler",b="At Nesingwary's Expedition, Sir S. J. Erlgadin considers your trials nearly complete. One final quarry remains to prove your worth against the jungle's predators: a panther named Bhag'thera. The beast has so far eluded the expedition's own party as it prowls the wilds of Stranglethorn Vale. Erlgadin calls on you to track down this great stalker and claim the Fang of Bhag'thera as proof of your skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin gives this challenge at Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"quest giver","who gives panther mastery","erlgadin quest"}},{q="What beast are you hunting?",a="The quarry is Bhag'thera, a great panther that prowls the jungle and has so far eluded the expedition's party.",al={"what is the target","who is bhag'thera","panther target"}},{q="What trophy is required?",a="Sir S. J. Erlgadin requires the Fang of Bhag'thera as evidence of the beast's defeat.",al={"what proof","what item","bhag'thera trophy"}},{q="What came before this hunt?",a="This challenge follows the third trial in the Panther Mastery line, building on the earlier panther hunts.",al={"previous quest","panther mastery prerequisite"}}},kw={"bhag'thera","fang of bhag'thera","nesingwary's expedition","panther mastery","sir s. j. erlgadin","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter"},m={start="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",["end"]="Sir S. J. Erlgadin",level="40",id=193},src={"Panther Mastery (4)"}}
E["quest:194"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="At his expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges travelers to prove their prowess in the wilderness. The famed hunter demands ten Stranglethorn Raptors slain to test whether you possess genuine hunting talent.",h="At his expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges travelers to prove their...",sec={{t="A Test of Skill",b="Following your arrival in the jungle after Welcome to the Jungle, Hemet Nesingwary offers to test your tracking and hunting capabilities. Rather than handing out maps or directions, he insists that finding the Stranglethorn Raptors yourself is half the test, challenging you to venture out into the brush and bring down ten of the fierce beasts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this hunting challenge?",a="Hemet Nesingwary, the renowned big game hunter stationed at the expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, issues this challenge.",al={"who gives raptor mastery","raptor mastery quest giver","hemet nesingwary raptors"}},{q="What beasts are you asked to track down?",a="You are asked to track down and slay ten Stranglethorn Raptors scattered throughout the jungle wilds.",al={"which raptors","what do i kill for raptor mastery","target of raptor mastery"}},{q="Why does Hemet refuse to tell you where the raptors live?",a="Hemet believes that tracking and locating your quarry is half the trial of becoming a true big game hunter, so he leaves the search entirely up to you.",al={"where are the raptors","why no raptor location","raptor locations"}},{q="What step comes before this trial?",a="This hunting trial follows the initial greeting in the wilderness, Welcome to the Jungle.",al={"prerequisite for raptor mastery","previous quest raptor mastery","raptor mastery chain start"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For those walking the path of the hunter, Hemet Nesingwary's trials in the wild serve as a quintessential proving ground of tracking and marksmanship."},kw={"big game hunter","hemet nesingwary","raptor mastery","stranglethorn raptor","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:5762","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter","quest:208"},m={start="Hemet Nesingwary",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="34",faction="Neutral",id=194},src={"Raptor Mastery (Classic)"}}
E["quest:195"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Deep in the jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges hunters to step up their game against more dangerous quarry. Following an earlier raptor hunt, he directs adventurers to pursue and bring down ten Lashtail Raptors.",h="Deep in the jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges hunters to step up their game against...",sec={{t="A Steeper Challenge",b="After proving an initial measure of hunting prowess, Hemet Nesingwary expects more than idly passing time by the camp's fire. To prove true focus and skill, hunters are dispatched into the dense jungle brush just north of Grom'gol Base Camp to track down and slay ten fierce Lashtail Raptors.",sp=0},{t="Trophies for the Hearth",b="Returning successful from the jungle earns Nesingwary's hearty approval. The seasoned hunter considers such dangerous predators worthy quarry, well suited for securing trophies above the hearth, and prepares the adventurer for even greater challenges.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunting challenge?",a="The famed big game hunter Hemet Nesingwary issues the challenge from his expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who starts raptor mastery 2","raptor mastery quest giver","where to get raptor mastery"}},{q="What quarry are you tasked with hunting?",a="You are challenged to track into the jungle and slay ten Lashtail Raptors.",al={"what raptors to kill","which raptor quest","lashtail raptor target"}},{q="Where are the Lashtail Raptors found?",a="Lashtail Raptors prowl the wild foliage of northern Stranglethorn Vale, particularly north of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"where are lashtail raptors","lashtail raptor location","where to find lashtails"}},{q="Where does this hunt fit into Nesingwary's trials?",a="This is the second trial in the raptor series, following the introductory Raptor Mastery hunt and leading into a third part of the challenge.",al={"what comes before this raptor hunt","raptor mastery progression","raptor quest chain"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For trackers and beast stalkers, Hemet Nesingwary's challenges test fundamental hunting discipline against the deadlier predators roaming Stranglethorn Vale."},kw={"grom'gol base camp","hemet nesingwary","hunting","lashtail raptor","raptor mastery","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:5762","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:hunter"},m={start="Hemet Nesingwary",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="36",id=195},src={"Raptor Mastery (2)"}}
E["quest:196"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Hemet Nesingwary raises the stakes of his hunting expedition by sending you after a elusive breed known as Jungle Stalkers. Tracking down ten of these cunning raptors will prove your mettle as a true stalker of wild beasts in Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Hemet Nesingwary raises the stakes of his hunting expedition by sending you after a elusive breed known as...",sec={{t="A Cagey Quarry",b="Having tested your aim against lesser raptors, Hemet Nesingwary presents a more demanding quarry. Jungle Stalkers are notably cagey and far more difficult to track and slay than the breeds hunted previously. Hemet expects you to venture out into the jungle, fell ten of these wary predators, and return to camp to earn a lead on his finest hunt yet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt?",a="Hemet Nesingwary, the renowned big game hunter encamped in northern Stranglethorn Vale, issues this challenge.",al={"quest giver","who starts raptor mastery 3","hemet nesingwary hunt"}},{q="What beast are you asked to track down?",a="You are tasked with finding and slaying ten Jungle Stalkers, a particularly cagey and elusive variety of raptor.",al={"what raptor","target raptor","which raptors to kill"}},{q="Where are Jungle Stalkers found?",a="Jungle Stalkers roam Stranglethorn Vale, particularly in the regions situated north and west of the Gurubashi Arena.",al={"jungle stalker location","where do jungle stalkers roam","find jungle stalkers"}},{q="What comes before this challenge?",a="This hunt directly follows the second stage of the Raptor Mastery trials, continuing Hemet Nesingwary's progression through the local raptor breeds.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous raptor mastery","what quest comes before"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Stalking wary prey like Jungle Stalkers serves as a prime showcase for tracking prowess and wilderness marksmanship under Hemet Nesingwary's watchful eye."},kw={"big game hunter","gurubashi arena","hemet nesingwary","jungle stalkers","raptor mastery","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:5762","subzone:gurubashi-arena","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter","quest:208"},m={start="Hemet Nesingwary",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="41",id=196},src={"Raptor Mastery (3)"}}
E["quest:197"] = {t="quest",n="Raptor Mastery",z="stranglethorn",s="Deep in Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges seasoned trackers to bring down an elusive predator that has escaped even him. Having proven your mettle against lesser beasts, you are tasked with tracking the cunning raptor known as Tethis and securing its talon.",h="Deep in Stranglethorn Vale, Hemet Nesingwary challenges seasoned trackers to bring down an elusive predator...",sec={{t="The Wily Predator of the Vale",b="Following your earlier trials in the jungle, Hemet Nesingwary reveals the existence of a particularly vicious raptor named Tethis. While lesser hunters have chased prey across the foliage, Tethis has evaded capture entirely, defying even the expedition leader himself. Ajeck Rouack bestowed the beast with its moniker, marking it as the ultimate prize among Stranglethorn's scaled horrors.",sp=0},{t="Claiming the Talon",b="To stand recognized as a premier big game hunter, you are directed to prowl the grounds north of the Gurubashi Arena where Tethis is known to roam. Bringing back a talon from the slain terror will earn you the title of master raptor slayer, a feat no other big game hunter has accomplished.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to hunt Tethis?",a="Hemet Nesingwary directs the hunt from his expedition encampment in northern Stranglethorn Vale after you prove your tracking capabilities against ordinary jungle raptors.",al={"who gives raptor mastery","raptor mastery questgiver","who wants tethis dead"}},{q="Where can Tethis be found?",a="The ferocious beast prowls the jungle wilderness surrounding the Gurubashi Arena, most frequently sighted through the brush to the north of the colosseum.",al={"tethis location","where is tethis","where to find tethis"}},{q="What proof does Hemet require of the kill?",a="Hemet requires the talon of Tethis as undeniable proof that the cunning creature has finally been brought down.",al={"what do i bring hemet","tethis proof","raptor mastery turn in item"}},{q="Who originally named the raptor Tethis?",a="Ajeck Rouack, one of the hunters at Nesingwary's expedition camp, bestowed the elusive predator with the name Tethis.",al={"who named tethis","origin of tethis name"}}},kw={"ajeck rouack","gurubashi arena","hemet nesingwary","raptor mastery","stranglethorn vale","talon of tethis","tethis"},rel={"quest:208","subzone:gurubashi-arena","zone:stranglethorn","topic:hunter","quest:5762"},m={start="Hemet Nesingwary",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="43",id=197},src={"Raptor Mastery (4)"}}
E["quest:198"] = {t="quest",n="Supplies to Private Thorsen",z="stranglethorn",s="Krazek in Booty Bay hires a courier to haul miscellaneous goblin supplies north to Lieutenant Doren's camp. Local troll aggression has halted routine shipments, requiring an outside hand to ensure the goods reach Private Thorsen near the northern border.",h="Krazek in Booty Bay hires a courier to haul miscellaneous goblin supplies north to Lieutenant Doren's camp.",sec={{t="A Route Disrupted",b="Lieutenant Doren and his outfit stationed near the border between Stranglethorn Vale and Duskwood rely on regular shipments arranged through Krazek. Persistent attacks from local trolls have made standard delivery hazardous, prompting the goblin merchant to contract an independent courier. The package must travel all the way up the jungle road, with Private Thorsen designated to receive it either in their camp northwest of the road or along his patrol route to the south.",sp=0},{t="The Shipment's True Contents",b="Although listed only as miscellaneous goblin supplies, the shipment contains land mines. Private Thorsen reveals that these explosives are meant to help defend their post against Colonel Kurzen and his men.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sending these supplies?",a="Krazek, a goblin merchant conducting business in Booty Bay, arranges the shipment and provides the supplies.",al={"who gives supplies to thorsen","krazek delivery","who starts supplies to private thorsen"}},{q="Why have the supplies been delayed?",a="Aggression from local trolls in Stranglethorn Vale disrupted standard delivery operations, leaving Lieutenant Doren's men waiting on their scheduled goods.",al={"why delayed","troll attacks delivery","why wasn't it delivered"}},{q="Where can Private Thorsen be found?",a="He can be found at Lieutenant Doren's camp, located northwest of the main road near the entrance to Stranglethorn from Duskwood, or patrolling the path immediately south of the encampment.",al={"where is thorsen","thorsen location","find private thorsen"}},{q="What happens if the supplies are lost?",a="Krazek warns that anyone who fails to deliver the shipment will be held financially accountable and owe him restitution.",al={"what if i lose supplies","krazek restitution","failing krazek"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lieutenant Doren's soldiers guard the northern entrance into Stranglethorn Vale from Duskwood, relying on supplies from the goblins to hold their position."},kw={"booty bay","duskwood","goblin supplies","krazek","kurzen","lieutenant doren","private thorsen","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:doren","topic:goblin","zone:stranglethorn","zone:duskwood","topic:troll"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Private Thorsen",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=198},src={"Supplies to Private Thorsen"}}
E["quest:200"] = {t="quest",n="Bookie Herod",z="stranglethorn",s="Lieutenant Doren fears a spy among his own men after Kurzen discovered Thorsen's secret. To uncover how the secret slipped out, an investigator must infiltrate Kurzen's Compound and recover the records kept by Kurzen's logistics officer.",h="Lieutenant Doren fears a spy among his own men after Kurzen discovered Thorsen's secret.",sec={{t="A Leak in the Ranks",b="Following the discovery of Thorsen's secret, Lieutenant Doren suspects that a traitor operates within their midst. The intelligence leak threatens their operations, and finding the traitor has become an urgent concern. Thorsen maintained a line of communication directly into Kurzen's Compound through Bookie Herod, the colonel's logistics officer. Because Herod knows how Kurzen's Compound is run from day to day, Doren believes the officer's written records hold the truth about how the operation was exposed.",sp=0},{t="The Logistics Office",b="Reaching Bookie Herod's paperwork requires venturing into Kurzen's Compound. During Doren's time serving under Kurzen, Herod kept his office on the top floor of the compound's lone two-story house. There, among supply requisitions and missives from Colonel Kurzen himself, lie the documents that could trace how the secret was betrayed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bookie Herod?",a="Bookie Herod serves as the logistics officer for Colonel Kurzen's men. He oversees supplies and camp operations at Kurzen's Compound, and he previously served as an inside contact for Thorsen.",al={"herod role","who is the bookie","bookie herod lore"}},{q="Why does Lieutenant Doren want Herod's records?",a="Lieutenant Doren believes a spy has betrayed their camp because Colonel Kurzen learned of Thorsen's secret. Doren hopes Herod's logistics logs and correspondence will explain how that information was leaked.",al={"why get herod records","doren spy","how was thorsen caught"}},{q="Where are Bookie Herod's records located?",a="Herod's office sits on the top floor of the only two-story house inside Kurzen's Compound, where Doren believes his records are probably still kept.",al={"where are the records","herod office location","two story house kurzen"}},{q="What comes before this investigation?",a="This investigation directly follows Jungle Secrets, where Lieutenant Doren concludes that someone must have betrayed Thorsen's secret to Kurzen's men.",al={"prior quest","bookie herod prerequisite"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lieutenant Doren and his men once stood with Colonel Kurzen before breaking away, and now hunt for a spy in their own ranks."},kw={"bookie herod","colonel kurzen","kurzen's compound","lieutenant doren","stranglethorn vale","thorsen"},rel={"quest:215","quest:328","subzone:kurzen-s-compound","npc:colonel-kurzen","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Lieutenant Doren",["end"]="Bookie Herod's Records",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=200},src={"Bookie Herod (quest)"}}
E["quest:202"] = {t="quest",n="Colonel Kurzen",z="stranglethorn",s="Lieutenant Doren calls upon you to deliver the final strike against Colonel Kurzen and his inner guard. You are sent into the Stockpile to eliminate the rogue commander and his remaining leaders to secure the Rebel Camp's survival.",h="Lieutenant Doren calls upon you to deliver the final strike against Colonel Kurzen and his inner guard.",sec={{t="The Heart of the Stockpile",b="Lieutenant Doren and his band of defectors have reached the climax of their struggle against their former commander. Following the suppression of Kurzen's elite specialists, Doren recognizes that the rebel forces will never truly be safe while Kurzen retains control of his jungle redoubt. He directs you into the Stockpile cave, where Kurzen directs his forces alongside his subchiefs and elites.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Serpent's Head",b="To permanently end the threat, Doren asks for conclusive proof of Kurzen's downfall by demanding the rogue colonel's head, along with the defeat of his elites and subchiefs. Entering the cave to face Kurzen's leadership offers the rebels their sole prospect of breathing easier amid the perils of northern Stranglethorn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this task?",a="Lieutenant Doren sends you after Kurzen from the Rebel Camp situated in northern Stranglethorn Vale, immediately following the completion of Special Forces.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","where to pick up colonel kurzen"}},{q="Where is Colonel Kurzen located?",a="Kurzen directs his troops from deep within the cave system known as the Stockpile, located inside the Kurzen compound in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is kurzen","kurzen location","how to find colonel kurzen"}},{q="What proof does Lieutenant Doren require?",a="Lieutenant Doren asks you to bring back Kurzen's head to definitively prove the rogue commander has fallen, alongside defeating his elites and subchiefs.",al={"what proof is needed","kurzen proof","turn in item"}},{q="What came before this confrontation?",a="This confrontation immediately follows Special Forces, where you weakened Kurzen's specialized battlefield operatives before targeting his core command structure.",al={"prerequisite quest","what is previous quest","chain before kurzen"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Eliminating Kurzen breaks the grip of a rogue Stormwind officer over the northern reaches of Stranglethorn Vale."},kw={"colonel kurzen","kurzen","lieutenant doren","rebel camp","stockpile","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:574","subzone:rebel-camp","npc:doren","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Lieutenant Doren",["end"]="Lieutenant Doren",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=202},src={"Colonel Kurzen (quest)"}}
E["quest:203"] = {t="quest",n="The Second Rebellion",z="stranglethorn",s="At the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Sergeant Yohwa seeks help against the overwhelming forces of Colonel Kurzen. Outnumbered ten to one by a cunning tactician, the rebels must rely on swift, covert strikes to survive. Cutting down Kurzen's jungle fighters is the first step toward relieving the relentless pressure on their refuge.",h="At the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Sergeant Yohwa seeks help against the overwhelming forces...",sec={{t="A Losing Battle",b="The soldiers at the Rebel Camp face dire odds against Colonel Kurzen. Yohwa explains that the Colonel is a brilliant military tactician whose force outnumbers the rebellion by at least ten to one. Unable to wage an open war of attrition, the rebels have no choice but to adopt the Colonel's own covert tactics, launching quick incursions into his encampment to thin his ranks and escaping before heavy reinforcements can retaliate.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Compound",b="To stem the tide, Yohwa asks you to push east into Kurzen's stronghold and eliminate a sizable contingent of his jungle fighters. Thinning out these foot soldiers eases the pressure bearing down on the Rebel Camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sergeant Yohwa?",a="Sergeant Yohwa is an officer stationed at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, coordinating covert strikes against the host led by Colonel Kurzen.",al={"yohwa","who gives the second rebellion","sergeant yohwa"}},{q="Where is Colonel Kurzen's camp located?",a="Colonel Kurzen's compound lies to the east of the Rebel Camp in the dense wilderness of northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"kurzen camp location","where are the jungle fighters","kurzen location"}},{q="Why are the rebels using covert tactics instead of open war?",a="The rebels are outnumbered at least ten to one by Colonel Kurzen, a brilliant military strategist. Facing such massive odds, a direct assault is impossible, forcing the rebels to rely on rapid guerrilla strikes.",al={"why covert","why not fight kurzen openly","rebel tactics"}},{q="What comes after The Second Rebellion?",a="After cutting down Kurzen's jungle fighters, Sergeant Yohwa offers the follow-up step titled Special Forces.",al={"next quest","what is after the second rebellion","follow up to the second rebellion"}}},kw={"colonel kurzen","jungle fighter","kurzen","rebel camp","sergeant yohwa","special forces","stranglethorn vale","yohwa"},rel={"subzone:rebel-camp","npc:colonel-kurzen","quest:574","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Sergeant Yohwa",["end"]="Sergeant Yohwa",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=203},src={"The Second Rebellion"}}
E["quest:204"] = {t="quest",n="Bad Medicine",z="stranglethorn",s="At the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Sergeant Yohwa seeks to blunt Colonel Kurzen's military advantage by targeting his medical support. The renegades rely on powerful remedies and toxins concocted by their practitioners, leaving the resistance fighters desperate to turn those same concoctions to their own advantage.",h="At the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Sergeant Yohwa seeks to blunt Colonel Kurzen's military...",sec={{t="Stripping the Compound's Support",b="Colonel Kurzen has bolstered his jungle force with numerous medicine men who heal his forces and poison Yohwa's fighters with venom fern extracts. To turn the tide of the conflict, Sergeant Yohwa directs adventurers into the Kurzen Compound to scavenge those vital supplies. Securing their jungle remedies will help treat wounded fighters at the Rebel Camp, while capturing a sample of their venom fern extract will enable the resistance to study the toxin and manufacture their own cures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this assignment?",a="Sergeant Yohwa, stationed at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, asks you to retrieve these medical supplies.",al={"who gives bad medicine","bad medicine quest giver","yohwa quest"}},{q="Why does Sergeant Yohwa want Jungle Remedies?",a="Kurzen's medicine men use the remedies to heal their own soldiers. The resistance fighters need those same supplies to treat and sustain their own wounded comrades.",al={"why need jungle remedies","jungle remedy purpose"}},{q="What is the Venom Fern Extract used for?",a="Kurzen's forces use the venom fern extract to poison Yohwa's fighters. Sergeant Yohwa needs a sample so the camp can study the compound and brew their own remedies against it.",al={"why venom fern extract","extract use"}},{q="Where are these medical supplies kept?",a="Both are held within the Kurzen Compound. The medicine men carry the remedies directly, while the venom fern extracts are stowed inside supply boxes around the encampment.",al={"where to find jungle remedies","extract location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Cutting off Kurzen's healing support keeps more of the Rebel Camp's fighters alive against his forces."},kw={"jungle remedy","kurzen","kurzen compound","medicine men","rebel camp","sergeant yohwa","stranglethorn","venom fern extract"},rel={"subzone:rebel-camp","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Sergeant Yohwa",["end"]="Sergeant Yohwa",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=204},src={"Bad Medicine (Classic)"}}
E["quest:205"] = {t="quest",n="Troll Witchery",z="stranglethorn",s="Brother Nimetz seeks insight into the corruption of Colonel Kurzen by examining dark troll enchantments. Following Kurzen's Mystery, he asks you to venture south into Skullsplitter territory and secure fetishes from their spellcasters.",h="Brother Nimetz seeks insight into the corruption of Colonel Kurzen by examining dark troll enchantments.",sec={{t="Unraveling the Corruption",b="While reviewing the legends recovered from the jungle, Brother Nimetz turns his attention to the second troll tribe lingering further south. He suspects that dark troll sorcery may be responsible for Colonel Kurzen's descent into evil. To verify his theory, he asks you to venture into Skullsplitter lands and pry fetishes directly from their Witch Doctors and Mystics so he can study their magic at the Rebel Camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Troll Witchery?",a="Brother Nimetz gives it at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"troll witchery quest giver","who starts troll witchery","where to get troll witchery"}},{q="Why does Brother Nimetz want Skullsplitter fetishes?",a="Brother Nimetz intends to study the dark magical implements to see if troll witchcraft explains Colonel Kurzen's fall into evil.",al={"why brother nimetz needs fetishes","purpose of troll witchery","kurzen corruption fetishes"}},{q="Which enemies carry the fetishes?",a="The fetishes are carried by Skullsplitter Witch Doctors and Skullsplitter Mystics within Skullsplitter territory.",al={"who drops skullsplitter fetishes","which trolls have fetishes","troll witchery fetish source"}},{q="What quest precedes Troll Witchery?",a="This assignment follows Kurzen's Mystery, continuing Brother Nimetz's investigation into the colonel's madness.",al={"troll witchery chain","what comes before troll witchery","prerequisite for troll witchery"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Brother Nimetz operates out of the Rebel Camp, enlisting Alliance travelers to uncover what corrupted Colonel Kurzen."},kw={"brother nimetz","colonel kurzen","mystic","rebel camp","skullsplitter","stranglethorn vale","troll witchery","witch doctor"},rel={"subzone:rebel-camp","npc:colonel-kurzen","topic:troll","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:balia-mah-ruins","subzone:ruins-of-zul-mamwe","topic:alliance"},m={start="Brother Nimetz",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=205},src={"Troll Witchery"}}
E["quest:206"] = {t="quest",n="Mai'Zoth",z="stranglethorn",s="Brother Nimetz believes Colonel Kurzen was driven to evil by a hidden power that still lives. An ogre mage known as Mai'Zoth lurks within the eastern mountains, wielding an artifact reputed to twist and control minds. Destroying him and recovering this relic is meant to ensure no other commander suffers the same corruption.",h="Brother Nimetz believes Colonel Kurzen was driven to evil by a hidden power that still lives.",sec={{t="The Source of Corruption",b="Though Kurzen has fallen, Brother Nimetz insists the primary catalyst behind the rebellion remains intact. His research points to Mai'Zoth, an ogre mage dwelling inside an ogre mound deep within the eastern heights of Stranglethorn Vale. Nimetz is certain that Mai'Zoth employed mind-altering sorcery to warp Kurzen's thoughts, warning that leaving the ogre alive invites another commander to succumb to the very same sinister influence.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Relic",b="To permanently eliminate the threat, you are asked to strike down Mai'Zoth, take the Mind's Eye from him, and bring that corrupting artifact back to the Rebel Camp.",sp=0},{t="After the Delivery",b="Nimetz gives the one who brings the Mind's Eye his blessing, and means to study the artifact to learn whether its power might serve good. If it cannot, he says it must be destroyed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mai'Zoth?",a="Mai'Zoth is an ogre mage who resides in an ogre mound in the eastern mountains of Stranglethorn Vale. Brother Nimetz holds him responsible for mentally corrupting Colonel Kurzen through sinister enchantments.",al={"who is maizoth","maizoth lore","ogre mage maizoth"}},{q="What is the Mind's Eye?",a="The Mind's Eye is an artifact held by Mai'Zoth, reputed to possess mind-controlling magic that the ogre mage uses to corrupt and influence others.",al={"minds eye lore","what is the artifact","mind's eye"}},{q="Why does Brother Nimetz want Mai'Zoth slain?",a="Brother Nimetz fears that as long as Mai'Zoth lives, his corruption could turn someone else into another Kurzen.",al={"nimetz motive","why kill maizoth","reason for hunting maizoth"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Brother Nimetz operates out of the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, seeking Alliance champions to put an end to the hidden evil that corrupted Kurzen."},kw={"brother nimetz","kurzen","mai'zoth","maizoth","mind's eye","ogre mound","rebel camp","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:rebel-camp","quest:591","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Brother Nimetz",["end"]="Brother Nimetz",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=206},src={"Mai'Zoth (quest)"}}
E["quest:207"] = {t="quest",n="Kurzen's Mystery",z="stranglethorn",s="Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp wants to know what turned Colonel Kurzen to depravity. Suspecting that troll magic holds him, Nimetz sends you to the troll ruins of Stranglethorn to copy the legends written on four tablets.",h="Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp wants to know what turned Colonel Kurzen to depravity.",sec={{t="Searching for Answers",b="Colonel Kurzen was once a great and noble man, and Brother Nimetz means to learn what caused his fall into depravity. Nimetz suspects troll magic has a hold on the colonel. To test that, the old troll legends must be read, and they are carved on four tablets hidden among the troll ruins of Stranglethorn. You are asked to copy the markings from each tablet and carry the copies back.",sp=0},{t="Where the Tablets Lie",b="One tablet stands in the Bal'lal Ruins. Another lies deep underwater off the coast, in the Vile Reef, near a sunken city held by Saltscale murlocs. The last two are in the Ruins of Zul'Kunda.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the search for the troll tablets?",a="Brother Nimetz gives it, at the Rebel Camp.",al={"who gives kurzens mystery","where do i start kurzens mystery","brother nimetz quest"}},{q="Why does Brother Nimetz want copies of troll legends?",a="Brother Nimetz wants to know why Colonel Kurzen, once a great and noble man, sank into depravity. Troll magic may be to blame, and the legends on the tablets could confirm it.",al={"why need troll tablets","kurzens mystery purpose","why nimetz wants legends"}},{q="Where are the four troll tablets located?",a="Bal'lal Ruins hold one. Another is deep underwater in the Vile Reef, west of Grom'gol. Two more are in the Ruins of Zul'Kunda.",al={"tablet locations","where are the tablets","kurzen tablets map"}},{q="What comes after the four tablets are brought back?",a="Brother Nimetz studies the legends for a link between the trolls and Colonel Kurzen's fall, and the tale goes on with Troll Witchery.",al={"what next after kurzens mystery","kurzens mystery follow up","quest chain after tablets"}}},kw={"bal'lal ruins","brother nimetz","colonel kurzen","rebel camp","stranglethorn vale","troll legend","vile reef","zul'kunda"},rel={"quest:205","subzone:rebel-camp","npc:colonel-kurzen","subzone:bal-lal-ruins","subzone:vile-reef","zone:stranglethorn","topic:alliance","topic:troll"},m={start="Brother Nimetz",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=207},src={"Kurzen's Mystery"}}
E["quest:208"] = {t="quest",n="Big Game Hunter",z="stranglethorn",s="Having proven skill across Stranglethorn Vale by hunting the region's deadliest predators, Hemet Nesingwary offers a final supreme challenge. The famed marksman asks for the head of King Bangalash, a great white tiger and the very reason Hemet is in the jungle at all.",h="Having proven skill across Stranglethorn Vale by hunting the region's deadliest predators, Hemet Nesingwary...",sec={{t="The Master's Quarry",b="After completing the trials set by the expedition's huntsmen—slaying Sin'Dall, Bhag'thera, and Tethis—Hemet Nesingwary acknowledges your martial skill. According to the veteran marksman, who compares your prowess to the finest displays seen from Lordaeron's battlefields to the jungle depths, only one hunt remains to prove your abilities unmatched: felling King Bangalash, the grand white tiger that serves as the expedition leader's true target.",sp=0},{t="A Storied Beast",b="Hemet reveals that King Bangalash is the reason he is in Stranglethorn Vale. The great beast has repeatedly driven the expedition leader himself back to camp in defeat. Presenting the beast's head would prove your hunting skill second to none.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this hunt?",a="Hemet Nesingwary himself gives this hunt at his expedition encampment in northern Stranglethorn Vale after you finish all prior hunting masteries.",al={"quest giver","who starts big game hunter","hemet nesingwary quest"}},{q="What prerequisite hunts must be finished first?",a="You must complete the entire hunting series for the camp: slaying Sin'Dall in Tiger Mastery, Bhag'thera in Panther Mastery, and Tethis in Raptor Mastery.",al={"prerequisites","what quests come before big game hunter","bangalash requirements"}},{q="Why does Hemet Nesingwary want King Bangalash?",a="King Bangalash is the entire reason Hemet traveled to Stranglethorn Vale. The great white tiger has eluded him repeatedly, driving the veteran marksman back to camp on multiple occasions.",al={"why king bangalash","why hunt bangalash","bangalash lore"}},{q="What proof does Hemet require?",a="Hemet requires the head of King Bangalash to verify that the great white tiger has truly been felled.",al={"what item do i need","bangalash objective","proof of kill"}},{q="Where does Hemet say he has seen combat before?",a="Hemet does not tell of his own fights; he only compares your skill with weapons to what he has seen on the battlefields of Lordaeron and deep in the jungle, and says he has rarely seen better.",al={"hemet war history","hemet past","lordaeron hunter"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Hemet Nesingwary considers taking down King Bangalash the ultimate proof of tracking and hunting mastery."},kw={"bangalash","bhag'thera","big game hunter","hemet nesingwary","sin'dall","stranglethorn vale","tethis","white tiger"},rel={"quest:5762","zone:stranglethorn","topic:lordaeron","topic:hunter"},m={start="Hemet Nesingwary",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="43",faction="Neutral",id=208},src={"Big Game Hunter (Classic)"}}
E["quest:209"] = {t="quest",n="Skullsplitter Tusks",z="stranglethorn",s="Kebok in Booty Bay needs materials to meet export demands for tiger fangs destined for the South Seas. Because hunting genuine jungle predators proves too costly, he has devised an undetectable forging process using tusks harvested from the Skullsplitter trolls.",h="Kebok in Booty Bay needs materials to meet export demands for tiger fangs destined for the South Seas.",sec={{t="A Lucrative Substitute",b="Supplying tiger fangs to distant island buyers across the South Seas has grown too expensive and difficult through ordinary hunting. Rather than abandon the trade, Kebok devised an undetectable forging method that turns mundane horn-like objects into convincing replicas. The closest physical match for these fangs comes directly from the jaws of the local Skullsplitter trolls, leading Kebok to hire adventurers willing to strip eighteen tusks from the jungle tribe to fill his upcoming export shipment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Kebok need Skullsplitter tusks?",a="Hunting enough real tigers to supply buyers in the South Seas has proven far too expensive and difficult. Kebok discovered that troll tusks can be forged into undetectable replicas of tiger fangs, allowing his trade operation to fill its monthly export orders.",al={"why skullsplitter tusks","kebok tusk plan","why fake tiger fangs"}},{q="Who is buying the fangs?",a="The finished counterfeit fangs are shipped out to trading partners located on various islands throughout the South Seas.",al={"who buys the tusks","south seas buyers","where do the fangs go"}},{q="Where does this task fall in Kebok's chain?",a="This assignment follows Kebok's earlier request for Bloodscalp Ears.",al={"what comes before skullsplitter tusks","skullsplitter tusks prerequisite","kebok quest order"}}},kw={"booty bay","forgery","kebok","skullsplitter","south seas","stranglethorn","tiger fangs","tusks"},rel={"quest:189","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","subzone:south-seas"},m={start="Kebok",["end"]="Kebok",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=209},src={"Skullsplitter Tusks"}}
E["quest:210"] = {t="quest",n="Krazek's Cookery",z="stranglethorn",s="Corporal Kaleb's mechanical cooking pot, bought off a goblin trader in Booty Bay, was a marvel until it broke. Kaleb asks you to take it back to the goblin Krazek for mending.",h="Corporal Kaleb's mechanical cooking pot, bought off a goblin trader in Booty Bay, was a marvel until it broke.",sec={{t="A Broken Pot",b="Corporal Kaleb does most of the cooking for the camp. It used to be heavy work until Kaleb bought a mechanical pot off a goblin trader in Booty Bay, and the pot spared Kaleb hour after hour. Then it broke. Krazek's Crock Pot must go back to the goblin Krazek to be fixed, and Kaleb hopes you will carry it there.",sp=0},{t="Krazek Takes a Look",b="Krazek calls the pot ingenious work, though prone to popping a spring or slipping a gear from time to time. Looking it over, Krazek finds the steam charger rusted out, the knuckle-gasket cracked and the fobulator missing teeth. Krazek can mend it, but a price comes with it, as it always does.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Krazek?",a="Corporal Kaleb, on whom the camp's cooking mostly falls, sends you. The mechanical pot Kaleb bought has broken down.",al={"who gives krazek's cookery","who starts krazek cookery","corporal kaleb quest"}},{q="Where can Krazek be found?",a="Krazek is the goblin trader of Booty Bay who sold the pot to Kaleb.",al={"where is krazek","krazek location","krazek booty bay"}},{q="What does Corporal Kaleb want carried to Krazek?",a="A mechanical cooking pot named Krazek's Crock Pot, which broke after sparing Kaleb a great deal of work.",al={"what is krazek's crock pot","what do i bring krazek"}},{q="Why did Kaleb buy a cooking pot from Krazek?",a="Kaleb handles most of the camp's cooking, and the pot spared Kaleb a great many hours until it broke.",al={"why mechanical cooking pot","kaleb cooking pot"}}},kw={"booty bay","corporal kaleb","crock pot","krazek","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:627","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin"},m={start="Corporal Kaleb",["end"]="Krazek",level="37",id=210},src={"Classic quest text: Krazek's Cookery"}}
E["quest:213"] = {t="quest",n="Hostile Takeover",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, Gelriz's latest move draws Baron Revilgaz's wrath in Hostile Takeover. Gelriz has pushed aside moguls appointed by the trade princes and now moves against the most notorious pirate of all. Kebok sends you to steal strange blue crystals Venture Company geologists have found near Lake Nazferiti.",h="In Booty Bay, Gelriz's latest move draws Baron Revilgaz's wrath in Hostile Takeover.",sec={{t="A Matter of Business",b="Baron Revilgaz gives Kebok leave to answer the insult as he sees fit. Kebok chooses theft, targeting the strange blue stones Venture Company mining crews have been unearthing.",sp=0},{t="The Geologists' Cache",b="Venture Company geologists working around Lake Nazferiti have taken a keen interest in the unusual crystals. Kebok wants you to bring eight samples back to Booty Bay. How you get them matters little to him, so long as they end up in his hands.",sp=0},{t="A Tumbling Discovery",b="The returned crystals have been tumbled, suggesting the Venture Company means to use them as fuel or an industrial catalyst. Kebok plans to send samples to Head Chemist Gigglefont for closer study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Hostile Takeover?",a="Kebok, in Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale, gives you this assignment on Baron Revilgaz's behalf.",al={"hostile takeover questgiver","who starts hostile takeover","kebok quest"}},{q="Why is Baron Revilgaz angry with Gelriz?",a="Gelriz pushed aside moguls appointed by the trade princes and has now moved against the most notorious pirate. Baron Revilgaz will not tolerate it.",al={"why revilgaz mad","gelriz revilgaz conflict","why does kebok want crystals"}},{q="Where are the crystals located?",a="Venture Company geologists working around Lake Nazferiti carry the crystals.",al={"where to find tumbled crystals","tumbled crystal location","lake nazferiti crystals"}}},kw={"booty bay","gelriz","gigglefont","kebok","lake nazferiti","revilgaz","tumbled crystal","venture co."},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:lake-nazferiti","topic:pirate","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kebok",["end"]="Kebok",level="36",id=213},src={"Hostile Takeover"}}
E["quest:215"] = {t="quest",n="Jungle Secrets",z="stranglethorn",s="After being rescued from an ambush in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Private Thorsen explains why he re-enlisted with Kurzen's men. He directs you back to the Rebel Camp so his commander can verify his covert intentions.",h="After being rescued from an ambush in northern Stranglethorn Vale, Private Thorsen explains why he...",sec={{t="A Covert Undertaking",b="Following his rescue, Private Thorsen admits the scene looks bad and asks to explain. He claims Lieutenant Doren ordered him to re-enlist with Colonel Kurzen's men to gather desperately needed intelligence for the rebellion. What seemed to be an opportunity to infiltrate Kurzen's Compound quickly turned disastrous, forcing Thorsen to refer you directly to Doren at the Rebel Camp for official confirmation while begging for complete discretion.",sp=0},{t="Suspicions at Camp",b="Lieutenant Doren confirms that Thorsen was indeed acting under his orders. The rebels were once fiercely loyal to Kurzen until Kurzen's corruption twisted their loyalty into rage, and discovery of Thorsen's dealings would prompt his own comrades to slit his throat. Because only Doren, Sergeant Yohwa, and Thorsen were supposed to know of the plan, the failed ambush indicates an unsettling truth: an unknown traitor lurks within their ranks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Private Thorsen meeting with Kurzen's forces?",a="He was acting under orders from Lieutenant Doren to re-enlist among Colonel Kurzen's men as a spy and gather vital military intelligence for the rebels.",al={"why did thorsen meet kurzen","is thorsen a traitor","why was thorsen outside camp"}},{q="Where does Private Thorsen send you?",a="He directs you to speak with Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale so the commander can confirm his story.",al={"where do i go","thorsen turn in","where is doren"}},{q="Why does Thorsen insist on secrecy?",a="The rebels were once fiercely loyal to Colonel Kurzen. If word got out that Thorsen had been dealing with Kurzen's men, he could be killed in the night.",al={"why keep it secret","why secret mission"}},{q="What comes after reporting to Lieutenant Doren?",a="Following your conversation with Lieutenant Doren, your search leads into the next step, Bookie Herod.",al={"next quest","what follows jungle secrets"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Rebel Camp depends on the sorely needed intelligence Private Thorsen hopes to bring back from Kurzen's men."},kw={"doren","kurzen","rebel camp","stranglethorn","thorsen","traitor","yohwa"},rel={"npc:doren","npc:colonel-kurzen","subzone:rebel-camp","subzone:kurzen-s-compound","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Private Thorsen",["end"]="Lieutenant Doren",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=215},src={"Jungle Secrets"}}
E["quest:328"] = {t="quest",n="The Hidden Key",z="stranglethorn",s="Tucked away in the binding of Bookie Herod's ledgers is a small brass key alongside notes referencing a secure strongbox. Locating this container deep within the cavern complex behind Kurzen's Compound may reveal how Private Thorsen was betrayed.",h="Tucked away in the binding of Bookie Herod's ledgers is a small brass key alongside notes referencing a...",sec={{t="A Secret in the Bindings",b="Searching through Bookie Herod's ledgers yields no direct mention of Private Thorsen, but it reveals something else: a small brass key concealed inside a book's binding. Scraps among the paperwork make passing mention of a secure strongbox tucked away inside the Stockpile, the cavern complex at the rear of Kurzen's Compound. Opening that container might reveal how Thorsen's cover was blown.",sp=0},{t="Deep into the Stockpile",b="Reaching the strongbox requires delving into the cave system behind the compound. Heavy, bronze-bound, and sturdily constructed, the chest sits among stacked crates in the cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did this brass key come from?",a="The small brass key was hidden inside the binding of one of Bookie Herod's ledger books, uncovered while examining his paperwork.",al={"where was the key","how did i get the key","small brass key source"}},{q="Where is Bookie Herod's strongbox located?",a="The strongbox sits inside the Stockpile, which is the cave complex found at the very back of Kurzen's Compound.",al={"strongbox location","where is the strongbox","where is the chest"}},{q="Why search for Herod's strongbox?",a="Herod's loose papers fail to explain how Private Thorsen's presence was compromised, but they mention a secure strongbox that might hold the answer.",al={"why find the strongbox","what is in the box","purpose of the strongbox"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="This follows the investigation into Bookie Herod, where his ledger records were first sought out and searched.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"bookie herod","brass key","kurzen's compound","private thorsen","stockpile","stranglethorn vale","strongbox"},rel={"quest:200","quest:329","subzone:kurzen-s-compound","npc:colonel-kurzen","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Bookie Herod's Records",["end"]="Bookie Herod's Strongbox",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=328},src={"The Hidden Key"}}
E["quest:329"] = {t="quest",n="The Spy Revealed!",z="stranglethorn",s="Inside Bookie Herod's strongbox lies a damp piece of parchment detailing the daily routines of Private Thorsen. Bearing only the initial M, this correspondence suggests an informant has embedded themselves among the rebels in northern Stranglethorn Vale. The muddy note is meant for Lieutenant Doren.",h="Inside Bookie Herod's strongbox lies a damp piece of parchment detailing the daily routines of Private...",sec={{t="A Traitor in the Ranks",b="Opening the strongbox reveals not just valuables, but an itinerary tracking Private Thorsen. The barely legible writing recounts his patrol routes, his companions, and his daily activities around the Rebel Camp, marked only with the signature -M. Such detailed observations could only come from someone living alongside Thorsen, pointing to a traitor within the rebel camp.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Doren",b="Carrying the damp parchment back to the Rebel Camp brings the truth to Lieutenant Doren. Armed with the initialed note, the commander gains the evidence required to search for the infiltrator working within their own perimeter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on the muddy note?",a="The note contains an itinerary of Private Thorsen's daily routines. It outlines where he patrols, the people he speaks to, and how he occupies his hours within the camp, closed out by the single letter -M.",al={"muddy note text","what does the note say","spy note details"}},{q="Where did this note come from?",a="The note is discovered inside Bookie Herod's strongbox after unlocking it, sitting among the chest's other contents.",al={"where do i find the muddy note","spy revealed start","how to start the spy revealed"}},{q="Who receives the note?",a="The note must be delivered to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who do i turn the muddy note to","where to take the note","lieutenant doren turn in"}},{q="What comes next after reporting the note?",a="Following this report, Lieutenant Doren's investigation continues with Patrol Schedules.",al={"what quest is next","next step after the spy revealed","after the spy revealed"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unmasking an informant in Stranglethorn Vale protects the precarious foothold the Alliance rebels maintain against local threats."},kw={"doren","herod","muddy note","rebel camp","spy","stranglethorn","strongbox","thorsen","traitor"},rel={"npc:doren","subzone:rebel-camp","quest:328","quest:330","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Bookie Herod's Strongbox",["end"]="Lieutenant Doren",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=329},src={"The Spy Revealed!"}}
E["quest:330"] = {t="quest",n="Patrol Schedules",z="stranglethorn",s="Following the discovery of an incriminating message signed only by an initial, Lieutenant Doren seeks to identify the traitor within the Rebel Camp. By cross-referencing duty rosters, duty records can reveal who shared patrol routes with Private Thorsen during the previous week.",h="Following the discovery of an incriminating message signed only by an initial, Lieutenant Doren seeks to...",sec={{t="A Clue in the Rosters",b="The recovered note bears only the initial M, which provides little on its own to expose the conspirator aiding the Kurzen forces. However, the author mentions sharing regular duty paths alongside Private Thorsen throughout the previous week. Lieutenant Doren directs you across the Rebel Camp to speak with Corporal Sethman, the soldier responsible for maintaining duty logs, to identify who walked alongside Thorsen.",sp=0},{t="What the Records Show",b="Reviewing the official records confirms that Private Merle was assigned to the exact same duty times and routes as Thorsen for the entirety of the prior week. The realization exposes Merle as the informant feeding intelligence to Kurzen's men. Once identified, the traitor flees the encampment toward the northern boundary with Duskwood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Lieutenant Doren send you to Corporal Sethman?",a="Corporal Sethman oversees the duty logs and schedules for the Rebel Camp. Because the recovered note mentions walking regular routes with Private Thorsen, Sethman's records can pinpoint who was assigned to duty alongside him.",al={"why talk to sethman","corporal sethman role","sethman patrol schedules"}},{q="What clue is found in the recovered note?",a="The message is signed with the single letter M and explicitly mentions that its author walked the same duty paths as Private Thorsen during the previous week.",al={"note clue","letter clue","who signed note"}},{q="Where does this inquiry take place?",a="This investigation takes place entirely inside the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, passing between Lieutenant Doren and Corporal Sethman.",al={"where is patrol schedules","patrol schedules location"}},{q="What event preceded this inquiry?",a="In The Spy Revealed! you brought Lieutenant Doren the muddy note found among Bookie Herod's valuables, signed only with an initial.",al={"previous quest","what led to patrol schedules"}}},kw={"corporal sethman","kurzen","lieutenant doren","patrol schedules","private thorsen","rebel camp","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:329","quest:331","subzone:rebel-camp","zone:stranglethorn","npc:doren","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Lieutenant Doren",["end"]="Corporal Sethman",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=330},src={"Patrol Schedules"}}
E["quest:331"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Doren",z="stranglethorn",s="After obtaining the patrol information, Corporal Sethman directs you back to Lieutenant Doren. Delivering these findings brings crucial military intelligence directly to the rebels' commander in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",h="After obtaining the patrol information, Corporal Sethman directs you back to Lieutenant Doren.",sec={{t="Delivering the Intelligence",b="Corporal Sethman reminds you that Lieutenant Doren wants a direct report on the patrol information. You must bring what you learned back to Doren.",sp=0},{t="A Traitor Revealed",b="Presenting the patrol information reveals that Merle was the one who betrayed the camp. Lieutenant Doren mourns the loss of a soldier he once considered brave and loyal, yet feels immense relief at rooting out the traitor before Colonel Kurzen could take advantage.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Lieutenant Doren?",a="Corporal Sethman sends you to report to Lieutenant Doren once you have gone over the patrol schedules with him.",al={"who starts report to doren","who sends me to doren","report to doren giver"}},{q="What came before this report?",a="This follows Patrol Schedules, where Corporal Sethman goes through the patrol schedules for you.",al={"previous quest","what is before report to doren","patrol schedules"}},{q="Where is this report delivered?",a="You deliver the report directly to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is lieutenant doren","doren location","where do i go"}}},kw={"doren","kurzen","patrol schedules","sethman","stranglethorn"},rel={"npc:doren","quest:330","npc:colonel-kurzen","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Corporal Sethman",["end"]="Lieutenant Doren",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=331},src={"Report to Doren"}}
E["quest:338"] = {t="quest",n="The Green Hills of Stranglethorn",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot was trusted to proofread the manuscript for Hemet Nesingwary's novel, but a fierce gust of wind scattered the loose pages across the jungle. To spare him his master's anger, you are asked to scour the wilds, assemble the missing pages into four complete chapters, and return the finished work.",h="Barnil Stonepot was trusted to proofread the manuscript for Hemet Nesingwary's novel, but a fierce gust of...",sec={{t="A Scattered Manuscript",b="Following your arrival in the expedition camp after Welcome to the Jungle, Barnil Stonepot finds himself facing a disaster. While reviewing the draft of Hemet Nesingwary's novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, a sudden gale caught the loose leaves and flung them into the wild. Though he managed to recover a fair portion of the work, many sheets remain lost in the brush. To keep his master from discovering the mishap, he needs every misplaced page tracked down and compiled into Chapter I, Chapter II, Chapter III, and Chapter IV.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Hunter's Tale",b="Bringing back the four completed sections spares Barnil from an unpleasant confrontation with Nesingwary. With the chapters gathered safely in hand, he hopes the restored work will soon find its way into libraries across the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote The Green Hills of Stranglethorn?",a="The novel was written by the expedition's leader, Hemet Nesingwary, who entrusted the draft to Barnil Stonepot for proofreading.",al={"author of green hills of stranglethorn","who wrote the book","nesingwary book"}},{q="How were the pages lost?",a="A powerful gust of wind blew directly through the hunting camp while Barnil was reviewing the manuscript, scattering the loose sheets across the jungle.",al={"why are pages scattered","what happened to the pages","how did pages blow away"}},{q="What is needed to finish the manuscript?",a="You must collect the scattered pages and assemble them into four distinct parts: Chapter I, Chapter II, Chapter III, and Chapter IV, then hand the full set to Barnil.",al={"what chapters are needed","how to complete green hills","manuscript requirements"}},{q="Where did this assignment come from?",a="Barnil offers this job at the expedition camp in Stranglethorn Vale after you complete Welcome to the Jungle.",al={"green hills prerequisite","quest before green hills","how do i get this quest"}},{q="What does Barnil intend to do with the restored novel?",a="Beyond saving himself from Nesingwary's wrath, Barnil expects the completed manuscript will eventually be distributed to libraries across the world.",al={"why collect the pages","what happens to the book","where will the book go"}}},kw={"barnil stonepot","chapters","green hills of stranglethorn","hemet nesingwary","manuscript","pages","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:339","quest:340","quest:341","quest:342","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Barnil Stonepot",level="40",id=338},src={"The Green Hills of Stranglethorn (Classic)"}}
E["quest:339"] = {t="quest",n="Chapter I",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot is trying to restore the opening portion of Hemet Nesingwary's scattered hunting manuscript, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn. He needs four missing leaves gathered from across the jungle to bind the introductory section back together.",h="Barnil Stonepot is trying to restore the opening portion of Hemet Nesingwary's scattered hunting manuscript...",sec={{t="The Missing Introduction",b="Following your talk regarding The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, Barnil Stonepot sets his sights on restoring the book's opening passage. According to the dwarf, this first part sets the stage for the wider story and describes Nesingwary's hunting party, counting Barnil himself among the companions. Unfortunately, the manuscript's leaves remain lost in the wild, leaving pages one, four, six, and eight absent from the collection.",sp=0},{t="Binding the First Section",b="Once you bring back the four missing sheets, Barnil is able to piece the first segment of the master huntsman's text back into a single, cohesive part of the book.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for these pages?",a="Barnil Stonepot, a companion of Hemet Nesingwary stationed at their camp in Stranglethorn Vale, needs the pages to assemble the scattered hunting memoirs.",al={"who gives chapter 1","barnil stonepot","quest giver"}},{q="Which pages are needed for this part of the manuscript?",a="Barnil needs pages one, four, six, and eight to successfully reassemble the opening section of the work.",al={"what pages are needed","missing pages","which pages"}},{q="What is described in this part of the manuscript?",a="According to Barnil Stonepot, it sets the background for the story and introduces Nesingwary's hunting companions, including Barnil himself.",al={"what is chapter 1 about","manuscript contents"}},{q="What led up to this step?",a="This follows the broader effort to recover The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, where Barnil first informs you of the missing pages.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest"}}},kw={"barnil stonepot","chapter i","green hills of stranglethorn","hemet nesingwary","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:338","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Barnil Stonepot",level="40",id=339},src={"Chapter I"}}
E["quest:340"] = {t="quest",n="Chapter II",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot needs assistance gathering missing leaves from the second section of Hemet Nesingwary's scattered hunting manuscript. Having gathered most of the parchment himself, he relies on travelers across Stranglethorn Vale to recover the remaining scattered accounts of panther and tiger hunts.",h="Barnil Stonepot needs assistance gathering missing leaves from the second section of Hemet Nesingwary's...",sec={{t="Hunts of the Jungle Cats",b="Following the dispersal of Hemet Nesingwary's manuscript across Stranglethorn Vale, Barnil Stonepot managed to reclaim many leaves on his own. The second chapter focuses entirely on thrilling accounts of tracking panthers and tigers through the wilderness. Four specific pages—numbers 10, 11, 14, and 16—remain lost to the wind and the jungle's inhabitants, leaving this section of the expedition's chronicle unfinished.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for these manuscript pages?",a="Barnil Stonepot, who is assisting the Nesingwary expedition in Stranglethorn Vale, asks for help gathering the missing leaves.",al={"who gives chapter 2","quest giver chapter ii","barnil stonepot"}},{q="Which pages are needed for the second chapter?",a="Barnil needs pages 10, 11, 14, and 16 to finish assembling the second chapter.",al={"what pages are needed","pages for chapter 2","chapter ii pages"}},{q="What stories are recorded in the second chapter?",a="The second chapter documents tales of stalking and hunting the panthers and tigers that prowl Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"what is chapter 2 about","chapter ii lore","green hills chapter 2 content"}},{q="What comes before this request?",a="This request follows Barnil's initial call for aid regarding the lost manuscript, known as The Green Hills of Stranglethorn.",al={"prior quest","prerequisite chapter 2","green hills chain"}}},kw={"barnil stonepot","chapter ii","green hills of stranglethorn","nesingwary","pages","panther","stranglethorn vale","tiger"},rel={"quest:338","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Barnil Stonepot",level="40",id=340},src={"Chapter II"}}
E["quest:341"] = {t="quest",n="Chapter III",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot is trying to reconstruct the third chapter of Hemet Nesingwary's hunting manuscript in Stranglethorn Vale. The section recounts the first kill made with a dwarven rifle by Sir Erlgadin and Lady Rouack, but four specific leaves were blown across the jungle.",h="Barnil Stonepot is trying to reconstruct the third chapter of Hemet Nesingwary's hunting manuscript in...",sec={{t="A Hunt Recorded",b="Barnil Stonepot considers this portion of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn his personal favorite. The text recounts the early exploits of Sir Erlgadin and Lady Rouack, detailing their very first kill using a dwarven rifle. The chapter ends on a sharp cliffhanger.",sp=0},{t="Missing Leaves",b="To piece the narrative together again, Barnil requires pages 18, 20, 21, and 24. These missing fragments were scattered into the wild, carried off across Stranglethorn Vale like the rest of the manuscript.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is looking for Chapter III?",a="Barnil Stonepot, who proofread Hemet Nesingwary's manuscript at the expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, is piecing together its missing pages.",al={"who gives chapter 3","chapter 3 quest giver","barnil stonepot chapter iii"}},{q="What happens in Chapter III of the book?",a="The chapter recounts the first hunt that Sir Erlgadin and Lady Rouack undertook with a dwarven rifle, ending on an unresolved cliffhanger.",al={"what is chapter 3 about","chapter iii story","erlgadin and rouack"}},{q="Which pages are needed to finish Chapter III?",a="Barnil needs pages 18, 20, 21, and 24 to assemble Chapter III into one piece.",al={"what pages chapter 3","chapter iii pages needed","pages for chapter 3"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="This effort follows the initial undertaking known as The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, where Barnil first explains the loss of Hemet Nesingwary's manuscript.",al={"chapter 3 prerequisite","what leads to chapter iii"}}},kw={"barnil stonepot","chapter iii","erlgadin","green hills of stranglethorn","hemet nesingwary","page 18","page 20","page 21","page 24","rouack","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:338","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Barnil Stonepot",level="40",id=341},src={"Chapter III"}}
E["quest:342"] = {t="quest",n="Chapter IV",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot is trying to reconstruct the thrilling finale of Hemet Nesingwary's famous manuscript. Recovering the final three sheets will restore the climactic conclusion to the wild hunting tale.",h="Barnil Stonepot is trying to reconstruct the thrilling finale of Hemet Nesingwary's famous manuscript.",sec={{t="The Grand Finale",b="Barnil Stonepot considers this section the big finale of the entire hunting volume. To assemble the fourth chapter, he needs someone to track down and return pages twenty-five, twenty-six, and twenty-seven. Once these three lost sheets are gathered from across the jungle, the manuscript's exciting conclusion can finally be reassembled.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Chapter IV restored?",a="Barnil Stonepot asks for help collecting the scattered sheets so he can piece together the ending of Hemet Nesingwary's hunting book.",al={"who gives chapter iv","chapter iv quest giver","who needs chapter 4"}},{q="Which pages are required to finish Chapter IV?",a="You need pages twenty-five, twenty-six, and twenty-seven of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to complete the fourth chapter.",al={"chapter 4 pages","which pages for chapter iv","what pages do i need"}},{q="What comes before this request?",a="This request follows Barnil Stonepot's initial call to gather the scattered leaves of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn.",al={"chapter iv prerequisites","chapter 4 previous quest"}}},kw={"barnil stonepot","chapter 4","chapter iv","green hills of stranglethorn","hemet nesingwary","page 25","page 26","page 27","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:338","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Barnil Stonepot",level="40",id=342},src={"Chapter IV"}}
E["quest:348"] = {t="quest",n="Stranglethorn Fever",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, Fin Fizracket lies sick with Stranglethorn Fever, a deadly virus. He says the only cure is the heart of Mokk the Savage, an elusive white beast, and that he is dying.",h="In Booty Bay, Fin Fizracket lies sick with Stranglethorn Fever, a deadly virus.",sec={{t="A Desperate Cure",b="Fin Fizracket is stammering and fading, sure that he has caught Stranglethorn Fever. He says the only cure is to eat the heart of Mokk the Savage, an elusive white beast. Witch Doctor Unbagwa is the only one who can summon the creature, and Fin sends you to find Unbagwa in a hidden cave on the southern cape, the Spirit Den.",sp=0},{t="Back at Fin's Side",b="Once the heart of Mokk is in Fin's hands, his strength begins to return. He wakes confused about where he is, and when he learns it is Booty Bay, he talks of a strange dream. Some of the weakness still lingers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What illness is Fin Fizracket suffering from?",a="Fin says he has Stranglethorn Fever, a deadly virus. It leaves him cold and delirious, and he believes he is dying.",al={"what disease does fin have","stranglethorn fever illness","fin fizracket sick"}},{q="What is required to cure the fever?",a="Fin says the only cure is to eat the heart of Mokk the Savage, an elusive white beast.",al={"how to cure stranglethorn fever","cure for fin fizracket","mokk heart cure"}},{q="Who is Witch Doctor Unbagwa?",a="Fin says Witch Doctor Unbagwa is the only one who can summon Mokk the Savage. He is found in a hidden cave on the southern cape, the Spirit Den in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is unbagwa","who can summon mokk","witch doctor unbagwa role"}},{q="Where can Fin Fizracket be found?",a="Fin Fizracket is in Booty Bay.",al={"fin fizracket location","where is fin fizracket","booty bay fever guy"}}},kw={"booty bay","fin fizracket","heart of mokk","mokk the savage","stranglethorn fever","stranglethorn vale","witch doctor unbagwa"},rel={"quest:349","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:cape-of-stranglethorn","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Fin Fizracket",["end"]="Fin Fizracket",level="45",faction="Neutral",id=348},src={"Wowpedia: Stranglethorn Fever"}}
E["quest:349"] = {t="quest",n="Stranglethorn Fever",z="stranglethorn",s="Deep within Stranglethorn Vale, Witch Doctor Unbagwa claims to know how to draw out the beast known as Mokk the Savage. Before communion with the spirits can begin, the witch doctor requires ten Gorilla Fangs as an offering. Once the ritual commences, defending the troll from agitated jungle beasts is necessary to lure the creature forth.",h="Deep within Stranglethorn Vale, Witch Doctor Unbagwa claims to know how to draw out the beast known as Mokk...",sec={{t="A Ritual for the Savage",b="Witch Doctor Unbagwa possesses the ritual knowledge needed to summon Mokk the Savage out of the surrounding jungle. To begin the incantation, the witch doctor demands ten Gorilla Fangs. Communing with the spirits carries a heavy risk, as the ritual chant draws the attention of other gorilla beasts in the vicinity, demanding protection while the magic does its work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Witch Doctor Unbagwa?",a="Witch Doctor Unbagwa is a troll practitioner in Stranglethorn Vale who claims to speak with the spirits to lure the great ape Mokk the Savage.",al={"unbagwa","who is unbagwa","witch doctor unbagwa"}},{q="What does Witch Doctor Unbagwa require to start?",a="The witch doctor requires ten Gorilla Fangs before agreeing to speak with the spirits.",al={"gorilla fang quest","what item for unbagwa","unbagwa requirements"}},{q="Why must the witch doctor be defended?",a="Speaking with the spirits draws in the other gorilla beasts around him. Unbagwa cannot finish the communion to summon Mokk if overrun by these beasts.",al={"why defend unbagwa","defend witch doctor unbagwa","gorilla beasts ritual"}},{q="Who is Mokk the Savage?",a="Mokk the Savage is a formidable gorilla beast prowling Stranglethorn Vale that Witch Doctor Unbagwa knows how to summon.",al={"mokk","who is mokk","mokk the savage"}}},kw={"gorilla fang","mokk the savage","stranglethorn fever","stranglethorn vale","unbagwa","witch doctor"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Witch Doctor Unbagwa",["end"]="Witch Doctor Unbagwa",level="35",faction="Neutral",id=349},src={"Stranglethorn Fever (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3625"] = {t="quest",n="Enchanted Azsharite Fel Weaponry",z="stranglethorn",s="In Stranglethorn Vale, the master smith Galvan the Ancient works to fashion specialized armament capable of striking down powerful demons. This forging provides an enchanted weapon imbued with the Felcurse, designed specifically to weaken Razelikh the Defiler and his servitors.",h="In Stranglethorn Vale, the master smith Galvan the Ancient works to fashion specialized armament capable of...",sec={{t="A Weapon Against the Defiler",b="Galvan the Ancient requires patience while he works his craft just south of the path leading into Zul'Gurub. Rushing the forging risks creating a flawed blade, staff, or dagger. Once completed, the chosen weapon carries the power of the Felcurse, which can be unleashed periodically to weaken Razelikh the Defiler and his demonic underlings. The duration of this debilitating curse can vary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who forges these weapons?",a="Galvan the Ancient, a master smith found south of the road leading toward Zul'Gurub in Stranglethorn Vale, crafts the weaponry.",al={"who makes the weapon","galvan the ancient","who is the smith"}},{q="What power does the forged weapon hold?",a="The weapon channels the Felcurse, a specialized magic meant to weaken the demon Razelikh the Defiler and his demonic minions. Its weakening effects vary in length.",al={"what does the weapon do","felcurse power","how does felcurse work"}},{q="Where does the journey lead after the weapon is forged?",a="Once Galvan finishes the craftsmanship and presents the finished weapon, the path directs you back with Return to the Blasted Lands.",al={"what next","where do i go next","next quest"}}},kw={"azsharite","blasted lands","felbane","felcurse","galvan the ancient","razelikh the defiler","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:3626","zone:stranglethorn","zone:blastedlands","subzone:zul-gurub"},m={start="Galvan the Ancient",["end"]="Galvan the Ancient",level="58",id=3625},src={"Enchanted Azsharite Fel Weaponry"}}
E["quest:3626"] = {t="quest",n="Return to the Blasted Lands",z="stranglethorn",s="With newly forged weapons in hand, you are directed back from Stranglethorn Vale to the Blasted Lands. The spirit of the Fallen Hero of the Horde awaits your return to set you against the demon Razelikh.",h="With newly forged weapons in hand, you are directed back from Stranglethorn Vale to the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Call to Redemption",b="Following the completion of your enchanted armaments, Galvan the Ancient proclaims that the hour of redemption is at hand. You carry the newly crafted weapons back to the Blasted Lands, seeking out the Fallen Hero of the Horde. The ghostly warrior asks whether you are prepared to face Razelikh and his minions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you back to the Blasted Lands?",a="Galvan the Ancient directs you to take your newly fashioned weaponry and return to the Blasted Lands.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","galvan the ancient"}},{q="Whom are you sent to meet in the Blasted Lands?",a="You are sent to speak once again with the Fallen Hero of the Horde, who awaits your arrival to reveal your final confrontation.",al={"who do i turn this in to","where to turn in","fallen hero"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="This step follows Enchanted Azsharite Fel Weaponry, in which your specialized weapons were completed.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite"}},{q="Who is the enemy awaiting you in the Blasted Lands?",a="Upon your return, the Fallen Hero of the Horde asks if you are prepared to face Razelikh and his minions.",al={"who are we fighting","razelikh","final boss"}}},kw={"blasted lands","fallen hero of the horde","fel weaponry","galvan the ancient","razelikh","redemption","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:3625","npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde","zone:blastedlands","zone:stranglethorn","topic:horde"},m={start="Galvan the Ancient",["end"]="Fallen Hero of the Horde",level="58",id=3626},src={"Return to the Blasted Lands"}}
E["quest:568"] = {t="quest",n="The Defense of Grom'gol",z="stranglethorn",s="Commander Aggro'gosh seeks to safeguard the Horde's foothold in Stranglethorn Vale and protect their supply chain to Stonard. To keep that supply chain safe, he directs Horde champions to thin out the Lashtail Raptors outside Grom'gol Base Camp.",h="Commander Aggro'gosh seeks to safeguard the Horde's foothold in Stranglethorn Vale and protect their supply...",sec={{t="Securing the Foothold",b="At Grom'gol Base Camp, Commander Aggro'gosh carries the duty of protecting every member of the Horde within the jungle. The camp exists to keep supplies flowing safely to Stonard, but some of the local inhabitants are standing in the way.",sp=0},{t="Thinning the Jungle Predators",b="The raptors outside Grom'gol are the ones in the way. Aggro'gosh calls upon loyal fighters to thin out the Lashtail Raptors there, then report back to him for reassignment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the defense of the camp?",a="Commander Aggro'gosh, the officer placed in charge of the Warchief's stronghold at Grom'gol Base Camp, orders the raptors outside the camp thinned out.",al={"who gives the quest","commander aggrogosh","quest giver"}},{q="Why is Grom'gol Base Camp important to the Horde?",a="The outpost is vital for establishing a secure line of supply to the Horde encampment at Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"gromgol purpose","why gromgol","supply line"}},{q="What threats are targeting the camp's operations?",a="Some of the local inhabitants are hampering the Horde's supply line to Stonard, and Aggro'gosh wants the Lashtail Raptors outside the camp thinned out.",al={"what enemies","why raptors","what beasts"}},{q="What happens after culling the raptors?",a="Reporting your success back to Commander Aggro'gosh brings new orders from him in the next part of The Defense of Grom'gol.",al={"what is next","quest continuation","follow up"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Grom'gol Base Camp gives the Horde a foothold in the jungle and a safe chain of supply to Stonard."},kw={"aggrogosh","gromgol","horde","lashtail","raptors","stonard","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:stonard","topic:horde","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Commander Aggro'gosh",["end"]="Commander Aggro'gosh",level="36",faction="Horde",id=568},src={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}}
E["quest:569"] = {t="quest",n="The Defense of Grom'gol",z="stranglethorn",s="Commander Aggro'gosh seeks to safeguard Grom'gol's supply lines through Stranglethorn Vale. After the earlier hunt thinning the raptors outside the camp, a band of ogres encamped at the nearby Mizjah Ruins continues to harass supply caravans heading toward Stonard.",h="Commander Aggro'gosh seeks to safeguard Grom'gol's supply lines through Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="Securing the Caravans",b="The Horde's presence in northern Stranglethorn Vale is centered on supplying Stonard, an outpost of vital strategic interest. While Commander Aggro'gosh did not arrive with the intention of fighting every native group, a band of local Mosh'Ogg ogres has claimed the Mizjah Ruins southeast of the camp. Warnings have failed to stop their continuous raids against Horde supply shipments, prompting the commander to order a strike against the ogre brutes and witch doctors holding the ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the ogres based?",a="The ogres occupy the Mizjah Ruins, which lie to the southeast of Grom'gol Base Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"ogre location","where is mizjah ruins","ogre camp"}},{q="Why is Grom'gol targeting these ogres?",a="Grom'gol's main purpose is to route supplies to Stonard. The ogres at the Mizjah Ruins have repeatedly ambushed these caravans despite receiving formal warnings to back off.",al={"why kill the ogres","defense of gromgol reason","why fight moshogg"}},{q="Who orders this strike?",a="Commander Aggro'gosh, the military leader stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp, directs the effort to suppress the ogre threat.",al={"quest giver","who gives the quest","who is aggrogosh"}},{q="What comes before this request?",a="This follows the earlier hunt in which Aggro'gosh had the raptors outside Grom'gol thinned out.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","chain start"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Caravans traveling between Grom'gol and Stonard are vital to sustaining the Horde's presence in the southern Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"aggro'gosh","grom'gol","mizjah ruins","mosh'ogg","ogre brutes","stonard","stranglethorn vale","witch doctors"},rel={"quest:568","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:mizjah-ruins","subzone:stonard","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Commander Aggro'gosh",["end"]="Commander Aggro'gosh",level="37",faction="Horde",id=569},src={"The Defense of Grom'gol (2)"}}
E["quest:570"] = {t="quest",n="Mok'thardin's Enchantment",z="stranglethorn",s="Far Seer Mok'thardin seeks to harness the natural magic of Stranglethorn Vale for the benefit of the Horde. Building upon his previous rituals at Grom'gol Base Camp, he asks for sharp claws and a pristine feline fang to weave a powerful enchantment.",h="Far Seer Mok'thardin seeks to harness the natural magic of Stranglethorn Vale for the benefit of the Horde.",sec={{t="Harnessing the Jungle",b="Within Grom'gol Base Camp, Far Seer Mok'thardin works to understand and bend the feral power of the wild to strengthen the Horde. Having seen success in his initial rites, he promises to craft a specialized enchanted relic for those willing to brave the dense underbrush and stalk the deadly predators prowling the surrounding territory.",sp=0},{t="The Stalkers of Mizjah",b="The ritual demands eight claws taken from shadowmaw panthers and a pristine fang from a tigress. Mok'thardin notes that while these fierce felines wander across Stranglethorn Vale, a gathering of them prowls south-eastward, just past the river running by the Mizjah Ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is requesting these beast parts?",a="Far Seer Mok'thardin, an orc shaman stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale, asks for the ingredients to conduct his rituals.",al={"who gives mok'thardin's enchantment","quest giver mok'thardin","who is mok'thardin"}},{q="Where can the panthers and tigresses be found?",a="The beasts roam broadly throughout the dense jungle, but Mok'thardin directs hunters just across the river to the southeast of the Mizjah Ruins.",al={"shadowmaw claws location","pristine tigress fang location","where to hunt beasts"}},{q="Why does Far Seer Mok'thardin need these items?",a="Mok'thardin is working to harness the innate magic of the jungle to cast powerful enchantments and craft a special item for champions of the Horde.",al={"why collect claws and fangs","mok'thardin ritual purpose","why shadowmaw claws"}},{q="What comes next in Mok'thardin's ritual work?",a="After presenting the claws and fang to Mok'thardin, the far seer continues his ritual crafting in the next stage of the enchantment series.",al={"what is after mok'thardin's enchantment 2","next quest after shadowmaw claws","mok'thardin continuation"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin conducts his rituals to harness the jungle's magic for the Horde."},kw={"enchantment","far seer","grom'gol","mizjah","mok'thardin","shadowmaw","stranglethorn","tigress"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:mizjah-ruins","zone:stranglethorn","topic:horde"},m={start="Far Seer Mok'thardin",["end"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin",level="38",faction="Horde",id=570},src={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}}
E["quest:571"] = {t="quest",n="Mok'thardin's Enchantment",z="stranglethorn",s="Far Seer Mok'thardin in Grom'gol Base Camp needs a sturdy magical binding to hold together the Stranglethorn trophies collected so far. To bind the feathers, claws, and fang securely, he requires an aged sinew harvested from the elder primates roaming southern Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Far Seer Mok'thardin in Grom'gol Base Camp needs a sturdy magical binding to hold together the Stranglethorn...",sec={{t="A Magical Tether",b="Having gathered feathers, claws, and a pristine fang, Far Seer Mok'thardin reaches the next stage of his ritual. To fasten these potent relics together, he requires a magical tether of exceptional toughness. Only the aged sinew of an Elder Mistvale Gorilla will suffice to endure the magic he intends to weave.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Mistvale Elders",b="The beasts carrying the necessary sinew forage in the jungles east of Booty Bay. Mok'thardin warns that only a flawless sinew will do, meaning hunters may need to track and fell several of the elder gorillas before securing a specimen fit for the enchantment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the aged gorilla sinew needed for?",a="Far Seer Mok'thardin requires it as a magical tether to hold the previously gathered feathers, claws, and pristine fang securely together for his enchantment.",al={"why sinew","what does mokthardin need the sinew for","gorilla sinew purpose"}},{q="Where are the Elder Mistvale Gorillas located?",a="Elder Mistvale Gorillas forage in the southern jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, specifically to the east of Booty Bay.",al={"where to find elder mistvale gorilla","mistvale gorilla location","where are gorillas"}},{q="Who requests this hunt?",a="Far Seer Mok'thardin, an orc spiritual guide stationed at Grom'gol Basecamp in Stranglethorn Vale, asks for the sinew.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver"}},{q="Where does this fit into Mok'thardin's enchantment work?",a="This hunt comes after the gathering of the claws and the pristine fang, and Far Seer Mok'thardin's enchantment work carries on afterward.",al={"what comes before this","chain order","prerequisite"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin aids Horde adventurers out of Grom'gol Basecamp, crafting potent jungle magic to bolster their standing in Stranglethorn Vale."},kw={"aged gorilla sinew","booty bay","gorilla","grom'gol","mistvale","mok'thardin","sinew","stranglethorn"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="Far Seer Mok'thardin",["end"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin",level="41",faction="Horde",id=571},src={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment (2)"}}
E["quest:572"] = {t="quest",n="Mok'thardin's Enchantment",z="stranglethorn",s="Far Seer Mok'thardin continues assembling the components for a potent shamanistic item to aid the Horde. After working with feline trophies, he turns his attention toward the feathers worn by the raptors of Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Far Seer Mok'thardin continues assembling the components for a potent shamanistic item to aid the Horde.",sec={{t="Feathers of the Stalker",b="Following the recovery of materials from the jungle's feline predators, Far Seer Mok'thardin reveals that more components are needed before his shamanistic ritual can begin. To forge a tool fit to assist the Warchief, he requires feathers worn by Jungle Stalkers. These raptors inhabit the dense jungle south of Grom'gol Base Camp, not far from the great arena.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the feathers?",a="Far Seer Mok'thardin, an orc shaman stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale, seeks the feathers to complete a ritual enchantment.",al={"quest giver","mok'thardin","who needs feathers"}},{q="Where are the Jungle Stalkers located?",a="A tribe of these raptors can be found living directly south of Grom'gol Base Camp, in the jungle near the Gurubashi Arena.",al={"jungle stalker location","where are raptors","jungle stalker feathers where"}},{q="Why does Far Seer Mok'thardin need Jungle Stalker feathers?",a="Mok'thardin is combining various jungle curiosities and beast trophies through a shamanistic ritual to create an enchanted tool intended to assist the Horde and the Warchief.",al={"purpose of feathers","why stalker feathers","mok'thardin ritual"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="Adventurers previously aided Mok'thardin by hunting the feline beasts of the Vale to gather the initial components for his planned enchantment.",al={"previous quest","prior step"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin intends for the finished enchantment to be a useful tool for the Horde and the Warchief.",["class:Shaman"]="The Far Seer combines jungle trinkets with his shamanistic ritual to make an enchanted item."},kw={"enchantment","feathers","grom'gol","jungle stalker","mok'thardin","raptor","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:horde","quest:570"},m={start="Far Seer Mok'thardin",["end"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin",level="41",faction="Horde",id=572},src={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment (3)"}}
E["quest:573"] = {t="quest",n="Mok'thardin's Enchantment",z="stranglethorn",s="Far Seer Mok'thardin requires one final sacred component to complete the enchantment of a ceremonial choker at Grom'gol Base Camp. He directs you to an elevated Holy Spring along the southern bluffs near the western sea, which has drawn the attention of a hostile naga expedition.",h="Far Seer Mok'thardin requires one final sacred component to complete the enchantment of a ceremonial choker...",sec={{t="A Contested Spring",b="Following the earlier stages of Mok'thardin's enchantment, the far seer seeks water from a Holy Spring situated high above the bluffs in the southern reaches of Stranglethorn Vale, near the western coast. The site is a point of contention among scholars of the mystic and divine, with every race across Azeroth claiming the holy waters were sanctified specifically for their own people.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Incursion",b="A party of naga explorers has moved up to the spring and must be dealt with as well. Mok'thardin requires ten of these serpent intruders slain alongside a draught of the spring water to finish preparing the ceremonial choker in the name of the Warchief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Holy Spring located?",a="The Holy Spring sits high atop the bluffs toward the western coast in the southern region of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"holy spring location","where is holy spring water","holy spring bluffs"}},{q="Why is the Holy Spring considered important?",a="Religious and mystical scholars argue fiercely over the spring, as every race across Azeroth maintains that its divine waters were sanctified especially for them.",al={"why is the spring holy","holy spring significance"}},{q="Who is contesting the Holy Spring?",a="An expedition of naga explorers has advanced onto the bluffs surrounding the Holy Spring, menacing the area.",al={"who attacks the spring","holy spring enemies"}},{q="What is the water being used for?",a="The water serves as the final reagent required by Far Seer Mok'thardin to prepare and enchant a ceremonial choker in defense of the Horde.",al={"why need holy spring water","holy spring water purpose"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin asks Horde champions to help finish a ceremonial choker meant to honor the Warchief and protect the Horde."},kw={"ceremonial choker","grom'gol","holy spring","holy spring water","mok'thardin","naga explorer","stranglethorn"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","topic:horde","topic:naga"},m={start="Far Seer Mok'thardin",["end"]="Far Seer Mok'thardin",level="44",faction="Horde",id=573},src={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment (4)"}}
E["quest:574"] = {t="quest",n="Special Forces",z="stranglethorn",s="Following the reduction of the rogue colonel's rank-and-file soldiers, Sergeant Yohwa asks you to target the elite core of the compound. You are sent into the Stockpile cave to eliminate the commandos and headshrinkers before reporting to Lieutenant Doren.",h="Following the reduction of the rogue colonel's rank-and-file soldiers, Sergeant Yohwa asks you to target the...",sec={{t="Striking the Stockpile",b="With the regular soldiers of the Kurzen Compound diminished through the work of the Second Rebellion, Sergeant Yohwa sets her sights on the colonel's elite specialists. She knows many of Kurzen's troops personally and calls them skilled, loyal and cruel. When they are not out in the wilderness slaughtering rebel soldiers, they are found in a cave at the back of the compound called the Stockpile. To break their strength, you are sent into the cavern to dispatch ten Kurzen Commandos and six Kurzen Headshrinkers.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Command",b="After the fight, Sergeant Yohwa tells you to report to her commanding officer, Lieutenant Doren, at the Rebel Camp, who will want your account firsthand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the attack on Kurzen's elite troops?",a="Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale asks you to undertake this assault after you have helped thin Kurzen's regular infantry.",al={"who gives special forces","special forces questgiver","where to start special forces"}},{q="Where are Kurzen's commandos and headshrinkers located?",a="They are found in a cave at the back of the Kurzen Compound called the Stockpile, though they also range out into the wilderness to hunt rebels.",al={"where are headshrinkers","where is the stockpile","kurzen commando location"}},{q="To whom do you report after clearing the cave?",a="You deliver your firsthand report to Lieutenant Doren, the commanding officer stationed at the Rebel Camp.",al={"who to turn in to","where is doren","who completes special forces"}},{q="What comes before this assault in the rebel campaign?",a="This assignment follows The Second Rebellion, in which you weaken Colonel Kurzen's regular troops across the compound.",al={"special forces prerequisite","what quest comes before special forces"}}},kw={"kurzen commando","kurzen compound","kurzen headshrinker","lieutenant doren","rebel camp","sergeant yohwa","special forces","stockpile"},rel={"quest:203","npc:doren","subzone:rebel-camp","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Sergeant Yohwa",["end"]="Lieutenant Doren",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=574},src={"Special Forces"}}
E["quest:575"] = {t="quest",n="Supply and Demand",z="stranglethorn",s="Drizzlik, a leathercrafter in Booty Bay, claims to be the finest in the South Seas. Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union has placed an order for twelve Excelsior-line boots, and Drizzlik needs skins from crocolisks by the northern Stranglethorn river to start shaping them.",h="Drizzlik, a leathercrafter in Booty Bay, claims to be the finest in the South Seas.",sec={{t="An Order from the Tinkers' Union",b="Drizzlik brags that this leatherwork is famed everywhere as exquisite, a connoisseur's choice. The latest order comes from Director Riddlevox, the Tinkers' Union's chief inventor, who wants a dozen of the Excelsior-line boots he favors, among Drizzlik's best sellers. To begin shaping them, Drizzlik needs skins from the crocolisks by the northern Stranglethorn river. The equipment stands ready, and leaving so important a customer unsatisfied would be a poor idea.",sp=0},{t="Once the Skins Arrive",b="Drizzlik finds the skins good enough. How fine they are matters little, since they will form the inner layer of the boots, though they must still be comfortable. Skins that prove too stiff can be softened with tiger blood, one of the tricks of the trade.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Drizzlik?",a="Drizzlik is a leathercrafter in Booty Bay who boasts of being the finest in the South Seas and beyond.",al={"drizzlik booty bay","booty bay leatherworker"}},{q="Who ordered the Excelsior boots?",a="Director Riddlevox, the Tinkers' Union's chief inventor, ordered twelve Excelsior-line boots.",al={"who ordered the boots","director riddlevox","tinkers union order"}},{q="Where are the crocolisks found for this commission?",a="Drizzlik points to the northern Stranglethorn river, where the crocolisks live.",al={"crocolisk location","where are river crocs","where do i find the skins"}},{q="How many skins does Drizzlik want?",a="Two large river crocolisk skins.",al={"how many crocolisk skins","large river crocolisk skins"}}},kw={"booty bay","crocolisk","drizzlik","excelsior","leathercraft","riddlevox","stranglethorn","tinkers union"},rel={"quest:577","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:south-seas"},m={start="Drizzlik",["end"]="Drizzlik",level="31",id=575},src={"Classic quest text: Supply and Demand"}}
E["quest:576"] = {t="quest",n="Keep An Eye Out",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, the old sea dog Dizzy One-Eye lost his sight in battle and sees only through a special enchanted glass eye. Bloodsail Buccaneers ambushed him last night and took it, and Dizzy asks for help getting the eye back.",h="In Booty Bay, the old sea dog Dizzy One-Eye lost his sight in battle and sees only through a special...",sec={{t="The Enchanted Eye",b="Dizzy One-Eye lost both eyes in battle. By good fortune, Dizzy's ship docked at Menethil, where a traveling wizard made a special enchanted glass eye that gave Dizzy sight again. Without it, Dizzy feels useless, and recalls that the crow's nest was once home.",sp=0},{t="Taken by the Buccaneers",b="Last night, Bloodsail Buccaneers ambushed Dizzy on the way out and took the eye. It seems the Bloodsails have made their way into Booty Bay. Dizzy fears the captain will keelhaul Dizzy once the eye's fate comes out, and reckons a lookout who cannot see might only be fit for scrubbing the bilge. So Dizzy asks for help getting the eye back from the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dizzy One-Eye?",a="Dizzy One-Eye is an old sea dog in Booty Bay who worked as a lookout. Dizzy lost both eyes in battle and sees only through an enchanted glass eye.",al={"dizzy one eye","who gives keep an eye out","who is dizzy"}},{q="Where did Dizzy get the magical eye?",a="Dizzy's ship put in at Menethil, where a wizard passing through made a special enchanted glass eye that let Dizzy see again.",al={"how did dizzy get his eye","dizzy enchanted eye origin","glass eye wizard"}},{q="Who took Dizzy's eye?",a="Bloodsail Buccaneers ambushed Dizzy last night on the way out and took the eye.",al={"who stole the eye","who took dizzy eye","who has dizzy eye"}},{q="What does Dizzy fear will happen without the eye?",a="Dizzy fears the captain will keelhaul Dizzy for it, and reckons a lookout who cannot see might only be fit for scrubbing the bilge.",al={"what happens if dizzy loses eye","dizzy captain penalty"}}},kw={"bloodsail","booty bay","buccaneers","dizzy","glass eye","menethil","one-eye","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","quest:595","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Dizzy One-Eye",["end"]="Dizzy One-Eye",level="42",id=576},src={"Classic quest text: Keep An Eye Out"}}
E["quest:577"] = {t="quest",n="Some Assembly Required",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, Drizzlik reports that the boots are taking shape, but the skins you supplied will not cover the inner layers. Drizzlik proposes filling them out with cheaper, thicker hides from crocolisks near Lake Nazferiti.",h="In Booty Bay, Drizzlik reports that the boots are taking shape, but the skins you supplied will not cover the...",sec={{t="Filling the Boots",b="Drizzlik has settled the rough form of the boots and says they are coming along nicely, yet the skins from Supply and Demand do not go far enough for the insides. Nobody will ever see those layers, so Drizzlik will make do with thicker, cheaper hides from the crocolisks near Lake Nazferiti.",sp=0},{t="The Sales Pitch",b="Drizzlik's sales pitch promises the finest workmanship and boots of pure, top-grade saltwater crocolisk hide. Drizzlik likens the boots to sausages: they look great, they taste great, and they are said to hold only the finest ingredients. It is safer, and more enjoyable, to trust the maker and not look too closely at what is really inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for these skins?",a="Drizzlik in Booty Bay, who is working on the Excelsior boots and needs more skins after those delivered in Supply and Demand.",al={"quest giver","who gives some assembly required","drizzlik location"}},{q="What skins does Drizzlik need?",a="Five snapjaw crocolisk skins.",al={"what hides do i need","crocolisk skin type","which crocs"}},{q="Where are the required crocolisks found?",a="Drizzlik sends you to the crocolisks around Lake Nazferiti.",al={"lake nazferiti location","where are snapjaws","where to find crocs"}},{q="Why does Drizzlik want cheaper skins?",a="The insides of the boots stay hidden from every eye, so Drizzlik is happy to fill them out with thicker, cheaper skins.",al={"why cheaper skins","why snapjaw hides","boot padding"}}},kw={"boots","booty bay","crocolisk","drizzlik","lake nazferiti","snapjaw","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:575","quest:628","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:lake-nazferiti","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Drizzlik",["end"]="Drizzlik",level="36",id=577},src={"Classic quest text: Some Assembly Required"}}
E["quest:578"] = {t="quest",n="The Stone of the Tides",z="stranglethorn",s="Following rumours of a haunted isle off the jungle coast, Baron Revilgaz suspects an ancient troll relic has resurfaced. He directs explorers to scout the mysterious landmass and delivers a pass to research the artifact within the archives of Stormwind.",h="Following rumours of a haunted isle off the jungle coast, Baron Revilgaz suspects an ancient troll relic has...",sec={{t="A Magnate's Ambition",b="Having learned of strange apparitions and water elementals haunting an offshore island in Stranglethorn Vale, Baron Revilgaz sees an opportunity. Suspecting that the goblin mage Gazban may have uncovered the fabled Stone of the Tides, the ruler of Booty Bay sends you to locate the island and confirm whether the rumors are true. To satisfy any curiosity about the relic, he provides a library scrip redeemable among the scholars in Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="An Ancient Ward",b="Confirming the unnatural presence on the isle confirms the baron's highest hopes: the legendary artifact is real. Yet claiming it will not be simple. The Stone of the Tides carries a potent magical curse that Revilgaz recognizes he cannot break alone, requiring the expertise of an experienced wizard before any recovery can begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks you to locate the haunted island?",a="Baron Revilgaz, leader of Booty Bay, sends you after hearing tales of strange activity off the coast.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver stone of the tides","who sends you"}},{q="Where is the haunted island located?",a="The island lies off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale, an island out at sea that you will have to find yourself.",al={"where is the island","island location","find haunted island"}},{q="What is the Stone of the Tides?",a="It is a legendary troll artifact that Revilgaz hopes to add to his collection, a legend he first came across in an old book.",al={"what is the stone","stone of tides lore","what is stone of the tides"}},{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz want the artifact?",a="The baron seeks to claim the powerful troll relic to add it to his extensive collection of ancient artifacts and relics.",al={"why does revilgaz want it","revilgaz motives"}},{q="What is the Library Scrip used for?",a="The scrip can be brought to Donyal Tovald at the Stormwind Library to obtain a copy of the book in which the baron first read of the legend.",al={"what is library scrip","stormwind library scrip","where do i take the scrip"}},{q="What was the previous step in this chain?",a="This investigation directly follows The Haunted Isle, which first brought word of the unusual sightings to the baron.",al={"what quest comes before","prerequisite quest"}}},kw={"baron revilgaz","booty bay","donyal tovald","gazban","gurubashi","stone of the tides","stormwind library","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:616","quest:601","npc:baron-revilgaz","quest:579","npc:donyal-tovald","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Baron Revilgaz",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=578},src={"The Stone of the Tides (quest)"}}
E["quest:580"] = {t="quest",n="Whiskey Slim's Lost Grog",z="stranglethorn",s="In the pirate haven of Booty Bay, Whiskey Slim finds himself in dire trouble with his captain. During a violent storm off the coast of the Hinterlands, Slim tapped into a seized crate of Pupellyverbos Port, only to lose the bottles to the churning sea. To escape a brutal flogging, he needs an adventurer to retrieve his misplaced grog.",h="In the pirate haven of Booty Bay, Whiskey Slim finds himself in dire trouble with his captain.",sec={{t="A Tempest off the Hinterlands",b="Whiskey Slim's crew was battling severe weather off the Overlook Cliffs, with the shore of the Hinterlands looming nearby, when the sailor sought a dose of liquid courage. His ship had seized a crate of Pupellyverbos Port from a privateer vessel sailing toward Stormwind. Facing waves that threatened to swallow their ship whole, Slim broke into the captain's crate, but a sudden surge swept the bottles right over the side.",sp=0},{t="A Sailor's Desperation",b="Back in Booty Bay, the clock is ticking down as the ship prepares to weigh anchor. Slim dreads facing the cat-o'-nine-tails once his commanding officer realizes the confiscated port is missing. He seeks someone willing to bring back twelve bottles before his theft comes to light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Whiskey Slim?",a="Whiskey Slim is a sailor residing in Booty Bay who has landed in deep trouble after losing his captain's stolen alcohol during a sea squall.",al={"whiskey slim","who gives lost grog","who is slim"}},{q="Where did the grog come from?",a="The crate of Pupellyverbos Port was commandeered by Slim's crew from a privateer vessel that was on its way to Stormwind.",al={"pupellyverbos port origin","where did slim get the grog","privateer booze"}},{q="Where did Whiskey Slim lose the bottles?",a="Slim lost the bottles overboard during a fierce storm off the Overlook Cliffs, near the coast of the Hinterlands, when a massive wave struck the ship.",al={"where was grog lost","overlook cliffs storm","hinterlands grog location"}},{q="Why does Whiskey Slim need the bottles back so quickly?",a="His ship is preparing to depart, and once the captain discovers his port is missing, Slim fears he will be punished with a flogging from the cat-o'-nine-tails.",al={"why help slim","what happens to slim","taste of the cat"}}},kw={"booty bay","grog","hinterlands","overlook cliffs","privateer","pupellyverbos port","stormwind","whiskey slim"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Whiskey Slim",["end"]="Whiskey Slim",level="50",id=580},src={"Whiskey Slim's Lost Grog"}}
E["quest:581"] = {t="quest",n="Hunt for Yenniku",z="stranglethorn",s="Nimboya has returned from Orgrimmar to the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale to search for Yenniku, the youngest son of his chieftain. Suspecting the Bloodscalp tribe holds the youth captive, the scout asks you to hunt their warriors and take their tusks to demonstrate your strength.",h="Nimboya has returned from Orgrimmar to the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale to search for Yenniku, the youngest...",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Lost Son",b="At Grom'gol Base Camp, Nimboya speaks of a grim fate looming over Yenniku, the youngest son of the Darkspear chieftain. In accordance with an old tribal custom, the boy had been placed among the Gurubashi trolls of Zul'Gurub. When the Darkspear tribe departed their homeland alongside the orc warchief Thrall, Yenniku was left behind and lost. Sent back from distant Orgrimmar, Nimboya has undertaken the responsibility of finding the chieftain's son and bringing him to safety.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Bloodscalps",b="Nimboya believes the Bloodscalp tribe now holds Yenniku. He demands proof that an adventurer is strong enough to hunt them. You are directed north to hunt Bloodscalp trolls and gather nine of their tusks. Bringing these trophies back to Grom'gol Base Camp proves your martial prowess and begins a longer pursuit to locate the chieftain's boy, leading directly into the hunt known as Headhunting.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Yenniku?",a="Yenniku is the youngest son of the Darkspear tribe's chieftain. By tribal custom, he was given to the Gurubashi trolls in Zul'Gurub, but he became separated from his people when the Darkspears left the region.",al={"yenniku lore","who is yenniku","chieftain son"}},{q="Why was Yenniku left behind in Stranglethorn?",a="Tribal custom saw Yenniku sent to the Gurubashi trolls of Zul'Gurub. When the Darkspear tribe allied with Thrall and departed, the youth was lost to them.",al={"why did yenniku stay","how was yenniku lost","why zul'gurub"}},{q="Who is Nimboya?",a="Nimboya is a Darkspear troll stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp. He was dispatched from distant Orgrimmar back to Stranglethorn Vale to search for his chieftain's lost son.",al={"who gives hunt for yenniku","nimboya","grom'gol scout"}},{q="Why do you need to collect Bloodscalp tusks?",a="Nimboya suspects the Bloodscalp tribe has captured Yenniku. He requires nine Bloodscalp tusks as proof that you have the strength to hunt these hostile trolls before continuing the search.",al={"bloodscalp tusks purpose","why tusks","hunt for yenniku tusks"}},{q="Where are the Bloodscalp trolls located?",a="Nimboya directs hunters to seek out the Bloodscalp tribe in the territory to the north of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"where to find bloodscalps","bloodscalp location","where are bloodscalp trolls"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, answering Nimboya's call means aiding their own chieftain's family and hunting the Bloodscalps who may hold him.",["faction:Horde"]="Sent directly from Orgrimmar, Nimboya relies on Horde allies operating out of Grom'gol Base Camp to help secure the Darkspear chieftain's kin."},kw={"bloodscalp","darkspear","grom'gol","hunt for yenniku","nimboya","stranglethorn","tusks","yenniku","zul'gurub"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:zul-gurub","npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll"},m={start="Nimboya",["end"]="Nimboya",level="34",faction="Horde",id=581},src={"Hunt for Yenniku (Classic)","In-game quest text: Hunt for Yenniku"}}
E["quest:582"] = {t="quest",n="Headhunting",z="stranglethorn",s="Nimboya at Grom'gol Base Camp needs to determine whether Yenniku, the son of the Darkspear chieftain, is dead. Adventurers are asked to hunt Bloodscalp headhunters and recover their shrunken heads so Nimboya can examine them.",h="Nimboya at Grom'gol Base Camp needs to determine whether Yenniku, the son of the Darkspear chieftain, is dead.",sec={{t="Searching the Trophies",b="Following the search begun in Hunt for Yenniku, Nimboya worries that the chieftain's son may have already perished at the hands of the Bloodscalp tribe. To find out, he asks you to hunt the Bloodscalp Headhunters roaming the ruins of Zuuldaia and Zul'Kunda up the northern coast. By gathering twenty shrunken heads from them, Nimboya hopes to inspect the grisly trophies and confirm whether Yenniku met a violent end, cursing the Bloodscalp chief Gan'zulah if the youth was indeed slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is looking for Yenniku?",a="Nimboya at Grom'gol Base Camp is searching for Yenniku, who is the son of the Darkspear tribe's chieftain.",al={"who gives headhunting","nimboya purpose","why find yenniku"}},{q="Why does Nimboya want shrunken heads?",a="Nimboya plans to inspect the shrunken heads taken from Bloodscalp headhunters to verify whether Yenniku's head is among their trophies.",al={"why collect shrunken heads","shrunken head purpose","what does nimboya do with heads"}},{q="Where can the Bloodscalp Headhunters be found?",a="Bloodscalp Headhunters gather along the northern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, particularly around the ruins of Zuuldaia and Zul'Kunda.",al={"headhunter location","where are zuuldaia and zulkunda","where to find shrunken heads"}},{q="Who leads the Bloodscalp tribe mentioned here?",a="The Bloodscalps are led by Chief Gan'zulah, upon whose spirit Nimboya wishes a six-hundred-year curse should Yenniku be dead.",al={"bloodscalp chief","who is ganzulah","ganzulah chief"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The fate of the chief's son is deeply personal to the Darkspear, who must face the Bloodscalp tribe to learn what happened to him.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Grom'gol Base Camp, Horde forces assist their Darkspear allies in discovering whether the chieftain's missing son still lives."},kw={"bloodscalp","gan'zulah","grom'gol base camp","headhunting","nimboya","shrunken head","yenniku","zul'kunda","zuuldaia"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","quest:584","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Nimboya",["end"]="Nimboya",level="37",faction="Horde",id=582},src={"Headhunting (Classic)"}}
E["quest:583"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome to the Jungle",z="stranglethorn",s="Barnil Stonepot welcomes newcomers arriving at the hunting camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Recognizing a fellow battle-tested wanderer, he arranges an introduction to the expedition's leader, the renowned huntsman Hemet Nesingwary.",h="Barnil Stonepot welcomes newcomers arriving at the hunting camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="An Audience with the Master",b="Barnil Stonepot greets newcomers at the camp in the jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, and he can tell a seasoned combatant when he sees one. He points out Hemet Nesingwary, a famous Alliance war hero and peerless tracker. Nesingwary reserves his fellowship for proven veterans, and Barnil believes the old marksman might be convinced to share his hunting wisdom with someone who has endured the trials of battle.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of the Expedition",b="Nesingwary welcomes you warmly, noting how rare it is to see someone of your calling in these wild lands. He explains that his expedition gathered here with a single goal: pursuing a legendary, elusive jungle beast. While he is willing to include you in the grand chase, trust must be earned through the blood of lesser quarry. Nesingwary personally oversees the stalking of raptors, while his comrades Ajeck and Sir Erlgadin tutor hunters in the ways of tigers and panthers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Hemet Nesingwary?",a="Hemet Nesingwary is a celebrated Alliance war veteran and a renowned big game hunter. He leads an expedition camp in the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"hemet nesingwary","who is hemet","nesingwary lore"}},{q="Who sends you to speak with Nesingwary?",a="Barnil Stonepot, one of the members stationed at the jungle encampment, directs seasoned adventurers to greet Nesingwary after recognizing their combat experience.",al={"barnil stonepot","quest giver","who starts welcome to the jungle"}},{q="What comes after speaking with Nesingwary?",a="Several hunts open up: Raptor Mastery, Tiger Mastery, Panther Mastery and The Green Hills of Stranglethorn.",al={"how to join the hunt","nesingwary trials","hunting lessons"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For a hunter wandering the jungles of Stranglethorn, Hemet Nesingwary may have some hunting pointers to share.",["faction:Alliance"]="Barnil Stonepot points out that Hemet Nesingwary is a renowned war hero of the Alliance with a soft spot for fellow veterans.",["race:Dwarf"]="The camp's famed hunter, Hemet Nesingwary, is a dwarf like you, and Barnil Stonepot points him out as a master big game hunter."},kw={"barnil","hemet","nesingwary","panther","raptor","stonepot","stranglethorn","tiger"},rel={"quest:5762","zone:stranglethorn","quest:194","quest:185","quest:190","quest:338","topic:alliance","topic:hunter"},m={start="Barnil Stonepot",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="30",faction="Neutral",id=583},src={"Welcome to the Jungle (Classic)"}}
E["quest:584"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodscalp Clan Heads",z="stranglethorn",s="Following the sorting of trophies gathered in the jungle, Nimboya confirms that the missing young troll Yenniku was not among them. To discover the truth of Yenniku's fate, the Darkspear seek to compel answers from the leaders of the rival Bloodscalp tribe.",h="Following the sorting of trophies gathered in the jungle, Nimboya confirms that the missing young troll...",sec={{t="Demanding Answers from the Dead",b="After the earlier hunt proved Yenniku was not among the fallen Bloodscalp trophies, Nimboya looks to higher leadership for answers. The Bloodscalp chief, Gan'zulah, and his witch doctor, Nezzliok the Dire, are enemies of the Darkspear tribe and would never talk willingly. Nimboya means to force the truth from their dead lips, bringing their heads to the cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp to make them talk.",sp=0},{t="Into Zul'Kunda",b="Both Bloodscalp leaders dwell deep within the ruins of Zul'Kunda in northwestern Stranglethorn Vale. Claiming their heads and casting them into the boiling brew is how Nimboya means to make them talk about Yenniku.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Nimboya want the heads of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok?",a="Yenniku is still missing, and Nimboya believes only the Bloodscalp chief and his witch doctor hold the truth. Because these leaders are enemies of the Darkspear and would never talk willingly, Nimboya plans to force the truth from their dead lips with the cauldron.",al={"why kill bloodscalp leaders","why severed heads","nimboya motivation"}},{q="Where are Gan'zulah and Nezzliok located?",a="Both troll leaders reside deep within Zul'Kunda, a ruin in northwestern Stranglethorn Vale, close to the beach.",al={"where is ganzulah","where is nezzliok","find bloodscalp chiefs","zulkunda location"}},{q="What happens once the heads are delivered?",a="The severed heads are placed directly into the bubbling cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp, so the two leaders can be made to talk.",al={"where do the heads go","what do i do with the heads","bubbling cauldron turn in"}},{q="How does this connect to the search for Yenniku?",a="This investigation began with the search for young Yenniku. After earlier headhunting proved he was not among the common dead, questioning the Bloodscalp leaders is the next effort to track his whereabouts.",al={"yenniku questline","hunt for yenniku connection"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, confronting the Bloodscalp chiefs means facing the leaders of a tribe that is their enemy.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde fighters at Grom'gol Base Camp lend their strength to the Darkspear search for Yenniku."},kw={"bloodscalp","cauldron","darkspear","gan'zulah","grom'gol","nezzliok","nimboya","yenniku","zul'kunda"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","quest:581","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:troll","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Nimboya",["end"]="Bubbling Cauldron",level="41",faction="Horde",id=584},src={"Bloodscalp Clan Heads"}}
E["quest:585"] = {t="quest",n="Speaking with Nezzliok",z="stranglethorn",s="After defeating the Bloodscalp witch doctor, his severed head speaks from the bubbling cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp. He claims to know where the lost Darkspear child was taken, but he refuses to give up the secret without a grim tribute.",h="After defeating the Bloodscalp witch doctor, his severed head speaks from the bubbling cauldron at Grom'gol...",sec={{t="A Spirit's Price",b="Though bound within the bubbling cauldron following the hunt for Bloodscalp Clan Heads, Nezzliok is far from cooperative. He admits knowing where Yenniku was taken, yet he demands appeasement before parting with the information. He commands that three trophy skulls be taken from the rival Skullsplitter tribe and brought to his resting place, ensuring his departed spirit will command thralls in the Nether.",sp=0},{t="Skulls of the Rivals",b="Nezzliok demands one skull taken directly from the Skullsplitter trophy pile at Balia'mah, a second from Ziata'jai, and a third from Zul'Mamwe. Only when all three offerings rest alongside his own head will the dead witch doctor consider his spirit satisfied.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nezzliok?",a="Nezzliok was a witch doctor of the Bloodscalp tribe. After falling in battle, his severed head was placed into a bubbling cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp, where his bound spirit continues to speak.",al={"nezzliok","witch doctor nezzliok","nezzliok lore"}},{q="What does Nezzliok demand?",a="He demands three trophy skulls stolen from the camps of his hated rivals, the Skullsplitters: one from Balia'mah, one from Ziata'jai, and one from Zul'Mamwe.",al={"what does nezzliok want","nezzliok trophies","speaking with nezzliok objective"}},{q="Why does Nezzliok want Skullsplitter trophies?",a="Nezzliok wants the trophy skulls placed with him so that when his spirit passes into the Nether, he will possess three servants bound to him in death.",al={"why trophy skulls","why nezzliok wants skulls"}},{q="Where does this happen?",a="The encounter takes place at the bubbling cauldron situated in Grom'gol Base Camp, deep in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is nezzliok","bubbling cauldron location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on bargaining with a bound enemy spirit at Grom'gol Base Camp to unravel the disappearance of Yenniku, the son of the Darkspear chieftain.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls must barter with the severed head of a hostile Bloodscalp witch doctor to uncover what became of their chieftain's stolen son."},kw={"balia'mah","bloodscalp","cauldron","grom'gol","nezzliok","skullsplitter","stranglethorn","yenniku","ziata'jai","zul'mamwe"},rel={"quest:584","quest:586","quest:588","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Bubbling Cauldron",["end"]="Bubbling Cauldron",level="40",faction="Horde",id=585},src={"Speaking with Nezzliok (Classic)"}}
E["quest:586"] = {t="quest",n="Speaking with Gan'zulah",z="stranglethorn",s="Even after losing his head to the boiling brew at Grom'gol Base Camp, the Bloodscalp chieftain Gan'zulah seethes with fury. To appease his lingering rage, the severed spirit demands the death of his bitter Skullsplitter rivals and the ruin of their ruler, Ana'thek the Cruel.",h="Even after losing his head to the boiling brew at Grom'gol Base Camp, the Bloodscalp chieftain Gan'zulah...",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Vengeance",b="Following the collection of the Bloodscalp Clan Heads, Gan'zulah's severed head continues to curse anyone standing over the bubbling pot. Consumed by hatred for both his captors and his ancestral enemies, the dead chieftain offers an avenue to quiet his boiling temper: an assault into the eastern stronghold of the Skullsplitter tribe. He demands a slaughter of their hunters, headhunters, and berserkers, daring travelers to perish against their ferocious warband.",sp=0},{t="The Broken Armor",b="Gan'zulah expects the assault to end in disaster, fully anticipating that Chief Ana'thek the Cruel will tear apart any intruder who dares challenge him. He demands nothing less than the shattered armor stripped from the Skullsplitter ruler himself as proof of triumph. Only bearing this trophy back to the cauldron in Grom'gol Base Camp can satisfy the dead chieftain's spite.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Peace",b="Presenting the shattered armor of Ana'thek silences Gan'zulah's insults. Faced with the reality of his rival's downfall, the chieftain's vengeful wrath finally relents. Though he acknowledges the strength required to defeat Ana'thek, he promises that this victory only delays their reckoning, swearing to clash again in the Nether.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Gan'zulah want you to go?",a="Gan'zulah directs you eastward into the heart of Skullsplitter territory, toward the settlement where their fighters gather under the command of Ana'thek the Cruel.",al={"where are the skullsplitters","where to go speaking with ganzulah","skullsplitter location"}},{q="Who is Ana'thek the Cruel?",a="Ana'thek the Cruel is the chieftain of the Skullsplitter trolls, a hated rival of Gan'zulah and the Bloodscalp tribe.",al={"who is anatek","who is the skullsplitter chief","anatek the cruel lore"}},{q="Why is Gan'zulah able to talk?",a="Gan'zulah's severed head sits immersed within the enchanted cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp, allowing his spirit to voice his lingering curses and demands from beyond death.",al={"how is ganzulah talking","why is the head talking","ganzulah cauldron"}},{q="What trophy does Gan'zulah demand?",a="He demands the broken armor stripped from Chief Ana'thek the Cruel, and the slaying of the Skullsplitter hunters, headhunters, and berserkers.",al={"what item does ganzulah need","broken armor of anatek","ganzulah turn in item"}},{q="What comes next after helping Gan'zulah?",a="Once the tribal chieftains are dealt with, the search continues with The Fate of Yenniku to uncover what became of the young Darkspear troll.",al={"what follows speaking with ganzulah","next quest after ganzulah","speaking with ganzulah follow up"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Gan'zulah's head sits in the cauldron at Grom'gol Base Camp, and he sends Horde champions against his Skullsplitter enemies.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, watching ancient rivals like the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter chieftains turn their undying hatred against each other is a grim reminder of the jungle's brutal feuds."},kw={"ana'thek","berserker","bloodscalp","cauldron","gan'zulah","grom'gol","headhunter","skullsplitter","stranglethorn"},rel={"quest:584","quest:585","quest:588","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:ruins-of-zul-mamwe","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Bubbling Cauldron",["end"]="Bubbling Cauldron",level="46",faction="Horde",id=586},src={"Speaking with Gan'zulah"}}
E["quest:587"] = {t="quest",n="Up to Snuff",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, the pirate Deeg likes a bottle of grog and fine snuff whenever in port, but the town's herbalist has sold out. The herbalist says Bloodsail Raiders hijacked the shipment, and Deeg wants fifteen shares of snuff brought to him.",h="In Booty Bay, the pirate Deeg likes a bottle of grog and fine snuff whenever in port, but the town's...",sec={{t="Vices Ashore",b="Deeg admits the sea life may not be the good life, yet it is the only one Deeg has. In port, Deeg looks for grog and good-quality snuff: bad habits, but a pirate needs his vices. Deeg was crushed to learn that the herbalist in Booty Bay has none left. The herbalist claims Bloodsail Raiders hijacked the shipment. Deeg figures a fearless adventurer could talk the raiders into sharing, and wants fifteen shares of snuff.",sp=0},{t="Deeg's Thanks",b="Deeg is delighted with the snuff, glad it arrived just before time to ship out, and thanks you warmly as an old friend.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Deeg?",a="Deeg is a pirate in Booty Bay who looks for grog and fine snuff whenever in port.",al={"deeg booty bay","who gives up to snuff"}},{q="Why is the herbalist out of snuff?",a="According to the herbalist, the shipment of snuff was hijacked by the Bloodsail Raiders.",al={"why no snuff","herbalist shipment hijacked"}},{q="Who has the snuff?",a="According to the herbalist, Bloodsail Raiders hijacked the shipment, and Deeg hopes they can be talked into sharing it.",al={"who took the snuff","bloodsail snuff"}},{q="How much snuff does Deeg want?",a="Fifteen shares of snuff, brought to Deeg in Booty Bay.",al={"how many snuff","up to snuff requirement"}}},kw={"bloodsail","booty bay","deeg","grog","herbalist","snuff"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:pirate"},m={start="Deeg",["end"]="Deeg",level="41",id=587},src={"Classic quest text: Up to Snuff"}}
E["quest:588"] = {t="quest",n="The Fate of Yenniku",z="stranglethorn",s="At Grom'gol Base Camp, the head of Nezzliok speaks from the bubbling cauldron, ready to tell what became of the young Darkspear troll Yenniku. Kin'weelay stands beside the pot, waiting to hear the spirit's words.",h="At Grom'gol Base Camp, the head of Nezzliok speaks from the bubbling cauldron, ready to tell what became of...",sec={{t="Words from the Kettle",b="Having placated the spirits of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok, you listen as the head within the bubbling cauldron finally imparts its secret. Kin'weelay stands right beside the cauldron, waiting to hear it.",sp=0},{t="What the Head Revealed",b="Nezzliok declares that Yenniku is lost to his clan, taken by the witch doctor Zanzil the Outcast. Zanzil has bound the boy completely, and nothing short of very strong magic will free him. Kin'weelay, hearing it, is left with only a faint hope.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who reveals Yenniku's whereabouts?",a="The head of Nezzliok speaks through the bubbling cauldron to disclose what happened to Yenniku.",al={"who speaks from cauldron","who reveals fate of yenniku","cauldron voice"}},{q="Who should be informed of Nezzliok's words?",a="Kin'weelay, who stands right beside the bubbling cauldron at the northern edge of Grom'gol Base Camp, needs to hear what Nezzliok revealed.",al={"who do i talk to","turn in fate of yenniku","kin'weelay location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the chief's son is vital for the Darkspear tribe and their allies stationed within Grom'gol Base Camp."},kw={"cauldron","grom'gol","kin'weelay","nezzliok","yenniku","zanzil"},rel={"npc:kin-weelay","quest:589","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll"},m={start="Bubbling Cauldron",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="45",faction="Horde",id=588},src={"The Fate of Yenniku"}}
E["quest:589"] = {t="quest",n="The Singing Crystals",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay seeks a way to rescue young Yenniku from the darkness that has claimed him. Following the revelation of Yenniku's plight, the witch doctor plans to locate a legendary jewel known as the Mind's Eye, sending you to gather resonance shards needed to master its power.",h="Kin'weelay seeks a way to rescue young Yenniku from the darkness that has claimed him.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Mind's Eye",b="After learning the grim fate that befell Yenniku, the medicine man Kin'weelay turns to ancient jungle lore for an answer. Tales speak of the Mind's Eye, a gem hidden within the depths of Stranglethorn that possesses immense magical strength. Kin'weelay believes this stone could hold the secret to freeing the young troll's spirit. While he communally seeks the guidance of the jungle spirits to pinpoint its location, he needs rare catalysts to safely command the jewel's potent sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Crystalvein Caverns",b="Kin'weelay directs you southeast toward Crystalvein Mine, where ironjaw basilisks dwell beneath the earth. From these creatures, you are to recover three pulsing blue shards. Kin'weelay intends to channel the inherent magic of these singing stones in a concluding ritual, bending the raw might of the Mind's Eye to his command once the gem is recovered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this task?",a="Kin'weelay, a troll medicine man stationed at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale, gives this assignment.",al={"who gives the singing crystals","quest giver","where to start the singing crystals"}},{q="Why are the pulsing blue shards needed?",a="Kin'weelay requires their magic to control the Mind's Eye, a powerful jewel he intends to use to pull Yenniku back from the dark forces that hold him.",al={"why do we need blue shards","what are the shards for","pulsing blue shard purpose"}},{q="Where can the ironjaw basilisks be found?",a="They dwell inside Crystalvein Mine, located southeast of Grom'gol Base Camp up in the peaks to the east of the Gurubashi Arena.",al={"ironjaw basilisk location","where are ironjaw basilisks","where is crystalvein mine"}},{q="What came before this task?",a="This follows The Fate of Yenniku, which established the young troll's dire circumstances.",al={"singing crystals prequest","previous quest"}},{q="What is Kin'weelay doing while you gather the shards?",a="He communes with the spirits of the jungle to uncover the exact hiding place of the Mind's Eye and find out what protects it.",al={"what is kinweelay doing","kinweelay role"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This effort aids the Darkspear tribe at Grom'gol Base Camp in their desperate struggle to recover the lost son of the Darkspear chief."},kw={"crystalvein mine","grom'gol","ironjaw basilisk","kin'weelay","mind's eye","pulsing blue shard","stranglethorn","yenniku"},rel={"quest:588","quest:591","npc:kin-weelay","subzone:crystalvein-mine","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:gurubashi-arena"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="45",faction="Horde",id=589},src={"The Singing Crystals"}}
E["quest:591"] = {t="quest",n="The Mind's Eye",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp seeks a powerful gem known as the Mind's Eye, an artifact essential for rescuing young Yenniku. The stone rests in the hands of the formidable ogre spellcaster Mai'Zoth, who dwells deep within the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound.",h="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp seeks a powerful gem known as the Mind's Eye, an artifact essential for...",sec={{t="A Powerful Gem",b="Following the recovery of the singing crystals, Kin'weelay turns his attention toward securing the Mind's Eye. This potent artifact is the solitary instrument capable of aiding the rescue of Yenniku, the son of the Darkspear chieftain. However, the stone is currently held by Mai'Zoth, a ruthless ogre mage whose presence Kin'weelay remembers from the tribe's earlier days in the jungle.",sp=0},{t="The Depths of Mosh'Ogg",b="Mai'Zoth resides deep inside the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound to the east of Grom'gol. His magical prowess was formidable even before acquiring the Mind's Eye, and the stone has only amplified his strength. Confronting him amidst the ogre stronghold is fraught with peril, but wresting the artifact from his grasp remains the sole hope of freeing the young troll.",sp=0},{t="Into the Nether",b="With the recovery of the gem, Kin'weelay notes that defeating Mai'Zoth casts the ogre mage out of the realm of flesh and bone into the Nether. While his physical threat is extinguished, Kin'weelay harbors quiet concern that Mai'Zoth may begin a new dominion within the spirit world. For the moment, however, those worries are set aside so the witch doctor can prepare the ritual needed for Saving Yenniku.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who possesses the Mind's Eye?",a="The Mind's Eye is held by Mai'Zoth, an ogre mage who makes his lair deep within the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound east of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"who has minds eye","where is the minds eye","who drops the minds eye"}},{q="Why does Kin'weelay need the Mind's Eye?",a="Kin'weelay requires the artifact to perform a ritual, which he believes is the only way to save Yenniku, the lost son of the Darkspear chief.",al={"why do we need minds eye","purpose of minds eye","why get the minds eye"}},{q="Where does this stand in the search for Yenniku?",a="This follows The Singing Crystals. Once the Mind's Eye is secured, the path opens for the next step, Saving Yenniku.",al={"what quest comes before the minds eye","previous quest minds eye","what comes after singing crystals"}},{q="Who is Mai'Zoth?",a="Mai'Zoth is a vicious ogre mage known to Kin'weelay from the era when the Darkspear trolls inhabited the jungle. His magic is exceptionally strong, magnified further by the power of the Mind's Eye.",al={"who is maizoth","about maizoth","maizoth lore"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Recovering the Mind's Eye is vital to freeing Yenniku, the son of the Darkspear chieftain.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Grom'gol Base Camp, this effort strikes directly at the ogre stronghold of Mosh'Ogg on behalf of the Darkspear trolls."},kw={"darkspear","grom'gol","kin'weelay","mai'zoth","mind's eye","mosh'ogg","ogre mound","yenniku"},rel={"quest:589","quest:592","npc:kin-weelay","quest:206","subzone:mosh-ogg-ogre-mound","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:mage"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="46",faction="Horde",id=591},src={"The Mind's Eye (Classic)"}}
E["quest:592"] = {t="quest",n="Saving Yenniku",z="stranglethorn",s="After obtaining the Mind's Eye, Kin'weelay crafts it into a specialized soul gem to rescue the young troll Yenniku from Zanzil the Outcast. The enchanted vessel is designed to stun Yenniku and capture his spirit, allowing him to be freed and carried back to Nimboya.",h="After obtaining the Mind's Eye, Kin'weelay crafts it into a specialized soul gem to rescue the young troll...",sec={{t="A Vessel for the Spirit",b="Following the recovery of the Mind's Eye, Kin'weelay reshapes the potent relic into a magical soul gem. Its dual enchantment allows an adventurer to first stun Yenniku and then place the stone upon his head to capture his wayward spirit within. Once the boy's essence is contained inside the gem, it can safely be returned to his kin at Grom'gol Base Camp.",sp=0},{t="The Outcast's Lair",b="Yenniku resides alongside Zanzil the Outcast within the Ruins of Aboraz, situated along the Crystal Shore on the southern reaches of the Cape of Stranglethorn. Reaching the fallen youth requires venturing into Zanzil's territory, using the crafted vessel to break the witch doctor's hold over him, and carrying the filled gem back to Nimboya.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who provides the Soul Gem for this task?",a="Kin'weelay crafts and provides the Soul Gem after reshaping the recovered Mind's Eye, sending you on to retrieve Yenniku's spirit.",al={"who gives the soul gem","where do I get the soul gem","who starts saving yenniku"}},{q="Where is Yenniku located?",a="Yenniku can be found with Zanzil the Outcast at the Ruins of Aboraz, on the Crystal Shore, far out on the Cape of Stranglethorn.",al={"where is yenniku","yenniku location","ruins of aboraz location"}},{q="How does the Soul Gem work?",a="The reshaped gem has a twofold enchantment: it is used first to stun Yenniku, and then placed directly upon his head to draw his soul inside.",al={"how to use soul gem","what does the soul gem do","soul gem stranglethorn"}},{q="Who receives the Filled Soul Gem once Yenniku is secured?",a="Once Yenniku's soul is safely trapped within the gem, it must be delivered to Nimboya back at Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"where to turn in filled soul gem","who gets the gem","where to deliver yenniku"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear tribe, freeing young Yenniku from the vile magic of Zanzil the Outcast brings a captive Darkspear youth back toward his people.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers from Grom'gol Base Camp carry Nimboya's search for Yenniku to Zanzil at the Ruins of Aboraz."},kw={"aboraz","kin'weelay","nimboya","saving yenniku","soul gem","stranglethorn","yenniku","zanzil"},rel={"quest:591","quest:593","quest:581","npc:kin-weelay","subzone:ruins-of-aboraz","subzone:crystal-shore","subzone:cape-of-stranglethorn","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Nimboya",level="46",faction="Horde",id=592},src={"Saving Yenniku (Classic)"}}
E["quest:593"] = {t="quest",n="Filling the Soul Gem",z="stranglethorn",s="Deep in the jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, an attempt is made to preserve the young troll Yenniku. With the youth caught in a trance, a prepared soul gem is brought forth to capture his spirit.",h="Deep in the jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, an attempt is made to preserve the young troll Yenniku.",sec={{t="A Trance in the Jungle",b="Following the effort to save Yenniku, you stand face to face with the young troll in Stranglethorn Vale. His mind is lost, caught entirely in another place while he remains motionless before you. The only path forward involves the enchanted gem prepared specifically to hold his essence.",sp=0},{t="The Vessel",b="Pressing the gem to Yenniku's forehead pulls his spirit directly into the stone. As the essence is drawn away, his physical form shudders and collapses into an empty, mindless shell.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What condition is Yenniku in when you reach him?",a="Yenniku stands stunned and unresponsive, his thoughts held far away from his physical surroundings.",al={"yenniku status","what is wrong with yenniku","yenniku stunned"}},{q="What item is used on Yenniku?",a="A soul gem brought from Stranglethorn Vale is used to interact with the young troll.",al={"what item is needed","gem used on yenniku","yenniku item"}},{q="What came before this moment?",a="This encounter directly follows the events of Saving Yenniku in the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"previous quest","prereq for filling the soul gem","what leads to this"}}},kw={"saving yenniku","soul gem","stranglethorn vale","troll","yenniku"},rel={"quest:592","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="None",["end"]="Yenniku",level="46",faction="Horde",id=593},src={"Filling the Soul Gem"}}
E["quest:594"] = {t="quest",n="Message in a Bottle",z="stranglethorn",s="A washed-up bottle found along the shores of Stranglethorn Vale holds an urgent plea for rescue. Its author claims to be held prisoner by a great beast on an isolated island in the South Seas.",h="A washed-up bottle found along the shores of Stranglethorn Vale holds an urgent plea for rescue.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Waves",b="Inside a glass container half-buried in the sand lies a neatly penned note asking for immediate assistance. The captive reports being trapped on a foreign island beneath thick jungle canopies, held by a great Skymane. Glimpses through the trees offer only faint landmarks: the coast of Wild Shore lies visible to the northwest, while large sailing vessels drift to the southwest.",sp=0},{t="The Writer of the Note",b="Following the nautical directions leads across the water to an offshore isle, where the message's writer awaits. The stranded captive is Princess Poobah, desperate for an adventurer to finally reach her and offer a chance at freedom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the note in the bottle say?",a="The message is an urgent plea written in clear handwriting. It explains that the author is held prisoner by a great Skymane on an island in the South Seas and begs whoever discovers the note for rescue.",al={"note contents","bottle note","what is written in the bottle"}},{q="Where does the writer say the island is located?",a="While jungle trees obscure the stars at night, the captive notes that on clear days the Wild Shore can be seen to the northwest, and large sailing vessels appear to the southwest.",al={"island location","how to find the captive","island landmarks"}},{q="What is holding the author captive?",a="The note states that a creature called a great Skymane is holding the author prisoner upon the island.",al={"who captured the author","what holds the author captive","skymane captor"}},{q="Does this lead to further adventures?",a="Finding the sender is the first part of a two-step chain, leading directly into a second part upon locating the captive.",al={"next quest","is there a follow up","what happens after this"}}},kw={"half-buried bottle","message in a bottle","princess poobah","skymane","south seas","stranglethorn vale","wild shore"},rel={"subzone:wild-shore","subzone:south-seas","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Half-Buried Bottle",["end"]="Princess Poobah",level="45",id=594},src={"Message in a Bottle (Classic)"}}
E["quest:595"] = {t="quest",n="The Bloodsail Buccaneers",z="stranglethorn",s="First Mate Crazz of the Blackwater Raiders needs an adventurer to investigate rumors of rival pirates. With his crew busy drinking and chasing company in Booty Bay, he asks you to scout a nearby cove along the Savage Coast for signs of the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",h="First Mate Crazz of the Blackwater Raiders needs an adventurer to investigate rumors of rival pirates.",sec={{t="A Scout along the Savage Coast",b="The Blackwater Raiders have newly docked in Booty Bay, only to hear word that their rivals, the Bloodsail Buccaneers, have been sighted across southern Stranglethorn Vale. With the rest of the crew distracted by grog and shoreline pursuits, First Mate Crazz turns to an outsider for help. He asks you to head north along the Savage Coast and scout a cove to see what the Bloodsail Buccaneers are up to.",sp=0},{t="Signs in the Cove",b="Searching the cove, you find a barrel with some coins and a map covered in hastily scribbled notes lying on top of it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is First Mate Crazz?",a="First Mate Crazz is an officer among the Blackwater Raiders stationed in Booty Bay. Faced with rumors of rival pirates and an unmotivated crew, he hires passing adventurers to scout the coast.",al={"first mate crazz","who gives the quest","who is crazz"}},{q="Why does First Mate Crazz need an outsider?",a="The Blackwater crew just reached port and have only just docked and are far too busy carousing ashore to scout anything themselves.",al={"why hire an adventurer","why cant his crew do it","why help crazz"}},{q="Where does Crazz send you to investigate?",a="He directs you to scout the cove located immediately north of Booty Bay along the stretch known as the Savage Coast.",al={"where do i go","where is the cove","where are the bloodsail"}},{q="What rivalry is troubling the Blackwater Raiders?",a="The Blackwater Raiders are locked in a bitter feud with the Bloodsail Buccaneers, who have recently been spotted spreading throughout southern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who are the rivals","why do they hate bloodsail","bloodsail rivalry"}}},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","correspondence","first mate crazz","savage coast","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:savage-coast","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="First Mate Crazz",["end"]="Bloodsail Correspondence",level="41",id=595},src={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers (Classic)"}}
E["quest:596"] = {t="quest",n="Bloody Bone Necklaces",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp has his own agenda in Stranglethorn Vale beyond assisting Nimboya. He seeks to weaken the rival Bloodscalp tribe by gathering trophies from their warriors.",h="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp has his own agenda in Stranglethorn Vale beyond assisting Nimboya.",sec={{t="Trophies of War",b="Though Kin'weelay arrived in the jungle outpost of Grom'gol Base Camp to help Nimboya, he maintains private purposes of his own. The Bloodscalp trolls dwelling to the north are enemies of the Darkspears. Kin'weelay believes that claiming personal trophies from fallen foes bestows spiritual power over them, asking travelers to hunt Bloodscalp warriors and take the bloody bone necklaces they wear around their necks.",sp=0},{t="Leeching the Spirits",b="Upon receiving the harvested bone adornments, Kin'weelay intends to boil and leech them down until they are reduced to paste. Through this ritual work, he aims to directly wither and weaken the lingering spirits of the Bloodscalp slain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the bone necklaces?",a="Kin'weelay offers the undertaking at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale. Although sent there to aid Nimboya, he uses the encampment to wage his own spiritual vendetta.",al={"quest giver","who gives bloody bone necklaces","kin'weelay quest"}},{q="Why does Kin'weelay want trophies from the Bloodscalp tribe?",a="The Bloodscalps are bitter enemies of the Darkspear tribe. Kin'weelay believes that taking trophies from slain foes grants power over them, allowing the Darkspear to assert dominance over their rivals.",al={"why collect necklaces","bloodscalp necklaces purpose","why hunt bloodscalp"}},{q="Where are the Bloodscalps located?",a="The Bloodscalp trolls dwell in the lands to the north of Grom'gol Base Camp throughout northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where to find bloodscalp","bloodscalp location","where are the trolls"}},{q="What comes next after this hunt?",a="After this hunt, Kin'weelay sends adventurers on to the follow-up, Split Bone Necklace.",al={"next quest","bloody bone necklaces followup","what after bloody bone necklaces"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, hunting the Bloodscalp is about gaining power over an enemy tribe.",["faction:Horde"]="Kin'weelay was sent to Grom'gol Base Camp to aid Nimboya, and uses his time there to hunt the Bloodscalp tribe to the north."},kw={"bloodscalp","darkspear","grom'gol","kin'weelay","necklaces","nimboya","stranglethorn"},rel={"npc:kin-weelay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="37",faction="Horde",id=596},src={"Bloody Bone Necklaces","In-game quest text: Bloody Bone Necklaces"}}
E["quest:597"] = {t="quest",n="The Bloodsail Buccaneers",z="stranglethorn",s="At Booty Bay, the Bloodsail Buccaneers’ plans now point to a camp and an attack signal.",h="At Booty Bay, the Bloodsail Buccaneers’ plans now point to a camp and an attack signal.",sec={{t="A Plot Revealed",b="A map marks the Bloodsail Buccaneers’ intended camp in Booty Bay with a red X. Their orders call for silence. The crew must kill anyone who approaches and wait for a signal from the southern command post before attacking.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to the Harbor",b="You carry the findings back to First Mate Crazz in Booty Bay. He sent you to scout, and the pirates are still waiting for the signal before they attack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written on the Bloodsail correspondence?",a="The recovered Bloodsail Buccaneers correspondence orders the crew to camp quietly at the marked spot, kill anyone who approaches, and wait for a signal from their southern command post before attacking.",al={"bloodsail orders text","what does the note say","bloodsail map details"}},{q="Where does the map point?",a="A red X on the map of Booty Bay marks the pirates’ intended camp.",al={"bloodsail map x","what does the red x mean","where is the camp"}},{q="Who needs to hear about this discovery?",a="First Mate Crazz in Booty Bay needs to hear of the discovery. He sent you to scout the area.",al={"who do i turn this in to","who gets the bloodsail map","first mate crazz report"}},{q="What came before finding this correspondence?",a="First Mate Crazz first sent you from Booty Bay to investigate the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest bloodsail","bloodsail chain start"}}},kw={"bloodsail buccaneers","bloodsail correspondence","booty bay","first mate crazz","southern command post","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Bloodsail Correspondence",["end"]="First Mate Crazz",level="41",id=597},src={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers (2)"}}
E["quest:598"] = {t="quest",n="Split Bone Necklace",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp calls upon Horde allies to hunt the Skullsplitter tribe living to the southeast. Although the Darkspears left Stranglethorn Vale behind, their ancient conflict with these jungle rivals remains unresolved. Returning with twenty-five split bone trophies aids the Darkspears in their war and earns their friendship.",h="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp calls upon Horde allies to hunt the Skullsplitter tribe living to the...",sec={{t="An Unbroken Feud",b="Following the collection of Bloodscalp trophies, Kin'weelay turns his attention toward another longstanding enemy. The Skullsplitter tribe dwells to the southeast of Grom'gol Base Camp, where they have clashed with the Darkspears across many years. Even though the Darkspears no longer reside within the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, they remain bound to this enduring war.",sp=0},{t="Trophies of War",b="To earn the friendship and respect of the Darkspear tribe, an adventurer must march into Skullsplitter territory and claim twenty-five of their distinctive split bone necklaces. Kin'weelay takes pride in seeing these hostile trolls cut down like young saplings by a basilisk, counting every retrieved trophy as a victory for his people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this hunt, and where is he located?",a="Kin'weelay offers the hunt from Grom'gol Base Camp, a Horde outpost on the western coast of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who gives split bone necklace","kinweelay location","quest giver split bone necklace"}},{q="What came before this task?",a="This assignment follows Bloody Bone Necklaces, an earlier hunt wherein Kin'weelay tasked adventurers with collecting trophies from the Bloodscalp tribe.",al={"split bone necklace prerequisite","prior quest to split bone necklace","previous step"}},{q="Why do the Darkspears fight the Skullsplitters if they left Stranglethorn Vale?",a="The Darkspears and Skullsplitters waged war against each other for years in the jungle. Even though the Darkspear tribe has migrated away from Stranglethorn Vale, Kin'weelay explains that they remain bound to the conflict and intend to see their foes regret ever starting it.",al={"why darkspears hate skullsplitters","skullsplitter war lore","darkspear skullsplitter conflict"}},{q="Where can the Skullsplitter tribe be found?",a="The Skullsplitters inhabit territories located to the southeast of Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"skullsplitter location","where are skullsplitters","skullsplitter camps"}},{q="What proof does Kin'weelay demand from the hunt?",a="Kin'weelay requires twenty-five Split Bone Necklaces taken directly from fallen Skullsplitter trolls.",al={"what items needed for kinweelay","split bone necklace item","how many necklaces"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Aiding Kin'weelay in Grom'gol Base Camp in the war against the Skullsplitters earns the friendship of the Darkspears.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, taking trophies from the Skullsplitters carries on a long war that did not end when the tribe left Stranglethorn."},kw={"darkspear","grom'gol base camp","kin'weelay","skullsplitter","split bone necklace","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:596","npc:kin-weelay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:troll","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="42",faction="Horde",id=598},src={"Split Bone Necklace (quest)"}}
E["quest:599"] = {t="quest",n="The Bloodsail Buccaneers",z="stranglethorn",s="First Mate Crazz has learned that the Bloodsail Buccaneers intend to launch an assault against Booty Bay. The scale of the threat demands the attention of the Blackwater Raiders' commander, Fleet Master Seahorn, who needs to hear the warning immediately.",h="First Mate Crazz has learned that the Bloodsail Buccaneers intend to launch an assault against Booty Bay.",sec={{t="A Warning for the Fleet Master",b="Upon discovering that the Bloodsail Buccaneers scheme to strike Booty Bay directly, First Mate Crazz decides it is bigger than he thought. He directs you to seek out Fleet Master Seahorn, who is somewhere in the port town, and inform him of the brewing assault before the rival pirates can make their move.",sp=0},{t="Seahorn's Defiance",b="When presented with the report of the planned strike, Fleet Master Seahorn scoffs at the rival pirates' ambition, declaring an attack on Booty Bay as foolish as leaping from the Overlook Cliffs. Even so, he acknowledges the value of the intelligence and thanks you on behalf of the Blackwater Raiders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to warn Fleet Master Seahorn?",a="First Mate Crazz sends you to warn Seahorn after learning the extent of the Bloodsail Buccaneers' hostile plans against the port.",al={"who starts this quest","first mate crazz quest","bloodsail buccaneers quest giver"}},{q="Where can Fleet Master Seahorn be found?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn is stationed within the pirate haven of Booty Bay in southern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is seahorn","seahorn location","fleet master seahorn town"}},{q="What is the Bloodsail Buccaneers' scheme?",a="The Bloodsail Buccaneers are preparing an outright attack against Booty Bay, challenging the Blackwater Raiders' rule over the town.",al={"what are bloodsail doing","bloodsail attack plan","bloodsail buccaneers plot"}},{q="Which faction controls Booty Bay?",a="Booty Bay is held and operated by the Blackwater Raiders, who fiercely protect the port from their Bloodsail rivals.",al={"who runs booty bay","booty bay pirates faction"}}},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail bucaneers","booty bay","first mate crazz","fleet master seahorn","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","quest:595"},m={start="First Mate Crazz",["end"]="Fleet Master Seahorn",level="41",id=599},src={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers (3)"}}
E["quest:600"] = {t="quest",n="Venture Company Mining",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, the goblin Crank Fizzlebub wants someone to strike at the Venture Company's operations in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Their dig site near Crystalvein Mine continues to produce valuable Singing Blue Crystals from the nearby hills, and Crank asks for ten of those stones brought back to him.",h="In Booty Bay, the goblin Crank Fizzlebub wants someone to strike at the Venture Company's operations in...",sec={{t="Disrupting the Competition",b="Following your earlier collection of Singing Blue Shards, Crank Fizzlebub points toward a larger rival. The Venture Company runs operations across the jungle, cutting into the profits of independent goblins. Though the many basilisks keep the miners from setting foot inside Crystalvein Mine itself, the workers continue digging into the surrounding hillsides to extract Singing Blue Crystals. Crank asks you to take the crystals from these miners and bring them to Booty Bay as proof of their setback.",sp=0},{t="After the Crystals Arrive",b="While Crank frames the request as righteous retribution against a ruthless cartel, his excitement upon seeing the gathered Singing Blue Crystals exposes his real interest. Far from merely wanting the Venture Company humbled, he intends to sell the recovered stones for a substantial fortune in Booty Bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the Venture Company Mining quest?",a="Crank Fizzlebub, a goblin found in Booty Bay, offers the work after you complete Singing Blue Shards.",al={"who starts venture company mining","venture company mining questgiver"}},{q="Where are the miners digging for these crystals?",a="The Venture Company is operating near Crystalvein Mine in the northern region of Stranglethorn Vale, working the hills around the mine.",al={"where is venture company mining","venture company mine location stranglethorn"}},{q="Why aren't the Venture Company miners inside the mine?",a="Crank explains that the many basilisks in Crystalvein Mine keep the miners from venturing inside, forcing them to dig along the perimeter hills instead.",al={"why outside crystalvein mine","crystalvein mine basilisks"}},{q="What does Crank Fizzlebub ask you to bring him?",a="He asks for ten Singing Blue Crystals taken from the Venture Company miners working near Crystalvein Mine.",al={"venture company mining items needed","what items for crank fizzlebub"}},{q="What came before Venture Company Mining?",a="The previous quest in this sequence is Singing Blue Shards, where Crank first has you gather smaller crystal shards in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"venture company mining chain","prerequisite for venture company mining"}}},kw={"booty bay","crank fizzlebub","crystalvein mine","singing blue crystals","stranglethorn vale","venture company"},rel={"quest:605","subzone:crystalvein-mine","topic:venture-company","subzone:booty-bay","topic:goblin","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Crank Fizzlebub",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="41",id=600},src={"Venture Company Mining (Classic)"}}
E["quest:601"] = {t="quest",n="Water Elementals",z="stranglethorn",s="Following discoveries regarding the Stone of the Tides, Baron Revilgaz seeks a way to counteract the artifact's curse. He sends adventurers back to the island to harvest bracers from conjured water elementals so their magical residue can be inspected by experts.",h="Following discoveries regarding the Stone of the Tides, Baron Revilgaz seeks a way to counteract the...",sec={{t="Curbing the Curse",b="Believing the water elementals were summoned by the goblin wizard Gazban, Baron Revilgaz suspects their magical residue holds clues to dealing with the Stone of the Tides. The stone is said to curse anyone who wields it, causing the bearer to drift in and out of reality. To find a countermeasure, Revilgaz directs you back to the island off the coast to gather elemental bracers that might be scrutinized by the scholarly mages of Dalaran.",sp=0},{t="Booty Bay's Master",b="Upon receiving the bracers, Revilgaz admits he lacks the specialized expertise to tell whether any of them will be of use. Rather than travel to Dalaran himself—he will not leave Booty Bay just to chat with tiresome old mages—he sends you north to have a mage look at them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the water elemental bracers?",a="Baron Revilgaz, leader of the Blackwater Raiders in Booty Bay, asks for the bracers to investigate the magic surrounding the Stone of the Tides.",al={"who gives water elementals quest","baron revilgaz quest","who wants bracers"}},{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz need elemental bracers?",a="He hopes that studying the magical residue on the bracers can reveal a method to counteract the curse of the Stone of the Tides, which causes its bearer to fade in and out of existence.",al={"why collect bracers","water elemental bracers purpose","curse of the stone of the tides"}},{q="Who summoned these water elementals?",a="Baron Revilgaz believes they were conjured by Gazban, a goblin wizard said to have found the Stone of the Tides.",al={"who summoned elementals","gazban lore","goblin wizard"}},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="Next comes Magical Analysis: Revilgaz sends the bracers north to Dalaran so a mage can examine their residue.",al={"what is after water elementals","next quest","where do bracers go"}},{q="Why doesn't Revilgaz take the bracers to Dalaran himself?",a="He has no wish to leave Booty Bay just to chat with tiresome old mages, and he insists he has nothing to fear from would-be rivals.",al={"why doesnt revilgaz go","revilgaz dalaran","why stay in booty bay"}}},kw={"booty bay","bracers","curse","dalaran","gazban","revilgaz","stone of the tides","water elemental"},rel={"quest:578","quest:602","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage","topic:goblin","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Baron Revilgaz",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=601},src={"Water Elementals (Classic)"}}
E["quest:602"] = {t="quest",n="Magical Analysis",z="stranglethorn",s="Baron Revilgaz directs you northward from Booty Bay to consult the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. Taking a bag of water elemental bracers, you seek out Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver to decipher the arcane curse tied to the Stone of the Tides.",h="Baron Revilgaz directs you northward from Booty Bay to consult the Kirin Tor in Dalaran.",sec={{t="A Plea to Dalaran",b="Following your hunt for the water elemental bracers, Baron Revilgaz hands over a bundle of their bracers. The goblin leader knows that unraveling the curse behind the Stone of the Tides requires deeper magical expertise than Booty Bay can provide. He directs you north toward the ruins of Dalaran, where the wizards remain deeply engaged in rebuilding their broken kingdom. Convinced that arcane scholars cannot ignore an intriguing puzzle, Revilgaz recommends seeking Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver directly, having had dealings with the knowledgeable wizard in the past.",sp=0},{t="The Archmage's Lore",b="Reaching Ansirem Runeweaver amid Dalaran's ongoing efforts, the busy archmage pauses upon hearing of the relic. Years ago, Runeweaver authored an entire scholarly treatise on the ancient legends of the Gurubashi Empire, giving him rare insight into the relic's past. Examining the bracers, he spots trace magical residue suitable for scrutiny, setting aside his work to uncover what the enchantment holds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Dalaran for this study?",a="Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay gives you the bag of elemental bracers and instructs you to consult the wizards of Dalaran.",al={"who gives magical analysis","magical analysis quest giver","who starts magical analysis"}},{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz pick Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver?",a="Revilgaz has dealt with Runeweaver before and knows the archmage's knowledge is vast; he also trusts that mages cannot resist a magical puzzle.",al={"why ansirem","revilgaz ansirem connection","why ansirem runeweaver"}},{q="What came before this journey to Dalaran?",a="This assignment directly follows Water Elementals, where you gathered water elemental bracers for Baron Revilgaz.",al={"previous quest","prereq magical analysis","what quest leads here"}},{q="What comes next after reaching the archmage?",a="Handing the bracers over leads on to Ansirem's Key.",al={"next quest","what follows magical analysis","after delivering bracers"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Delivering arcane artifacts to an archmage of the Kirin Tor suits mages, since Baron Revilgaz himself says mages can't resist a magical puzzle."},kw={"ansirem runeweaver","baron revilgaz","booty bay","dalaran","gurubashi empire","magical analysis","stone of the tides","water elemental bracers"},rel={"npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:archmage-ansirem-runeweaver","quest:603","subzone:dalaran","zone:stranglethorn","quest:578","topic:mage"},m={start="Baron Revilgaz",["end"]="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=602},src={"Magical Analysis"}}
E["quest:603"] = {t="quest",n="Ansirem's Key",z="stranglethorn",s="Following his magical examination, Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver points toward an ancient troll dagger capable of disrupting the focal altar empowering the Stone of the Tides. He passed it long ago to his daughter Catelyn, a headstrong girl who left home for the pirates of Booty Bay.",h="Following his magical examination, Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver points toward an ancient troll dagger capable...",sec={{t="A Wayward Daughter",b="Ansirem Runeweaver determines that an altar or focal point amplifies the power of the Stone of the Tides. Overpowering that magic calls for another troll relic: an ancient dagger he found while researching in Stranglethorn. He passed it long ago to his daughter Catelyn, a headstrong girl who left home for the pirates of Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="A Fighter Disarmed",b="Reaching Booty Bay reveals that the dagger is no longer at Catelyn's hip. Once celebrated as the settlement's sharpest knife fighter, she suffered defeat in a duel against one of the Bloodsail Buccaneers. Her victor claimed the troll blade as a trophy, leaving her disarmed, humiliated, and bitterly mocked by her fellow cutthroats.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Archmage Ansirem need the troll dagger?",a="The mage holding the Stone of the Tides is channeling its magic through an altar. Ansirem means to disrupt that empowerment by overpowering it, and he knows of an ancient troll dagger that could do it.",al={"why need dagger","ansirem key purpose","what is the dagger for"}},{q="Who is Catelyn?",a="Catelyn is the headstrong daughter of Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver. She left her father behind to run off to Booty Bay and take up life as a pirate.",al={"who is catelyn","ansirem daughter","catelyn the blade"}},{q="Where did Ansirem find the dagger originally?",a="Ansirem uncovered the relic while conducting research in the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale before giving it to his daughter.",al={"dagger origin","where did ansirem find dagger"}},{q="Where can Catelyn be found?",a="She resides down in the pirate haven of Booty Bay at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is catelyn","catelyn location"}}},kw={"ansirem","booty bay","catelyn","dagger","runeweaver","stone of the tides","troll relic"},rel={"npc:archmage-ansirem-runeweaver","quest:602","quest:578","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:pirate","topic:troll"},m={start="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver",["end"]="Catelyn the Blade",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=603},src={"Ansirem's Key"}}
E["quest:604"] = {t="quest",n="The Bloodsail Buccaneers",z="stranglethorn",s="Fleet Master Seahorn trusts a loyal ally of the Blackwater Raiders with striking the Bloodsail Buccaneers' so-called southern command post on the Wild Shore. Recovering their charts and written orders will show exactly what those pirates are up to.",h="Fleet Master Seahorn trusts a loyal ally of the Blackwater Raiders with striking the Bloodsail Buccaneers'...",sec={{t="Raiding the Wild Shore",b="Following earlier efforts for Crazz, Fleet Master Seahorn takes notice of your loyalty to the Blackwater Raiders. The Bloodsail Buccaneers have set up what they call a southern command post on the Wild Shore. Seahorn directs you to raid this encampment, cut down their swashbucklers, and seize their naval charts and written orders so the fleet can learn their intentions.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Fleet's Scheme",b="With the charts and orders in hand, Seahorn learns the Bloodsail plan and concludes that the pirates have anchored close to the cape.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who assigns this raid?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn gives this assignment from Booty Bay after hearing praise about your dedication from Crazz.",al={"who gives the bloodsail buccaneers quest","seahorn quest"}},{q="Where is the Bloodsail command post located?",a="The Buccaneers have set up their southern command camp along the Wild Shore, south of Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"bloodsail southern command post location","where is wild shore"}},{q="What items are needed from the Bloodsail encampment?",a="Seahorn asks for the Bloodsail Charts and their written Bloodsail Orders to decipher what the rival buccaneers intend to do.",al={"what documents does seahorn want","bloodsail orders and charts"}},{q="Why does Fleet Master Seahorn want their charts and orders?",a="Seahorn wants to see exactly what the Bloodsail Buccaneers are up to.",al={"why raid wild shore","what does seahorn want to know"}}},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail buccaneers","bloodsail charts","bloodsail orders","booty bay","fleet master seahorn","wild shore"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:wild-shore","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","quest:595"},m={start="Fleet Master Seahorn",["end"]="Fleet Master Seahorn",level="42",id=604},src={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers (4)"}}
E["quest:605"] = {t="quest",n="Singing Blue Shards",z="stranglethorn",s="Crank Fizzlebub seeks an enterprising adventurer to gather Singing Crystal Shards from the basilisks of Stranglethorn Vale. Competition with the Venture Company prevents him from harvesting the mineral deposits directly, leaving basilisk hides as the next best option. He promises a cut of the profits to anyone willing to bring him ten decent specimens.",h="Crank Fizzlebub seeks an enterprising adventurer to gather Singing Crystal Shards from the basilisks of...",sec={{t="A Lucrative Opportunity",b="Crank Fizzlebub has identified an eager market for the Singing Crystals unique to Stranglethorn Vale. Unfortunately for his business ambitions, the aggressive presence of the Venture Company makes it hard for him to gather raw crystal in the field. To circumvent his rivals, Fizzlebub turns to an alternative method: basilisks consume the crystals, incorporating the mineral into their hardened hides, which allows usable shards to be retrieved from them instead.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Coast",b="While any basilisk in the jungle might yield acceptable crystal fragments, Fizzlebub says the gentler ones are found along the shores south of Zul'Kunda, up north. Gathering ten shards allows him to move forward with his buyers, after which his business concerns shift toward the operations of the Venture Company itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Crank Fizzlebub want Singing Crystal Shards?",a="Singing Crystals are unique to Stranglethorn Vale and hold great value for select buyers. Crank Fizzlebub says he can move them, and promises a cut of the profits.",al={"why singing crystals","crank fizzlebub purpose","what are singing crystals for"}},{q="Why cannot Crank Fizzlebub harvest the crystals directly?",a="Fizzlebub blames the Venture Company for making it hard for an honest trader like him to gather the raw crystals himself.",al={"why kill basilisks","venture company problem","why not mine crystals"}},{q="Why do basilisks have these crystals?",a="The basilisks of Stranglethorn Vale feed on the crystals, which gradually integrate into their hides and give them their hardened, rocky skin.",al={"basilisk crystal lore","why do basilisks drop crystals"}},{q="Where does Crank Fizzlebub suggest looking for basilisks?",a="Fizzlebub says any basilisk can yield shards, but the gentler ones live along the shores south of Zul'Kunda, up north.",al={"where to find shards","basilisk location","zul kunda basilisks"}},{q="What happens after turning in the shards?",a="Upon receiving ten shards, Fizzlebub pays out your promised cut of the profits and directs his attention directly toward the operations of the Venture Company.",al={"what next after singing blue shards","singing blue shards follow up"},sp=1}},kw={"basilisks","crank fizzlebub","singing blue shards","singing crystals","stranglethorn vale","venture company","zul'kunda"},rel={"topic:venture-company","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Crank Fizzlebub",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="35",id=605},src={"Singing Blue Shards","In-game quest text: Singing Blue Shards"}}
E["quest:606"] = {t="quest",n="Scaring Shaky",z="stranglethorn",s="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley can't stand unpaid gambling debts, and plenty of people owe him. First is \"Shaky\" Phillipe by the docks in Booty Bay, who still owes a good deal from last week's game. MacKinley's plan is a scare, using giblets from Elder Mistvale Gorillas.",h="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley can't stand unpaid gambling debts, and plenty of people owe him.",sec={{t="Collecting a Debt",b="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley cannot abide gambling debts left unpaid, and many people owe. First among them is \"Shaky\" Phillipe, who is by the docks and whose debt from last week's game is large. The way to collect is to frighten Phillipe. You are sent out of town to hunt Elder Mistvale Gorillas and bring back a good haul of giblets for Phillipe. MacKinley wants it kept quiet that they came from an animal, so that Phillipe imagines the worst.",sp=0},{t="Phillipe's Reaction",b="Phillipe recoils at the giblets and does not want to know where they came from. Then Phillipe asks whether Sea Wolf sent you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley?",a="MacKinley is owed gambling debts by many people and wants help collecting them, starting with \"Shaky\" Phillipe.",al={"who is mackinley","sea wolf mackinley","who gives scaring shaky"}},{q="Why does MacKinley want to scare \"Shaky\" Phillipe?",a="Phillipe still owes MacKinley a large sum from last week's game, and MacKinley thinks a fright is the way to get paid.",al={"why scare shaky","shaky phillipe debt","why target phillipe"}},{q="What creatures provide the giblets?",a="Elder Mistvale Gorillas, which MacKinley says are found outside town.",al={"where do giblets come from","mistvale giblets source","what do i kill for giblets"}},{q="Where can \"Shaky\" Phillipe be found?",a="Down by the docks in Booty Bay.",al={"where is shaky phillipe","shaky location","find shaky phillipe"}},{q="What should you tell Phillipe about the giblets?",a="Nothing. MacKinley wants Phillipe to imagine the worst, so the giblets' animal origin is not to be mentioned.",al={"do i tell shaky where giblets came from"}}},kw={"booty bay","gambling debt","mistvale giblets","mistvale gorillas","scaring shaky","sea wolf mackinley","shaky phillipe","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:607","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",["end"]="\"Shaky\" Phillipe",level="41",id=606},src={"Classic quest text: Scaring Shaky"}}
E["quest:607"] = {t="quest",n="Return to MacKinley",z="stranglethorn",s="After the scare of the giblets, \"Shaky\" Phillipe hands you a pouch to carry to \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley. Phillipe swears the debt was always meant to be paid and adds that there is no need to get rough.",h="After the scare of the giblets, \"Shaky\" Phillipe hands you a pouch to carry to \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley.",sec={{t="Shaky's Plea",b="Phillipe presses a pouch of payment on you for Sea Wolf. Phillipe wants MacKinley told that the debt was always meant to be repaid, and swears to it. Phillipe puts it down to getting a little drunk and losing the way, and says MacKinley will understand and that there is no need to get rough.",sp=0},{t="Sea Wolf Hears the Tale",b="MacKinley chuckles and asks how hard Phillipe shook when shown the giblets. MacKinley adds that Phillipe is so easy to read that, playing cards against Phillipe, winning comes without effort.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives you the pouch?",a="\"Shaky\" Phillipe gives you the pouch of payment for Sea Wolf MacKinley.",al={"who gives return to mackinley","where do i start return to mackinley"}},{q="What excuse does Phillipe give for not paying?",a="Phillipe puts it down to getting a little drunk and losing the way, and swears the debt was always going to be repaid.",al={"why didn't shaky pay","phillipe excuse","why was shaky phillipe late"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="This follows Scaring Shaky, where MacKinley had you frighten Phillipe with giblets.",al={"what comes before return to mackinley","previous quest"}}},kw={"debt","mackinley","sea wolf","shaky phillipe","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:606","quest:609","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="\"Shaky\" Phillipe",["end"]="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",level="41",id=607},src={"Classic quest text: Return to MacKinley"}}
E["quest:608"] = {t="quest",n="The Bloodsail Buccaneers",z="stranglethorn",s="In Stranglethorn, the Bloodsail Buccaneers gather strength for an attack. Fleet Master Seahorn will not risk his whole fleet in a counterstrike, so he sends a small crew against their leaders before they can begin.",h="In Stranglethorn, the Bloodsail Buccaneers gather strength for an attack.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Pirate Fleet",b="Fleet Master Seahorn means to halt the Bloodsail attack before it gains strength. He mocks Fleet Master Firallon's skill at sea, then chooses to strike at the commanders. Seahorn will not risk a full naval battle. Instead, he sends a small crew to Firallon's landing camp to kill Firallon, Captain Stillwater, and Captain Keelhaul. Without their leaders, the buccaneers will be left without command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the strike on the Bloodsail leadership?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay orders the strike. He hopes to break the hostile fleet before it can attack.",al={"who gives the bloodsail buccaneers quest","bloodsail buccaneers questgiver","who sends you after firallon"}},{q="Which buccaneer commanders need to be eliminated?",a="The targets are Fleet Master Firallon, Captain Stillwater, and Captain Keelhaul, leaders of the Bloodsail forces.",al={"targets for bloodsail buccaneers","bloodsail commanders to kill","who are the bloodsail bosses"}},{q="Why does Fleet Master Seahorn send adventurers instead of his ships?",a="Seahorn believes a capable crew can strike the landing camp and kill the enemy officers. That could bring down the fleet without risking his ships.",al={"why send adventurers to firallon","why not send the blackwater fleet","seahorn plan"}},{q="Where does this clash fit in the broader confrontation with the Bloodsail Buccaneers?",a="The clash follows the discovery of the buccaneers' written attack plans during the earlier stages of the Bloodsail investigation in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"previous bloodsail quest","what quest comes before this","bloodsail chain order"}}},kw={"blackwater","bloodsail","booty bay","firallon","keelhaul","pirates","seahorn","stillwater"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","quest:595"},m={start="Fleet Master Seahorn",["end"]="Fleet Master Seahorn",level="42",id=608},src={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers (5)"}}
E["quest:609"] = {t="quest",n="Voodoo Dues",z="stranglethorn",s="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay needs to balance his books by collecting outstanding debts from three old associates. Though rumors claim the men were cursed and bewitched into wandering ancient jungle ruins, MacKinley expects their prized possessions retrieved regardless of their grim fate.",h="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay needs to balance his books by collecting outstanding debts from three old...",sec={{t="Unpaid Accounts",b="Following your earlier collection efforts for \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley, the pirate still holds an active ledger of unsettled debts. Three particular debtors—Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins, Jon-Jon the Crow, and Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\"—have let their accounts sit delinquent for months. MacKinley initially assumed the trio merely skipped out of Booty Bay to avoid paying, but he later heard they met a stranger and darker fate deep in the jungle.",sp=0},{t="Bewitched in the Ruins",b="Whispers say the three debtors were bewitched and cursed, leaving them to wander the ancient stonework northeast of Booty Bay at the Ruins of Aboraz and the Ruins of Jubuwal. Unconcerned with their misfortune, MacKinley directs you to venture into the ruins, track down each man, and seize their notable valuables: Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass, Chucky's Huge Ring, and Maury's Clubbed Foot.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking to collect these debts?",a="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley makes this request from his post in Booty Bay. He is working his way down a list of debtors who owe him money and refuses to let their debts slip away.",al={"who gives voodoo dues","sea wolf mackinley quest"}},{q="Who are the three debtors?",a="The debtors are Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins, Jon-Jon the Crow, and Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\". Their payments have been outstanding for several months.",al={"who owes mackinley","voodoo dues targets"}},{q="Where can the three debtors be found?",a="They wander the ancient stone structures northeast of Booty Bay, specifically within the Ruins of Aboraz and the Ruins of Jubuwal.",al={"where are the debtors","where are aboraz and jubuwal"}},{q="What happened to the three men?",a="According to word that reached MacKinley, the three were bewitched and cursed, and now roam the jungle ruins instead of returning to port.",al={"why are they cursed","what is wrong with them"}},{q="What specific items must be recovered?",a="MacKinley requires three specific valuables: Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass, Chucky's Huge Ring, and Maury's Clubbed Foot.",al={"what items does mackinley want","voodoo dues items"}},{q="What came before this task in the chain?",a="This follows the earlier jobs of Scaring Shaky and Return to MacKinley, as you assist the pirate with his collection list.",al={"voodoo dues prerequisites","previous quest"}}},kw={"booty bay","chucky ten thumbs","jon-jon the crow","maury club foot wilkins","ruins of aboraz","ruins of jubuwal","sea wolf mackinley","stranglethorn vale","voodoo dues"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:ruins-of-aboraz","subzone:ruins-of-jubuwal","quest:613","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",["end"]="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",level="44",faction="Neutral",id=609},src={"Voodoo Dues"}}
E["quest:610"] = {t="quest",n="\"Pretty Boy\" Duncan",z="stranglethorn",s="After tracking down Catelyn the Blade on behalf of her father, an adventurer learns that her weapon is no longer in her hands. She demands that her lost dagger be retrieved from a pirate named Pretty Boy Duncan before she cooperates further.",h="After tracking down Catelyn the Blade on behalf of her father, an adventurer learns that her weapon is no...",sec={{t="A Pirate's Grievance",b="Following the trail from Ansirem's Key leads directly to Catelyn the Blade, who ran away from a quiet life of scholarship and dusty tomes alongside mages. She cannot hand over her dagger at her father's request, since she no longer has it. If anyone hopes to secure her blade, they will first have to deal with the Bloodsail Buccaneer who took it.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Steel",b="Catelyn suffered an uncharacteristic defeat at the hands of Pretty Boy Duncan, who struck her unconscious and made off with her signature weapon. As a fighter who relies on her personal knife, she insists on recovering that exact weapon from the buccaneer before anything else can move forward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pretty Boy Duncan?",a="Pretty Boy Duncan is a member of the Bloodsail Buccaneers operating near Booty Bay. He beat Catelyn the Blade in a fight, knocked her out cold, and took her dagger.",al={"pretty boy duncan","who is duncan","duncan pirate"}},{q="Why does Catelyn want her dagger back?",a="Catelyn relies on her knife in combat and refuses to settle for another. After losing it to Duncan in a knife fight, she wants the blade back before aiding anyone who comes looking for her.",al={"catelyn dagger","catelyn knife","why get blade back"}},{q="Why did Catelyn run away from home?",a="Catelyn abandoned her family to escape a dull existence spent reading old books and keeping company with rigid, aged mages; she refused to live that boring life.",al={"why catelyn ran away","ansirem daughter","catelyn backstory"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the search?",a="This confrontation follows the recovery of Ansirem's Key and precedes the unraveling of The Curse of the Tides.",al={"quest chain","what leads to pretty boy duncan"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Catelyn explicitly mocks scholars of the arcane, claiming she fled home precisely to avoid spending her days surrounded by stuffy, grey-haired spellcasters."},kw={"bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","catelyn the blade","catelyn's blade","pretty boy duncan","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:603","quest:611","quest:578","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:mage"},m={start="Catelyn the Blade",["end"]="Catelyn the Blade",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=610},src={"\"Pretty Boy\" Duncan (quest)"}}
E["quest:611"] = {t="quest",n="The Curse of the Tides",z="stranglethorn",s="With her knife recovered from Pretty Boy Duncan, Catelyn the Blade loans the troll artifact so it can be used against a sunken altar off the coast. Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay wants the Stone of the Tides for his collection of ancient troll artifacts.",h="With her knife recovered from Pretty Boy Duncan, Catelyn the Blade loans the troll artifact so it can be used...",sec={{t="The Sunken Altar",b="Catelyn the Blade lends her recovered troll dagger to break an altar submerged deep beneath the waves. Though no expert on troll ruins like her father, she has heard of a sunken troll city, and she points toward it, out near the reef northwest of Grom'gol Base Camp. Within the underwater ruins of the Vile Reef, the Altar of the Tides rests, surrounded by a distinct blue glow amid sea life and murlocs.",sp=0},{t="The Trapped Mage",b="Striking the Altar of the Tides with Catelyn's blade shatters its magic and draws forth Gazban, a goblin mage who carries the Stone of the Tides and takes the form of a water elemental when challenged. Once he is overcome, the stone can be carried alongside the loaned dagger back to Booty Bay, where Baron Revilgaz prepares a special display stand to showcase the relic's captured oceanic magic among his prized collection.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Altar of the Tides located?",a="The altar rests deep under the sea in the Vile Reef, a sunken ruin situated off the coast northwest of Grom'gol Base Camp. It radiates a noticeable blue glow beneath the water.",al={"where is the altar","altar of the tides location","where do i find the altar"}},{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz want the stone?",a="Baron Revilgaz is an avid collector of ancient troll antiquities and has cleared space and bought a fine stand specifically to show off the relic.",al={"revilgaz stone","why revilgaz wants the stone","what does revilgaz do with it"}},{q="Why does Catelyn lend her blade?",a="After having her special knife recovered from Duncan, Catelyn lends the troll relic to shatter the altar, demanding its safe return once the deed is finished.",al={"catelyn knife","why lend knife","catelyn blade"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers finish Baron Revilgaz's search for the ancient relic, venturing into waters close to the Horde encampment at Grom'gol Base Camp."},kw={"altar of the tides","baron revilgaz","booty bay","catelyn the blade","gazban","stone of the tides","stranglethorn vale","vile reef"},rel={"quest:578","subzone:vile-reef","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin","topic:alliance"},m={start="Catelyn the Blade",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=611},src={"The Curse of the Tides"}}
E["quest:613"] = {t="quest",n="Cracking Maury's Foot",z="stranglethorn",s="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley has retrieved the foot of his late debtor Maury, only to find that what he is owed is locked inside it. To claim what is owed, he directs travelers to the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound in Stranglethorn Vale to search for the missing key.",h="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley has retrieved the foot of his late debtor Maury, only to find that what he is owed is...",sec={{t="A Locked Prize",b="Following the retrieval of Maury's foot in Voodoo Dues, \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley faces an unexpected complication in Booty Bay. The late debtor put a lock on his foot, and the valuables he owes are sealed inside.",sp=0},{t="The Ogres' Mound",b="Maury liked to gamble with the ogres of the Mosh'Ogg mound, off to the northeast. MacKinley remembers Maury saying the ogres drove him away once he had won too much, so he suspects they now hold the key and sends travelers to look for it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley need Maury's key?",a="Maury sealed what he owed inside his own foot and put a lock on it. MacKinley cannot access the debt owed to him without the key to unlock it.",al={"why need key","what is the key for","maury key purpose"}},{q="Where is Maury's key thought to be?",a="MacKinley suspects the key may be held by the Mosh'Ogg ogres at their mound located to the northeast of Booty Bay.",al={"where is key","key location","where to find maury key"}},{q="Why would the Mosh'Ogg ogres have the key?",a="Maury often gambled with the Mosh'Ogg ogres, and MacKinley recalls the ogres driving him off after a big win. That is why he guesses they may be holding the key.",al={"why ogres have key","maury ogres connection","did maury know the ogres"}},{q="What comes before this in MacKinley's business?",a="This follows the collection in Voodoo Dues, which came after Scaring Shaky and Return to MacKinley in the debt-settling efforts around Booty Bay.",al={"previous quest","chain order","what comes first"}}},kw={"booty bay","key","mackinley","maury","mosh'ogg","ogres","sea wolf","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","quest:609","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",["end"]="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley",level="44",id=613},src={"Cracking Maury's Foot"}}
E["quest:616"] = {t="quest",n="The Haunted Isle",z="stranglethorn",s="Krazek keeps his ears open for unusual rumors throughout Booty Bay on behalf of Baron Revilgaz. A tale shared by tavern sailors speaks of a haunted island off the coast, inhabited by water elementals and the ghost of a raving goblin. Delivering this rumor to Revilgaz piques the baron's interest in an ancient troll legend.",h="Krazek keeps his ears open for unusual rumors throughout Booty Bay on behalf of Baron Revilgaz.",sec={{t="Tavern Tales in Booty Bay",b="In the bustling port of Booty Bay, Krazek gathers word of anything unusual happening throughout Stranglethorn Vale at the request of Baron Revilgaz. While Krazek normally pays little heed to spectral gossip, stories told by sailors drinking in the local tavern caught his attention. They speak of an offshore isle occupied by water elementals and haunted by a raving goblin ghost, so he asks you to relay the story to the baron.",sp=0},{t="A Troll Legend",b="Upon hearing Krazek's report of the haunted isle, Baron Revilgaz recalls an old troll legend he once read about in a book. The presence of water elementals and the goblin apparition leads the baron to suspect that an ancient relic, the Stone of the Tides, might finally be within his grasp to add to his personal collection of artifacts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Baron Revilgaz?",a="Krazek asks you to deliver the rumor to Baron Revilgaz after overhearing an unsettling tale from local sailors in the Booty Bay tavern.",al={"who gives the haunted isle","haunted isle quest giver","krazek rumor"}},{q="What rumors did the sailors share?",a="The sailors reported an island off the coast that is overrun with water elementals and haunted by the ghost of a raving goblin.",al={"what is on the island","haunted island rumor","sailor stories"}},{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz care about a ghost story?",a="The baron remembers a troll legend recorded in an old book. The bizarre accounts from the island suggest that an ancient relic called the Stone of the Tides might actually be located there.",al={"why revilgaz wants to know","revilgaz reaction","stone of the tides interest"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Baron Revilgaz directs your attention toward the ancient relic itself, continuing the pursuit in the next step, The Stone of the Tides.",al={"what quest is next","haunted isle follow up","next step after haunted isle"}}},kw={"baron revilgaz","booty bay","goblin ghost","krazek","stone of the tides","stranglethorn vale","troll legend","water elementals"},rel={"quest:578","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin","topic:troll"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=616},src={"The Haunted Isle"}}
E["quest:617"] = {t="quest",n="Akiris by the Bundle",z="stranglethorn",s="Privateer Bloads in Booty Bay is looking to acquire bundles of valuable akiris reeds for an associate named Groy. The plants have to be taken from the naga, who were last spotted on the northern beach.",h="Privateer Bloads in Booty Bay is looking to acquire bundles of valuable akiris reeds for an associate named...",sec={{t="A Profitable Ocean Plant",b="Privateer Bloads offers work in Booty Bay for anyone willing to tackle a seaside venture. An associate named Groy pays handsomely for bundles of akiris reed, a reed that grows by the sea and that the naga call by that name. Bloads does not know why Groy wants them, only that ten stalks are needed and that the naga were last spotted on the northern beach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Privateer Bloads?",a="Privateer Bloads is a privateer in Booty Bay who has work for those who ask.",al={"bloads","who gives akiris by the bundle","who is bloads"}},{q="What is an akiris reed?",a="Akiris reed is what the naga call a valuable ocean reed. While its exact purpose remains unknown to Privateer Bloads, collectors pay well for bundles of the stalks.",al={"akiris reed","what are akiris reeds","what is akiris used for"}},{q="Where can the naga holding the reeds be found?",a="The naga possessing the stalks prowl the coastline north of Booty Bay along the beaches of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where are the naga","where to get akiris reed","akiris reed location"}},{q="Who buys the reeds from Privateer Bloads?",a="Bloads secures the bundles on behalf of an associate named Groy, who earns a substantial profit selling the harvested ocean reeds.",al={"who is groy","who wants akiris reed","bloads buyer"}}},kw={"akiris reed","booty bay","groy","naga","privateer bloads","reeds","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","topic:naga","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Privateer Bloads",["end"]="Privateer Bloads",level="43",id=617},src={"Akiris by the Bundle (Classic)"}}
E["quest:618"] = {t="quest",n="Facing Negolash",z="stranglethorn",s="Following the trail of Captain Hecklebury Smotts' lost weapon, Sprogger reveals a plan to bait the giant Negolash using the creature's favorite delicacies. By staging a banquet in a wrecked lifeboat on the coast of Stranglethorn Vale, adventurers can confront the brute and reclaim the captain's stolen cutlass.",h="Following the trail of Captain Hecklebury Smotts' lost weapon, Sprogger reveals a plan to bait the giant...",sec={{t="A Hungry Giant",b="When giants smashed Captain Smotts' vessel, one brute named Negolash headed straight for the galley. Unlike his brethren, he wasn't hungry for the crew. Sprogger saw that Negolash wanted wine and Barbecued Buzzard Wings, Sprogger's own specialty, whose recipe he had to travel to the Badlands to get.",sp=0},{t="The Trap in the Lifeboat",b="To lure the giant, Sprogger devises an irresistible feast. Adventurers must haul ten helpings of the wings alongside five bottles of wine into the captain's ruined lifeboat down the southeastern shoreline. Drawn by the smell of the banquet, Negolash can be cornered, slain, and stripped of the captain's prize blade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Negolash?",a="Negolash is a hungry giant who helped wreck Captain Smotts' ship. Instead of hunting the sailors, he ransacked the vessel's galley for food and drink.",al={"what is negolash","who is the giant","negolash lore"}},{q="Why does Sprogger know how to lure Negolash?",a="Sprogger witnessed the giant raid his kitchen during the shipwreck. Negolash showed an obsession with Sprogger's Barbecued Buzzard Wings and bottles of Junglevine Wine, making those exact provisions the ideal bait.",al={"how to bait negolash","why buzzard wings","negolash food"}},{q="Where does the confrontation take place?",a="The banquet must be placed in Captain Smotts' old ruined lifeboat, which sits stranded along the coast southeast of Sprogger's position.",al={"where is negolash","where to place the food","lifeboat location"}},{q="What came before this task?",a="This confrontation is the conclusion of a trail that begins with The Monogrammed Sash and continues through The Captain's Cutlass.",al={"what quest comes first","facing negolash previous quest","prereqs for negolash"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The entire plan relies on Sprogger's culinary craft, specifically a specialized recipe for Barbecued Buzzard Wings that he traveled all the way to the Badlands to learn."},kw={"badlands","buzzard wings","captain smotts","junglevine wine","negolash","smotts' cutlass","sprogger","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:8553","quest:619","quest:8552","zone:stranglethorn","zone:badlands"},m={start="Sprogger",["end"]="Captain Hecklebury Smotts",level="42",faction="Both",id=618},src={"Facing Negolash"}}
E["quest:619"] = {t="quest",n="Enticing Negolash",z="stranglethorn",s="Along the shores of Stranglethorn Vale rests an abandoned lifeboat marked with the faded words Smotts' Revenge. Piling barbecued buzzard wings and junglevine wine upon the wrecked craft serves to lure out the giant Negolash.",h="Along the shores of Stranglethorn Vale rests an abandoned lifeboat marked with the faded words Smotts'...",sec={{t="A Tempting Offering",b="The wreckage of a small boat lies neglected, carrying only weathered lettering that names it Smotts' Revenge. To catch the attention of Negolash during the hunt against him, the boat must be turned into bait, heaped with ten barbecued buzzard wings and five bottles of junglevine wine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ruined Lifeboat?",a="It is an abandoned, broken boat bearing the faded inscription Smotts' Revenge, used as a platform to arrange food and drink to lure Negolash.",al={"smotts revenge boat","lifeboat strangletorn","what is smotts revenge"}},{q="What provisions are required for the offering?",a="The offering requires ten barbecued buzzard wings alongside five vessels of junglevine wine, which are stacked together directly onto the wreck.",al={"what food is needed","enticing negolash items","what items for negolash"}},{q="When does this task become available?",a="This offering can only be prepared while undertaking the hunt to face Negolash.",al={"when can i do enticing negolash","facing negolash prerequisite","how to unlock enticing negolash"}}},kw={"barbecued buzzard wing","junglevine wine","negolash","ruined lifeboat","smotts revenge","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:618","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Ruined Lifeboat",["end"]="Ruined Lifeboat",level="42",faction="Neutral",id=619},src={"Enticing Negolash"}}
E["quest:621"] = {t="quest",n="Zanzil's Secret",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, the goblin Crank Fizzlebub has set his sights on the potent concoction brewed by the exiled troll Zanzil. Zanzil uses this botanical blend to dominate the minds and empower the bodies of his followers among the nearby jungle ruins. Believing such a substance holds immense value for anyone seeking to control others, Fizzlebub wants samples retrieved for his own uses.",h="In Booty Bay, the goblin Crank Fizzlebub has set his sights on the potent concoction brewed by the exiled...",sec={{t="Mind-Bending Draughts",b="Northeast of Booty Bay, the outcast troll known as Zanzil has made a haven in the ruins of Jubuwal and Aboraz. Cast out by his former tribal leaders because they feared his mastery over the minds of others, Zanzil commands a band of followers entirely through concoctions derived from jungle vegetation. These mixtures deaden their will while enhancing their physical might, turning them into docile yet sturdy thralls.",sp=0},{t="A Lucrative Mixture",b="Crank Fizzlebub sees clear opportunity in the exile's craft. Anyone desiring dominance over others would pay handsomely for such an elixir, prompting the goblin to seek a supply directly from the ruins. Delivering enough samples secures not only standard coin but a quiet bonus, provided the carrier keeps quiet about the transaction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zanzil the Outcast?",a="Zanzil is a troll exile who dwells in the ruins northeast of Booty Bay. His own leaders banished him because they feared his hold over other people's minds.",al={"who is zanzil","zanzil lore","why was zanzil exiled"}},{q="What does Zanzil's mixture actually do?",a="Brewed from native jungle plants, the concoction breaks and suppresses the free will of whoever drinks it while unnaturally bolstering their physical strength.",al={"what is zanzils mixture","effects of zanzils mixture","zanzil potion effects"}},{q="Where does Zanzil reside?",a="Zanzil and his followers dwell in the ruins of Jubuwal and Aboraz, situated northeast of Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"zanzil location","where is zanzil","where are the ruins"}},{q="Why does Crank Fizzlebub want the mixture?",a="Crank Fizzlebub believes the mixture would fetch a high price among those who want to control others, and he intends to find a use for it.",al={"why does crank want the mixture","what will crank do with zanzils mixture"}},{q="Why did Crank pay extra upon delivery?",a="Crank provides a bonus sum explicitly to buy discretion, ensuring that the acquisition of the mind-controlling brew remains a private business affair.",al={"crank fizzlebub extra pay","discretion pay crank"},sp=1}},kw={"aboraz","booty bay","fizzlebub","jubuwal","mixture","stranglethorn","zanzil"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Crank Fizzlebub",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="44",faction="Neutral",id=621},src={"Zanzil's Secret (Classic)"}}
E["quest:622"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Corporal Kaleb",z="stranglethorn",s="Krazek has mended the pot and added a second steam whistle, plus a new chopper in the base made to cut through leg bones. The pot now has to go back to Corporal Kaleb at the Rebel Camp.",h="Krazek has mended the pot and added a second steam whistle, plus a new chopper in the base made to cut...",sec={{t="A Better Pot",b="Krazek has finished with the pot you brought in. It now has one more steam whistle and a new chopper set into the bottom, able to cut through leg bones. Krazek calls it a guaranteed cook-pleaser and expects the owner to be happy with it. It must go back to Corporal Kaleb at the Rebel Camp.",sp=0},{t="Back at the Camp",b="Kaleb is delighted to see the pot working, because dinner can finally get started. Kaleb then hopes your time in Booty Bay went well, calling it a rough town, and passes along a rumor that goblins sometimes drag drunken sailors off to slave boats headed for parts unknown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Corporal Kaleb?",a="Corporal Kaleb is at the Rebel Camp, awaiting a cooking pot that Krazek in Booty Bay has been fixing.",al={"corporal kaleb","who is kaleb","kaleb rebel camp","where is corporal kaleb","kaleb location"}},{q="What did Krazek do to the pot?",a="Krazek repaired it, then fitted a second steam whistle and a fresh chopper in the base that slices through leg bones.",al={"krazek pot upgrades","what did krazek fix","krazek crock pot"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="Favor for Krazek came first.",al={"previous quest","what led to return to corporal kaleb"}}},kw={"booty bay","corporal kaleb","crock pot","krazek","rebel camp","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:627","subzone:rebel-camp","subzone:booty-bay","topic:goblin","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Corporal Kaleb",level="37",id=622},src={"Classic quest text: Return to Corporal Kaleb"}}
E["quest:623"] = {t="quest",n="Akiris by the Bundle",z="stranglethorn",s="Privateer Bloads in Stranglethorn Vale needs a fresh bundle of akiris reeds transported across the sea to Dustwallow Marsh. A contact named Privateer Groy has a client in Theramore Isle who wants more right away, and Bloads himself will not be heading there for a week.",h="Privateer Bloads in Stranglethorn Vale needs a fresh bundle of akiris reeds transported across the sea to...",sec={{t="A Crossing to Theramore",b="Word has arrived from across the sea while you were away. Privateer Groy in Theramore Isle sent word to Privateer Bloads expressing satisfaction with the prior shipment of akiris reeds, noting that an interested client demands more immediately. With Bloads not scheduled to sail for Dustwallow Marsh for another week, he entrusts you with the packaged parcel of reeds to deliver by hand.",sp=0},{t="Delivery on the Docks",b="Privateer Groy waits along the docks of Theramore. Though dismissive of strangers at first, Groy inspects the bundle carefully upon learning that Bloads arranged the delivery. Pleased with the quality of the reeds, he pays a cut of coin for the courier work and promptly warns travelers not to loiter around his docks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Privateer Groy?",a="Privateer Groy is a contact of Privateer Bloads in Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh, who has a client wanting more akiris reeds.",al={"who is groy","groy theramore","privateer groy"}},{q="Why does Privateer Bloads need a courier?",a="Bloads received word that Groy has an urgent buyer waiting for another bundle of akiris reeds. Since Bloads is not scheduled to sail to Dustwallow Marsh for another week, he relies on a traveler to make the journey immediately.",al={"why carry reeds","why theramore","bloads delivery"}},{q="Where does this shipment need to go?",a="The bundle must be carried across the sea to Theramore Isle, an Alliance port located within Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where do i take the reeds","akiris delivery location","dustwallow marsh delivery"}},{q="What came before this journey?",a="This delivery follows the initial harvesting effort in Stranglethorn Vale, where bundles of akiris reeds were first gathered and brought to Privateer Bloads.",al={"previous quest","akiris reed chain","prerequisite"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore Isle is an Alliance stronghold in Dustwallow Marsh, though Privateer Bloads warns that visitors can still find trouble if they are the wrong kind of crowd."},kw={"akiris","bloads","dustwallow","groy","privateer","reeds","stranglethorn","theramore"},rel={"quest:617","zone:dustwallow","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Privateer Bloads",["end"]="Privateer Groy",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=623},src={"Akiris by the Bundle (2)"}}
E["quest:624"] = {t="quest",n="Cortello's Riddle",z="stranglethorn",s="A hidden parchment found aboard the Bloodsail Buccaneer vessels along the Wild Shore presents Cortello's cryptic verse. Deciphering the poem points travelers toward a clue waiting beneath an ornate bridge.",h="A hidden parchment found aboard the Bloodsail Buccaneer vessels along the Wild Shore presents Cortello's...",sec={{t="A Buccaneer's Riddle",b="Scattered notes aboard the Bloodsail fleet anchored off the southern coast of Stranglethorn Vale carry a rhyme. Cortello's verse describes a finely worked, much-used bridge that lies east of Deadwind and south of Redridge. Anyone seeking to unravel the mystery must follow these poetic directions out of the jungle and into the marshes to find what waits underneath.",sp=0},{t="The Marsh Crossing",b="Following the verse leads to the murky waters beneath an ornate bridge spanning the Swamp of Sorrows. Resting under the bridge lies a soggy parchment, waiting to reveal the next step in Cortello's puzzle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this mystery begin?",a="The riddle begins with a scrap of parchment found around the Bloodsail Buccaneers' fleet at anchor off the Wild Shore, south of Booty Bay.",al={"where to start cortello's riddle","cortellos riddle start location","where is cortello's riddle found"}},{q="What location is described in the riddle?",a="The rhyme points to a well-traveled, ornate bridge located in the Swamp of Sorrows, situated east of Deadwind Pass and south of the Redridge Mountains.",al={"what bridge is in cortellos riddle","where is the riddle pointing","bridge east of deadwind south of redridge"}},{q="What are you searching for beneath the bridge?",a="The riddle says something waits underneath the bridge, a hint or a clue that lies there for endless tomorrows.",al={"what do you find in swamp of sorrows","cortello clue under bridge","what is under the bridge"}},{q="Who wrote the riddle?",a="The riddle goes by Cortello's name, though the parchment says nothing more about who he was.",al={"who is cortello","cortello lore","who made cortello's riddle"}}},kw={"bloodsail buccaneers","bridge","cortello","riddle","scroll","swamp of sorrows","wild shore"},rel={"subzone:wild-shore","zone:stranglethorn","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="Cortello's Riddle",["end"]="A Soggy Scroll",level="43",faction="Neutral",id=624},src={"Cortello's Riddle (quest)"}}
E["quest:625"] = {t="quest",n="Cortello's Riddle",z="stranglethorn",s="Following the trail begun with a waterlogged parchment found in the Swamp of Sorrows, a second cryptic verse urges travelers to a far-off land in Kalimdor. Deciphering the lines points treasure hunters toward a cave in the southwest of Dustwallow Marsh.",h="Following the trail begun with a waterlogged parchment found in the Swamp of Sorrows, a second cryptic verse...",sec={{t="A Verse Pointing Across the Sea",b="The second verse left by Cortello directs searchers toward the far-off land of Kalimdor. The rhyme describes a perilous and gloomy territory situated east of the Barrens: the sodden, treacherous wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh.",sp=0},{t="The Southwest Cavern",b="According to the riddle, a clue waits to be found in a cave in the southwest of the marsh.",sp=0},{t="Where the Verse Leads",b="The cave in the southwest of the marsh is Bloodfen Burrow, where a musty scroll waits to be found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this riddle send travelers?",a="The verse sends searchers to Kalimdor, specifically to Dustwallow Marsh, which lies east of the Barrens.",al={"where to go cortellos riddle","cortello part 2 location","where is the second riddle clue"}},{q="Where in Dustwallow Marsh is the clue hidden?",a="The verse places the clue in a cave in the southwest of the marsh.",al={"where is the cave in dustwallow","dustwallow riddle cave","bloodfen burrow riddle"}},{q="What item initiates this step of the trail?",a="This step begins with a soggy scroll found at the end of the first riddle's trail, in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"how does this quest start","what starts cortellos riddle 2"}}},kw={"bloodfen burrow","cortello","cortello's riddle","dustwallow marsh","musty scroll","soggy scroll","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:bloodfen-burrow","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="A Soggy Scroll",["end"]="Musty Scroll",level="43",faction="Neutral",id=625},src={"Cortello's Riddle (2)"}}
E["quest:626"] = {t="quest",n="Cortello's Riddle",z="stranglethorn",s="A cryptic musty scroll provides the final set of verse left behind by Cortello. The rhyming instructions direct treasure hunters far north to the troubled continent of Lordaeron, where the trail reaches its conclusion along the coastal waterfalls of the Hinterlands.",h="A cryptic musty scroll provides the final set of verse left behind by Cortello.",sec={{t="The Final Clue",b="Following the earlier scrolls, this weathered text points away from the southern tropics toward the embattled lands of Lordaeron. The riddle bids searchers to seek out the great turmoil in the north, promising that the long chase ends by braving that unrest and pursuing the coastline.",sp=0},{t="Beneath the Cascade",b="The verse specifies that the final hoard lies along the shore of the Hinterlands. At the base of the great falls, the treasure lies underwater.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this riddle lead?",a="The verse leads to the coast of the Hinterlands in Lordaeron, directing seekers to look underwater at the base of the great waterfall cascading from the cliffs.",al={"where is cortellos riddle final","where do i go for cortello riddle 3","cortello hinterlands location"}},{q="What starts this part of the search?",a="This final riddle is read from a musty scroll uncovered during the earlier steps of Cortello's treasure hunt.",al={"how to start cortellos riddle part 3","where do i get the scroll"}},{q="Who wrote these verses?",a="The riddles and hidden scrolls were left behind by a figure named Cortello, leading searchers to his hidden treasure.",al={"who is cortello","who made cortellos riddle"}}},kw={"cortello","cortello's riddle","hinterlands","lordaeron","musty scroll","overlook cliffs","treasure","waterfall"},rel={"zone:hinterlands","topic:lordaeron","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Musty Scroll",["end"]="Cortello's Treasure",level="51",faction="Neutral",id=626},src={"Cortello's Riddle (3)"}}
E["quest:627"] = {t="quest",n="Favor for Krazek",z="stranglethorn",s="While repairing a crock pot brought down to Booty Bay, the goblin Krazek demands a personal favor in return. He wants rare lesser bloodstone ore retrieved from a distant cave in the northern hills before he will hand back the repaired cookware.",h="While repairing a crock pot brought down to Booty Bay, the goblin Krazek demands a personal favor in return.",sec={{t="A Northern Bargain",b="After accepting the broken cookware in Booty Bay, Krazek pauses his tinkering to ask for a trade. Rather than repairing the pot for free, he directs you far northward into the Arathi Highlands. Within a cave in Drywhisker Gorge lies lesser bloodstone ore, a low-grade yet prized mineral sought after by those who understand its properties.",sp=0},{t="Ore from the Gorge",b="Krazek promises to work on fixing the pot while you make the long journey north. He expects four loads of the bloodstone brought back to the port, offering payment in exchange for the favor if you return with enough samples. He also makes it clear that if you lack the knowledge to extract the ore yourself, you will need to rely on someone who does.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Krazek and what does he want?",a="Krazek is a goblin operating in Booty Bay. While repairing a broken crock pot delivered to him, he asks for four loads of rare bloodstone ore to be hauled back from the north.",al={"who is krazek","krazek request"}},{q="Where is the bloodstone ore located?",a="The lesser bloodstone ore is found inside a mountain cave located in Drywhisker Gorge, situated far to the north within the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where is bloodstone ore","bloodstone location","drywhisker gorge location"}},{q="Why does Krazek want low-grade ore?",a="Although the deposits in the cave are not of the highest quality, Krazek notes that even low-grade bloodstone holds substantial value to anyone possessing the craft and knowledge to utilize it.",al={"why lesser bloodstone","bloodstone value"}},{q="What happens before this task?",a="Before Krazek makes this demand, you are sent to Booty Bay to deliver the damaged vessel in Krazek's Cookery.",al={"previous quest","what came before"}},{q="What happens after gathering the bloodstone?",a="Once Krazek receives the four loads of ore and provides your compensation, the journey continues with Return to Corporal Kaleb.",al={"next quest","what comes next"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Krazek directly points out that harvesting the ore requires mining expertise, warning that anyone lacking the skill will need to find someone capable of extracting the veins."},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","booty bay","drywhisker gorge","favor for krazek","krazek","lesser bloodstone ore","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","zone:arathi","subzone:drywhisker-gorge"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Krazek",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=627},src={"Favor for Krazek"}}
E["quest:628"] = {t="quest",n="Excelsior",z="stranglethorn",s="In Booty Bay, Drizzlik has finished the inner part of the Excelsior boots and now needs the skin of an elder saltwater crocolisk for the outside.",h="In Booty Bay, Drizzlik has finished the inner part of the Excelsior boots and now needs the skin of an elder...",sec={{t="The Outer Layer",b="With the inside done, only the outer layer remains, and for it Drizzlik uses nothing but the finest elder crocolisk skins, which are tougher and make a better surface for the designs and accents of the Excelsior line. The only skin that fits Drizzlik's plan is that of an elder saltwater crocolisk, and finding one is hard, for such elders come out only to guard other saltwater crocolisks. Drizzlik has also read somewhere that the numbers of saltwater crocolisks are dwindling, which would hurt business.",sp=0},{t="Drizzlik's Thanks",b="Drizzlik is pleased: the order can be filled and shipped to Director Riddlevox aboard the next boat bound for Undermine, and early at that. Drizzlik also made extras and gives you a pair for your trouble, insisting no boot is as fine as the Excelsior line.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Drizzlik?",a="Drizzlik is the maker of the Excelsior line of boots, working in Booty Bay.",al={"drizzlik","booty bay bootmaker","drizzlik npc"}},{q="Why does Drizzlik need an elder saltwater crocolisk skin?",a="Drizzlik says elder skins are tougher and give a better surface for the Excelsior designs and accents, and that only the skin of an elder saltwater crocolisk fits the plan.",al={"why croc skin","excelsior boot materials","elder crocolisk skin use"}},{q="Why are elder saltwater crocolisks hard to find?",a="Drizzlik says elders come out only to defend other saltwater crocolisks.",al={"where are elder crocs","find elder saltwater crocolisk","how to summon elder croc"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="Some Assembly Required came first.",al={"previous quest","excelsior prerequisite","some assembly required link"}},{q="What concern does Drizzlik have about saltwater crocolisks?",a="Drizzlik has read that saltwater crocolisks are dwindling in number, which would be bad for business.",al={"are crocs dying out","saltwater croc population","crocolisk extinction"}}},kw={"booty bay","crocolisk","drizzlik","elder crocolisk","excelsior","saltwater crocolisk","stranglethorn"},rel={"quest:577","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Drizzlik",["end"]="Drizzlik",level="38",id=628},src={"Classic quest text: Excelsior"}}
E["quest:629"] = {t="quest",n="The Vile Reef",z="stranglethorn",s="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp seeks a piece of an ancient stone tablet resting deep beneath the Savage Coast. The sunken city, known as the Vile Reef, is infested with aggressive murlocs and holds the legendary history of Gri'lek, which the Darkspear tribe wishes to preserve in Orgrimmar.",h="Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp seeks a piece of an ancient stone tablet resting deep beneath the Savage...",sec={{t="Sunken Legends",b="Northwest of Grom'gol Base Camp, an ancient troll city slipped beneath the waters along the Savage Coast when a violent earthquake shattered the land long ago. Now referred to as the Vile Reef, its flooded ruins crawl with hostile murlocs that assault anyone venturing near. Resting on the sea floor among the ruins is a massive stone tablet carved with the story of Gri'lek, a legendary troll hero whose memory remains sacred to the Darkspear.",sp=0},{t="A Keepsake for Orgrimmar",b="Because the full monument is far too massive to carry away from the depths, Kin'weelay asks you to break off a shard from the stone. He intends to carry this fragment back to Orgrimmar, enshrining it in a sacred place so the Darkspear will never forget the strength and honor of Gri'lek.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Vile Reef located?",a="The Vile Reef lies underwater along the Savage Coast, northwest of Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"vile reef location","where is vile reef","how to find vile reef"}},{q="Why does Kin'weelay want the tablet shard?",a="The tablet preserves the sacred story of the troll hero Gri'lek. Kin'weelay plans to bring the shard back to Orgrimmar and place it in a sacred site so the Darkspear tribe can honor their heritage in their new home.",al={"why get tablet shard","tablet shard purpose","why griklek tablet"}},{q="What happened to the ancient city at the Vile Reef?",a="Long ago, a tremendous earthquake shook the Savage Coast and caused the entire troll city to sink beneath the ocean waves.",al={"what happened to vile reef","how did vile reef sink","sunken troll city history"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Vile Reef now?",a="Hostile murlocs have made their home among the submerged ruins and attack anyone who approaches the sunken city.",al={"monsters in vile reef","vile reef enemies","who lives in vile reef"}},{q="Who is Gri'lek?",a="Gri'lek is a legendary troll hero whose history was carved upon the sunken tablet beneath the Savage Coast and is held sacred by the Darkspear.",al={"who is griklek","grilek lore","hero griklek"}},{q="Why take only a shard instead of the whole tablet?",a="The carved monument on the ocean floor is far too immense to haul up from the ruins, so retrieving a single broken piece is the only practical way to bring the legend back to Orgrimmar.",al={"why only a shard","can we take whole tablet","bring whole tablet"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, retrieving this fragment keeps their ancient traditions and reverence for the great hero Gri'lek alive in their new home in Orgrimmar.",["faction:Horde"]="Helping Kin'weelay recover this relic for Orgrimmar strengthens the bond of trust between the Horde and the Darkspear tribe."},kw={"darkspear","gri'lek","grom'gol base camp","kin'weelay","murloc","savage coast","stranglethorn","tablet shard","vile reef"},rel={"npc:kin-weelay","subzone:vile-reef","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:savage-coast","zone:stranglethorn","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:orgrimmar","topic:murloc"},m={start="Kin'weelay",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="37",faction="Horde",id=629},src={"The Vile Reef (quest)","In-game quest text: The Vile Reef"}}
E["quest:630"] = {t="quest",n="Message in a Bottle",z="stranglethorn",s="Having answered an ocean-borne plea, you find Princess Poobah chained as a captive on an isolated island off the Stranglethorn coast. The monstrous ape King Mukla commands the local beasts and keeps her bound, requiring his defeat to secure the key to her shackle.",h="Having answered an ocean-borne plea, you find Princess Poobah chained as a captive on an isolated island off...",sec={{t="A Captive on the Isle",b="Following the message in the bottle brings you directly to Princess Poobah, who is held against her will by a heavy chain. The great Skymane gorilla known as King Mukla commands the creatures roaming the island and oversees her imprisonment. Poobah places her faith in you to face this formidable ape and retrieve the key needed to sever her bonds.",sp=0},{t="The Beast to the Southeast",b="Poobah notes that her captor can often be heard prowling around the southeastern side of the island. Confronting King Mukla is no small feat, but taking him down is the only way to claim the shackle key and secure Poobah's release.",sp=0},{t="Deliverance and Gratitude",b="Bringing the shackle key back frees Princess Poobah from captivity and saves her from what she considers a deep dishonor. Though she lacks the power to grant you full induction into her tribe, she offers you a token of thanks for your courage.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Princess Poobah?",a="Princess Poobah is a tribal captive found chained on an island off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale. After sending out a plea in a bottle, she waits for someone daring enough to overcome her captor and unlock her shackle.",al={"poobah","who is poobah","princess poobah lore"}},{q="Who holds Princess Poobah captive?",a="She is held captive by King Mukla, a massive Skymane gorilla who holds sway over the surrounding beasts on the island.",al={"who captured poobah","poobah captor","king mukla captive"}},{q="Where is King Mukla found?",a="Princess Poobah states that King Mukla can frequently be heard wandering across the southeastern side of the island.",al={"where is mukla","mukla location","find king mukla"}},{q="What is needed to free Princess Poobah?",a="You need to defeat King Mukla and find the key to her shackle, then bring it back to unlock the chain binding her.",al={"poobah shackle key","how to free poobah","key to free princess poobah"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the story?",a="This follows the original plea found in a bottle, serving as the direct confrontation against King Mukla to deliver Princess Poobah from her chains.",al={"message in a bottle chain","message in a bottle part 2","poobah quest line"}}},kw={"jaguero island","king mukla","princess poobah","shackle key","skymane","stranglethorn"},rel={"quest:594","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Princess Poobah",["end"]="Princess Poobah",level="51",faction="Neutral",id=630},src={"Message in a Bottle (2)"}}
E["quest:638"] = {t="quest",n="Trollbane",z="stranglethorn",s="Vol'jin has ordered the Darkspear trolls to recover the ancient sword Trol'kalar from the ruined human kingdom of Stromgarde. With King Thoras Trollbane fallen, the blade is meant to serve the Horde in future conflicts against the trolls of Zul'Gurub.",h="Vol'jin has ordered the Darkspear trolls to recover the ancient sword Trol'kalar from the ruined human...",sec={{t="A King Fallen, A Blade Coveted",b="Following the death of King Thoras Trollbane and the collapse of Stromgarde into ruin, Chieftain Vol'jin has ordered that every effort be made to spirit Trol'kalar away. This storied blade has long rested in human hands, but the Darkspear tribe hopes to claim it for the battles looming against the jungle trolls dwelling within Zul'Gurub.",sp=0},{t="Journey to Hammerfall",b="To carry out Vol'jin's directive, a seasoned hunter named Zengu was sent to the Horde outpost of Hammerfall, situated in the northeastern reaches of the Arathi Highlands. Nimboya directs travelers from Stranglethorn Vale to seek out Zengu and assist in securing the legendary weapon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Vol'jin want the sword Trol'kalar?",a="Vol'jin intends to use Trol'kalar in the coming battles against the hostile jungle trolls in Zul'Gurub.",al={"why trolkalar","why trollbane sword","purpose of trolkalar"}},{q="Who is Zengu?",a="Zengu is an experienced hunter dispatched by the Darkspear to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands to oversee the recovery of Trol'kalar.",al={"who is zengu","zengu role","hunter zengu"}},{q="Where does this journey send you?",a="The journey leads north out of Stranglethorn Vale to Hammerfall, an outpost in the northeastern Arathi Highlands.",al={"where to go","quest destination","where is zengu"}},{q="What happened to Stromgarde?",a="Stromgarde lies in ruins following the demise of its ruler, King Thoras Trollbane.",al={"stromgarde status","what happened to thoras trollbane"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Vol'jin specifically seeks Trol'kalar to arm the Darkspear against their ancient kin in Zul'Gurub.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's hunter Zengu waits at Hammerfall to see the legendary sword taken from the humans."},kw={"hammerfall","nimboya","stromgarde","trol'kalar","trollbane","vol'jin","zengu","zul'gurub"},rel={"npc:vol-jin","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","topic:human","topic:hunter"},m={start="Nimboya",["end"]="Zengu",level="37",faction="Horde",id=638},src={"Trollbane (quest)"}}
E["quest:7810"] = {t="quest",n="Arena Master",z="stranglethorn",s="Is there more to mastering the arena than this? Short John Mithril, the Pirate behind the Gurubashi event, may have the answer, and you will find him in the Stranglethorn Arena.",h="Is there more to mastering the arena than this?",sec={{t="Seeking the Pirate",b="Whatever you have gained at Gurubashi, it seems that mastering the arena asks for more. Short John Mithril, the Pirate who organizes the contests there, may know what. Look for him inside the Stranglethorn Arena.",sp=0},{t="Short John's Word",b="Short John Mithril tells you that a single trinket is too little to make you master of the arena. Now, he says, comes the true proving of your steel.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do I need to speak with?",a="Short John Mithril, the Pirate behind the Gurubashi event.",al={"who do i talk to","arena master turn in","where to go"}},{q="Where is Short John Mithril?",a="In the Stranglethorn Arena, at Gurubashi in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"gurubashi location","where is stranglethorn arena","arena location"}},{q="What is hinted about being master of the arena?",a="Only that mastering the arena seems to ask for more than you have done so far, and that the Pirate behind the Gurubashi event may know.",al={"how to be arena master","am i arena master yet"}}},kw={"arena master","gurubashi","pirate","short john mithril","stranglethorn arena","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","topic:pirate"},m={start="Arena Master",["end"]="Short John Mithril",level="55",id=7810},src={"Wowpedia: Arena Master (quest)"}}
E["quest:8551"] = {t="quest",n="The Captain's Chest",z="stranglethorn",s="Captain Hecklebury Smotts used to sail between Booty Bay and Ratchet in Kalimdor, until sea giants wrecked the ship, killed the crew and sent Smotts off in a lifeboat toward Booty Bay. The giant Gorlash took Smotts' Captain's Chest, and Smotts wants it back.",h="Captain Hecklebury Smotts used to sail between Booty Bay and Ratchet in Kalimdor, until sea giants wrecked...",sec={{t="A Ruined Captain",b="Smotts says the voyages to Ratchet in Kalimdor built a successful career and a fine reputation. The sea giants ended all that: they smashed the ship, killed the crew and sent Smotts off in a lifeboat toward Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Chest",b="The giant Gorlash took Smotts' Captain's Chest, saying he wanted it as a snuffbox. The chest was Smotts' favorite, with a secret compartment where the greatest treasures were stored. Smotts has heard that Gorlash roams the shore east of Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="Smotts' Thanks",b="Smotts is overjoyed to have the chest back, and it takes some of the fire out of the anger, yet the revenge is not complete.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Hecklebury Smotts?",a="Smotts is a ship captain in Booty Bay who once sailed between there and Ratchet in Kalimdor, until sea giants smashed the ship and killed the crew.",al={"captain smotts","who is smotts","hecklebury smotts"}},{q="Who took the chest?",a="Gorlash, one of the sea giants, took it and said he wanted it as a snuffbox.",al={"who stole the chest","who has smotts chest","gorlash"}},{q="Where can Gorlash be found?",a="East of Booty Bay, along the shore. That is where Smotts has heard the giant roams.",al={"where is gorlash","gorlash location","find gorlash"}},{q="Why does Smotts want the chest back?",a="It was Smotts' favorite chest, and its hidden compartment kept the greatest treasures.",al={"what is in the chest","why does smotts want the chest"}}},kw={"booty bay","gorlash","ratchet","sea giant","smotts","snuffbox","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:ratchet","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Captain Hecklebury Smotts",["end"]="Captain Hecklebury Smotts",level="47",id=8551},src={"Classic quest text: The Captain's Chest"}}
E["quest:8552"] = {t="quest",n="The Monogrammed Sash",z="stranglethorn",s="A fine sash bearing embroidered initials hints at a rightful owner somewhere in Stranglethorn Vale. Finding the seafarer who lost it leads on to The Captain's Cutlass.",h="A fine sash bearing embroidered initials hints at a rightful owner somewhere in Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="A Marked Garment",b="This fine sash bears the letters 'HS' embroidered along its hem. Whoever lost it can only be traced by those two letters.",sp=0},{t="The Smotts Connection",b="Returning the garment to Captain Hecklebury Smotts confirms it belongs to him. Recovering it reveals that the sea giant Mok'rash has been slain, bringing relief to the captain after the brute took part in destroying his vessels and crew on multiple occasions.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What letters are stitched into the sash?",a="The hem of the fine sash is embroidered with the initials 'HS'.",al={"what initials are on sash","initials on monogrammed sash","sash letters"}},{q="Where does this lead next?",a="Once the sash is returned to its owner, the next step is The Captain's Cutlass.",al={"what quest comes after monogrammed sash","monogrammed sash next quest","next step"}}},kw={"hecklebury smotts","hs","mok'rash","monogrammed sash","sea giant","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"quest:8553","quest:618","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Monogrammed Sash",["end"]="Captain Hecklebury Smotts",level="50",id=8552},src={"The Monogrammed Sash"}}
E["quest:8553"] = {t="quest",n="The Captain's Cutlass",z="stranglethorn",s="Captain Hecklebury Smotts bought a second vessel named Smotts' Revenge to hunt down the sea giants who took his first ship, only to suffer another defeat. The giants smashed the vessel and killed the crew, and one of them, Negolash, stole the captain's cutlass. Smotts directs you to consult his former ship cook, Sprogger, to track down the behemoth.",h="Captain Hecklebury Smotts bought a second vessel named Smotts' Revenge to hunt down the sea giants who took...",sec={{t="A Second Calamity",b="Following the loss of his initial ship, Captain Hecklebury Smotts procured a second craft called Smotts' Revenge, gathering a fresh crew and provisions to take vengeance on the sea giants. The venture ended in disaster when the giants shattered the ship and slew the crew, leaving Smotts adrift once more in a lifeboat. During the onslaught, the giant Negolash took the captain's cutlass.",sp=0},{t="Consulting the Cook",b="Determined to retrieve his stolen blade, Smotts relies on his cook. Sprogger, who served aboard Smotts' Revenge, lived through the attack and can help find Negolash.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What ship did Captain Hecklebury Smotts lose in this attack?",a="Smotts purchased and outfitted a ship called Smotts' Revenge to hunt the giants that destroyed his first vessel, but the giants destroyed it as well.",al={"what was the second ship called","smotts second ship","what ship was smashed"}},{q="Who stole the captain's cutlass?",a="Negolash, one of the sea giants that smashed Smotts' Revenge and killed the crew, took the weapon.",al={"who has the cutlass","which giant took the cutlass","who took smotts cutlass"}},{q="Who is Sprogger?",a="Sprogger worked as the cook aboard Smotts' Revenge and survived the attack that destroyed the vessel. Captain Smotts directs travelers to him for help finding Negolash.",al={"who is sprogger","sprogger role","who was the cook"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the hunt for the sea giants?",a="This step follows The Monogrammed Sash and leads directly to Facing Negolash.",al={"what quest comes before this","what is the next quest","cutlass quest chain"}}},kw={"cutlass","hecklebury smotts","negolash","sea giants","smotts revenge","sprogger","stranglethorn"},rel={"quest:8552","quest:618","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Captain Hecklebury Smotts",["end"]="Sprogger",level="42",faction="Both",id=8553},src={"The Captain's Cutlass"}}
E["quest:98463"] = {t="quest",n="Talk of the Town",z="stranglethorn",s="A friendly barkeep points travelers eager for a livelier gathering toward the port of Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale. Those looking for wilder company are directed to seek out Nixxrax Fillamug at the Salty Sailor Tavern.",h="A friendly barkeep points travelers eager for a livelier gathering toward the port of Booty Bay in...",sec={{t="A Word Across the Counter",b="Word passes quickly between drink-servers and their patrons, and news travels far beyond the local counter. A friendly bartender passes along a tip about where the genuine commotion is brewing, pointing anyone searching for wilder spectacles toward the port of Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="The Salty Sailor",b="The destination is the Salty Sailor Tavern, a lively establishment maintained by goblins amidst the bustle of Stranglethorn Vale. There, Nixxrax Fillamug keeps cups topped up for anyone who walks in.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this lead?",a="This leads to Stranglethorn Vale, straight to the goblin-run port town of Booty Bay.",al={"where do i go","destination","booty bay directions"}},{q="Who are you supposed to find in Booty Bay?",a="You are directed to find Nixxrax Fillamug inside the Salty Sailor Tavern, where he keeps everyone's drinks topped up.",al={"who to visit","who is nixxrax","nixxrax fillamug"}},{q="Why send someone all the way to Stranglethorn Vale?",a="Bartenders hear all the gossip from their patrons, and word has it that the Salty Sailor Tavern holds the wildest festivities around, regardless of goblin management.",al={"why salty sailor","why go to booty bay","why the recommendation"}}},kw={"booty bay","goblin tavern","nixxrax fillamug","salty sailor tavern","stranglethorn vale","talk of the town"},rel={"subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin"},m={id=98463},src={"In-game quest text: Talk of the Town"},fv=true}
E["subzone:bal-lal-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Bal'lal Ruins",z="stranglethorn",s="Bal'lal Ruins are ancient Gurubashi troll ruins set along the northwestern shore of Stranglethorn Vale, just north of Grom'gol Base Camp. Overlooking the murky waters of the Vile Reef, the crumbling stone foundations are currently occupied by hostile Bloodscalp trolls.",h="Bal'lal Ruins are ancient Gurubashi troll ruins set along the northwestern shore of Stranglethorn Vale, just...",sec={{t="A Crumbling Outpost on the Reef",b="Perched on the coastline north of Grom'gol Base Camp, Bal'lal Ruins stand as another remnant of the shattered Gurubashi Empire. Once part of the grand troll civilization that dominated southern Azeroth, the site has decayed into moss-covered stone walls and cracked masonry. The ruins sit immediately adjacent to the Vile Reef, offering an elevated vantage over the treacherous coastal shallows. Today, aggressive Bloodscalp trolls hold the grounds, fiercely defending the weathered relics of their ancestors against intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Bal'lal Ruins?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by members of the Bloodscalp tribe, who aggressively guard the territory against outsiders, travelers, and rivals alike.",al={"who lives here","ballal ruins mobs","who is at ballal ruins"}},{q="Where are the Bal'lal Ruins located?",a="You can find them along the northwestern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, situated directly north of Grom'gol Base Camp and looking out over the Vile Reef.",al={"ballal ruins location","where is ballal ruins","how to find ballal ruins"}},{q="What history do these ruins have?",a="Like most stone structures scattered throughout Stranglethorn Vale, Bal'lal Ruins date back to the ancient Gurubashi Empire before its fragmentation into fractured, warring jungle troll tribes.",al={"ballal lore","history of ballal ruins","who built ballal ruins"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls aligned with the Horde, sites like Bal'lal are a sobering glimpse into the ruins of ancient Gurubashi glory, held by cousin tribes blinded by relentless bloodlust.",["faction:Horde"]="Lying just up the coast from Grom'gol Base Camp, the hostile Bloodscalp presence at Bal'lal poses an ongoing security nuisance to Horde patrols along the shoreline."},kw={"bal'lal ruins","ballal ruins","bloodscalp","grom'gol","gurubashi","stranglethorn vale","vile reef"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:vile-reef","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:troll"},src={"Bal'lal Ruins"}}
E["subzone:balia-mah-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Balia'mah Ruins",z="stranglethorn",s="The Balia'mah Ruins are the moss-covered remnants of an ancient Gurubashi settlement in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Located east of Grom'gol Base Camp across the river, the crumbling stone tiers are currently claimed and guarded by warriors of the hostile Skullsplitter troll tribe.",h="The Balia'mah Ruins are the moss-covered remnants of an ancient Gurubashi settlement in northern...",sec={{t="A Shattered Heritage",b="Like many of the stone edifices dotting the jungle, Balia'mah stands as a remnant of the sprawling Gurubashi Empire that once ruled much of the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Following the fall of their ancient capital, Gurubashi territory splintered into warring factions. Today, the ruins serve as a stronghold for the Skullsplitter tribe, who fiercely defend the stone terraces against wandering beasts, neighboring ogres from the Mosh'Ogg mound, and any outsiders foolish enough to cross the river.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Balia'mah Ruins located?",a="The ruins lie in northern Stranglethorn Vale, east-southeast across the river from the Horde outpost of Grom'gol Base Camp and southwest of the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound.",al={"bali'mah location","where is balia mah","baliamah ruins map"}},{q="Who controls the ruins right now?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by the Skullsplitter tribe, a hostile faction of jungle trolls that aggressively guards the ancient stone terraces.",al={"who lives in balia mah","what mobs are at balia mah","balia mah enemies"}},{q="What is the history of Balia'mah?",a="The complex was constructed during the height of the Gurubashi Empire. After the empire collapsed, the site fell into decay, eventually being reclaimed by jungle overgrowth and surviving troll tribes.",al={"balia mah lore","who built balia mah"}},{q="Are the Skullsplitters at Balia'mah connected to other troll camps?",a="Yes. The Skullsplitter tribe maintains several encampments and ruins throughout northern and central Stranglethorn Vale, engaged in constant territorial warfare against rival tribes such as the Bloodscalp.",al={"skullsplitters in stranglethorn","baliamah skullsplitters"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, walking these ancient stone tiers is a reminder of the proud Gurubashi civilization their ancestors shared, as well as the dark factionalism that tore jungle troll society apart.",["faction:Horde"]="Perched just across the river from Grom'gol Base Camp, the hostile Skullsplitters at Balia'mah present a constant perimeter threat to Horde scouts and supply lines."},kw={"balia'mah","baliamah","gurubashi","ruins","skullsplitter","stranglethorn"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:mosh-ogg-ogre-mound","topic:troll"},src={"Balia'mah Ruins"}}
E["subzone:booty-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Booty Bay",z="stranglethorn",s="Booty Bay is a sprawling pirate haven built into the sheer sea cliffs of southern Stranglethorn Vale, operated by the Steamwheedle Cartel's Blackwater Raiders. Entered by land through the gaping jaws of a giant shark carcass, it serves as a fiercely enforced neutral port where Alliance and Horde mingle under the watchful eyes of heavily armed goblin bruisers.",h="Booty Bay is a sprawling pirate haven built into the sheer sea cliffs of southern Stranglethorn Vale...",sec={{t="A Den of Scoundrels and Profit",b="Originally known as Blackwater Cove when it was a human settlement later overrun by jungle trolls, the bay was eventually captured by the goblins of the Steamwheedle Cartel. Today, it is an international crossroads and a haven for scoundrels, outcasts, and merchants alike. Overseen by Baron Revilgaz alongside Fleet Master Seahorn from the balconies of the Salty Sailor Tavern, the port is ostensibly lawless yet strictly managed: anyone may drink, trade, or hire mercenaries here, provided they obey the cartel's peace and pay their harbor fees.",sp=0},{t="Threats on the Water",b="Booty Bay's bustling docks connect the Eastern Kingdoms directly to Ratchet across the Great Sea, making it a critical hub for trade and cross-continental travel. However, its immense wealth attracts relentless hostility. The town's primary nemesis is the Bloodsail Buccaneers, an aggressive pirate fleet that constantly raids Blackwater shipping, roams the Stranglethorn coastline, and actively plots the total destruction and plunder of the goblin port.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Booty Bay?",a="The port is ruled by Baron Revilgaz, a prominent figure in the Steamwheedle Cartel, working in close concert with Fleet Master Seahorn, the tauren commander of the Blackwater Raiders. Both run their operations from the upper decks of the Salty Sailor Tavern overlooking the harbor.",al={"booty bay leader","who is in charge of booty bay","booty bay boss"}},{q="Why can Alliance and Horde players stand together here?",a="Booty Bay is controlled by the neutral Steamwheedle Cartel, which values profit and commerce far above the faction conflict. The cartel maintains strict neutrality, welcoming anyone with coin and unleashing elite goblin bruisers upon anyone foolish enough to start a brawl.",al={"why is booty bay neutral","booty bay safe zone","can horde attack alliance here"}},{q="Who are the Bloodsail Buccaneers?",a="The Bloodsail Buccaneers are a rival outlaw syndicate at bitter war with the Blackwater Raiders. They control ships along the southern coast of Stranglethorn Vale and actively scheme to overwhelm Booty Bay and seize its lucrative harbor.",al={"bloodsail pirates","why do bloodsail hate booty bay","bloodsail buccaneers lore"}},{q="Where does the boat in Booty Bay sail?",a="The passenger vessel operating from the lower docks sails across the Great Sea directly to the port town of Ratchet in the Barrens, providing the main neutral transit route between the southern Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"booty bay boat destination","where does the ship go","boat to kalimdor"}},{q="What is the giant statue standing at the bay's entrance?",a="The massive statue of an unknown goblin with outstretched arms stands on Janeiro's Point just outside the harbor mouth. It serves as a navigational beacon and welcoming monument for incoming merchant ships and pirate crews.",al={"booty bay statue","colossus of booty bay","statue on the island"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Known as a scoundrel's paradise, Booty Bay is teeming with underworld contacts, fences, lockboxes, and covert informants ready to trade secrets for coin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Far south of Stormwind's protected borders, Booty Bay provides Alliance travelers with rare neutral amenities, flight routes, and ship passage straight to Kalimdor."},kw={"blackwater raiders","bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","ratchet","revilgaz","salty sailor","seahorn","steamwheedle cartel","stranglethorn"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:ratchet","subzone:janeiro-s-point","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","topic:pirate"},src={"Booty Bay"}}
E["subzone:cape-of-stranglethorn"] = {t="subzone",n="Cape of Stranglethorn",z="stranglethorn",s="The Cape of Stranglethorn forms the sun-baked southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale, stretching south from the Gurubashi Arena down to the ocean cliffs. Anchored by the sprawling pirate port of Booty Bay, the region is a battleground contested by goblins, Bloodsail Buccaneers, ancient jungle trolls, and encroaching wildlife.",h="The Cape of Stranglethorn forms the sun-baked southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale, stretching south from the...",sec={{t="Edge of the Continent",b="South of the ancient colosseum of Gurubashi Arena, the dense jungle gives way to the coastline known as the Cape of Stranglethorn. Dotted with crumbling troll settlements like the Ruins of Jubuwal and the Ruins of Aboraz, the cape has long since slipped from imperial Gurubashi control. Today, its beaches, coves, and jungle clearings host a chaotic mix of dangerous predators, murloc encampments, and rival pirate crews warring over trade routes and buried plunder.",sp=0},{t="Booty Bay and the Buccaneer War",b="The dominant power along the cape is the Blackwater Raiders, led by Baron Revilgaz and Fleet Master Seahorn from the pirate city of Booty Bay. Carved directly into the cliffs of the southern bay, this neutral harbor connects the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor via steamships to Ratchet. However, goblin control remains precarious. The Bloodsail Buccaneers operate along the southern shoals and outer islands, raiding supply lines and openly scheming to overthrow Booty Bay and seize total dominion over the South Seas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between Stranglethorn Vale and the Cape of Stranglethorn?",a="The Cape of Stranglethorn specifically refers to the southern portion of the larger Stranglethorn Vale, encompassing the land and coasts south of the Gurubashi Arena down to Booty Bay.",al={"cape vs vale","stranglethorn geography","where is the cape"}},{q="Who rules the Cape of Stranglethorn?",a="No single authority controls the entire cape. Booty Bay and its surrounding waters are governed by Baron Revilgaz and the goblin-backed Blackwater Raiders, while the Bloodsail Buccaneers, naga, and troll remnants control various beaches and interior ruins.",al={"who leads booty bay","cape ruler","who controls the cape"}},{q="Can Horde and Alliance both use Booty Bay?",a="Yes. Booty Bay is an open, neutral port maintained by the Steamwheedle Cartel. So long as travelers keep their weapons sheathed and maintain peace within the city limits, both Alliance and Horde adventurers may access its docks, vendors, flight master, and auction house.",al={"is booty bay neutral","alliance horde booty bay","can horde enter booty bay"}},{q="What is the Gurubashi Arena?",a="The Gurubashi Arena is an ancient troll fighting pit near the northern edge of the cape, where combatants gather to test themselves.",al={"gurubashi chest","arena rules","pvp arena stranglethorn"}},{q="How do travelers get between the Cape and Kalimdor?",a="A goblin-operated steamship regularly runs between the docks of Booty Bay and the port town of Ratchet in the Barrens, providing one of the few trans-oceanic passenger links across the South Seas.",al={"boat to ratchet","kalimdor transport","booty bay boat"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The cape is a haven for privateers, scoundrels, and cutthroats, offering endless opportunities to pick pockets, run coastal contraband, or play the Blackwater Raiders against the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",["profession:Cooking"]="The surrounding South Seas and coastal waters provide valuable fishing grounds and rare recipes sold exclusively by the fishmongers and harbor cooks of Booty Bay."},kw={"baron revilgaz","blackwater raiders","bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","cape of stranglethorn","gurubashi arena","south seas","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:booty-bay","npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:gurubashi-arena","subzone:ratchet","subzone:ruins-of-aboraz","subzone:ruins-of-jubuwal"},src={"Cape of Stranglethorn"}}
E["subzone:crystal-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystal Shore",z="stranglethorn",s="Crystal Shore is a stretch of sandy coastline along the southeastern edge of Stranglethorn Vale, washed by the waves of the South Seas. Tucked beneath steep coastal bluffs, the beach lies just south of the ancient Ruins of Aboraz and across the waters from Jaguero Isle.",h="Crystal Shore is a stretch of sandy coastline along the southeastern edge of Stranglethorn Vale, washed by...",sec={{t="A Secluded Coastal Strip",b="Running along the southeastern perimeter of Stranglethorn Vale, the Crystal Shore forms a natural boundary between the dense tropical interior and the open waters of the South Seas. The beach itself is walled off from the inland jungles by steep ridges, leaving only a couple of rugged passes for travelers attempting to move between the coast and the deeper wilderness of Mistvale Valley. To the north lie the crumbling troll structures of the Ruins of Aboraz, while the Wild Shore extends along the southern curves of the cape. Its location makes it a quiet, windswept margin far removed from the bustling docks of Booty Bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Crystal Shore located?",a="The Crystal Shore is situated on the far southeastern coast of Stranglethorn Vale. It stretches along the waters facing the South Seas, positioned south of the Ruins of Aboraz and northeast of the Wild Shore.",al={"crystal shore location","where is crystal shore","crystal shore map"}},{q="How do you access the Crystal Shore from inland?",a="A steep ridge divides the beach from the mainland jungle. However, a couple of narrow natural passes cut through the high cliffs, including a trail leading directly into Mistvale Valley.",al={"how to get to crystal shore","path to crystal shore","reach crystal shore"}},{q="What landmarks are nearby?",a="Just to the north of the shore stand the ancient Ruins of Aboraz, while across the channel to the southwest sits Jaguero Isle. Further down the coastline to the south lies the Wild Shore.",al={"landmarks near crystal shore","what is near crystal shore"}},{q="Is the Crystal Shore settled by any faction?",a="No formal faction maintains a town or settlement along the Crystal Shore. It remains an untamed stretch of beach dominated by native wildlife, ancient troll ruins to the north, and the crashing waves of the South Seas.",al={"who lives at crystal shore","crystal shore settlement","crystal shore towns"}}},kw={"crystal shore","jaguero isle","mistvale valley","ruins of aboraz","south seas","stranglethorn vale","wild shore"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:ruins-of-aboraz","subzone:wild-shore","subzone:jaguero-isle","subzone:south-seas"},src={"Crystal Shore"}}
E["subzone:crystalvein-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystalvein Mine",z="stranglethorn",s="Crystalvein Mine is a cavern in central Stranglethorn Vale, situated near the ancient ruins of Zul'Mamwe. The cavern is rich in valuable 'Singing Crystals', but aggressive native basilisks have completely overrun the site, turning prospective miners to solid stone.",h="Crystalvein Mine is a cavern in central Stranglethorn Vale, situated near the ancient ruins of Zul'Mamwe.",sec={{t="A Lucrative Trap",b="Tucked away in the jungle hills near Zul'Mamwe, Crystalvein Mine boasts rare deposits of Singing Crystals, a unique mineral that fetches a high price in southern trade ports. Enticed by the promise of immense profit, the Venture Company set its sights on extracting the veins. However, the mine's natural inhabitants have proved catastrophic for business. Local basilisks consume the strange crystals, hardening their scales and making them unnaturally lethal. Outside the cave mouth, petrified statues of trolls and humans stand as a silent testament to the Venture Company's failed expeditions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes Crystalvein Mine valuable?",a="The mine holds deposits of rare 'Singing Crystals', a lucrative mineral found only in Stranglethorn Vale. Goblins such as Crank Fizzlebub prize them for their acoustic and monetary worth, driving prospectors to brave the dangerous caverns.",al={"why is crystalvein mine important","what is in crystalvein mine","singing crystals"}},{q="Why are there stone statues outside the mine?",a="The statues are the petrified remains of unfortunate troll locals and Venture Company laborers. The resident basilisks feed on the resonant crystals, enhancing their stony hides and petrifying anyone foolish enough to encroach on their feeding grounds.",al={"petrified people crystalvein","crystallized trolls crystalvein","stone bodies stranglethorn"}},{q="Who controls Crystalvein Mine right now?",a="Though the Venture Company claimed rights to exploit the cavern, they do not actually hold it. The basilisk infestation is so intense that the goblins have been unable to establish active mining operations within the depths.",al={"who owns crystalvein","crystalvein faction","venture co crystalvein"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners drawn by the promise of Singing Crystals must tread carefully, as the cave's native basilisk population makes prospecting here among the most dangerous endeavors in Stranglethorn."},kw={"basilisk","crank fizzlebub","crystalvein mine","singing crystals","stranglethorn vale","venture co","zul'mamwe"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","quest:764","topic:troll"},src={"Crystalvein Mine"}}
E["subzone:grom-gol-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Grom'gol Base Camp",z="stranglethorn",s="Grom'gol Base Camp is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in Stranglethorn Vale, situated along the western coast of northern Stranglethorn. Commanded by Commander Aggro'gosh, the settlement secures a critical foothold and supply chain in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. With direct zeppelin towers linking to Orgrimmar and the Undercity, it stands as an armed staging ground against local jungle troll tribes and hostile Alliance forces.",h="Grom'gol Base Camp is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in Stranglethorn Vale, situated along the western...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Jungle",b="Carved into the dense jungle of northwestern Stranglethorn Vale, Grom'gol Base Camp is a fortified military bastion commanded by Commander Aggro'gosh. Ringed by defensive palisades and heavily armed grunts, the base camp endures non-stop harassment from Bloodscalp headhunters, lurking naga, and prowling beasts. Despite these threats, its vital strategic location secures safe supply routes north toward Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows while keeping a watchful eye on Alliance traffic descending from Duskwood or traveling up from Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="Airbridge of the Horde",b="Grom'gol's prominent wooden zeppelin towers serve as one of the most vital logistical hubs in the Eastern Kingdoms. Goblin skycraft tethered here maintain regular routes directly to the capital cities of Orgrimmar and the Undercity. This uninterrupted airbridge allows Horde forces to rapidly deploy reinforcements and resources straight into the heart of Stranglethorn without braving Alliance-dominated highways or the deep sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Grom'gol Base Camp?",a="Grom'gol serves as the Horde's fortified military staging point in Stranglethorn Vale. Under the command of Commander Aggro'gosh, it establishes a logistical lifeline to the outpost of Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows and protects Horde interests against hostile jungle trolls and Alliance incursions.",al={"why is gromgol here","gromgol purpose","what is gromgol"}},{q="How do you travel to and from Grom'gol?",a="Grom'gol is home to major zeppelin towers that offer direct flights to both Orgrimmar in Kalimdor and the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades. It also maintains a wind rider roost connected to the flight network linking Kargath, Stonard, and Booty Bay.",al={"gromgol zeppelin","gromgol flight paths","how to get to gromgol"}},{q="Who leads Grom'gol Base Camp?",a="The outpost is commanded by the orc Commander Aggro'gosh, who oversees the defense of the stockade against hostile native troll tribes, savage wild raptors, and Alliance scouts.",al={"gromgol leader","who runs gromgol","commander of gromgol"}},{q="What threats does the camp face?",a="Grom'gol is hemmed in on all sides by dangerous adversaries. The Bloodscalp jungle trolls actively hunt along its borders, savage raptors stalk the fields to the north, and Alliance soldiers constantly venture down from Duskwood or up from the port of Booty Bay.",al={"gromgol enemies","who attacks gromgol"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Grom'gol is the primary safe haven and logistical staging area for Horde adventurers navigating the treacherous jungles and contested roads of Stranglethorn Vale.",["faction:Alliance"]="Grom'gol is a heavily defended enemy bastion that gives the Horde an immediate foothold and rapid zeppelin access deep inside the southern Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"aggro'gosh","grom'gol","gromgol","orgrimmar","stonard","stranglethorn","undercity","zeppelin"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:stonard","zone:undercity","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:booty-bay","zone:duskwood","subzone:kargath","topic:horde"},src={"Grom'gol Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:gurubashi-arena"] = {t="subzone",n="Gurubashi Arena",z="stranglethorn",s="Gurubashi Arena is an ancient stone colosseum standing in southern Stranglethorn Vale, originally built by the mighty Gurubashi Empire. In the present day, it serves as a chaotic free-for-all proving ground where pirates and wandering brawlers shed blood over locked chests of treasure.",h="Gurubashi Arena is an ancient stone colosseum standing in southern Stranglethorn Vale, originally built by...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Blood",b="Long before human or orc set foot in Stranglethorn Vale, the Gurubashi Arena—known also as the Great Arena—was built as a monument to martial strength by the sprawling Gurubashi troll empire. In ancient days, champions fought to the death upon its sands until the earth was slick with troll blood.",sp=0},{t="The Booty Run",b="Though the empire has long since fractured into warring tribes, the arena's floor never stays clean for long. Today, lawless buccaneers and ruffians oversee a different sort of bloody spectacle. A pirate named Short John Mithril oversees the grounds, where every few hours a chest of plundered booty is hauled into the center of the ring. Anyone who steps onto the floor is fair game—faction allegiances vanish, and combatants must butcher their way to the prize against all comers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Gurubashi Arena?",a="It was constructed centuries ago by the Gurubashi Empire when they ruled the southern regions of the Eastern Kingdoms. It was designed as an enormous stadium for lethal trials of combat and ancient troll rituals honoring the loa.",al={"who made gurubashi arena","arena origin","troll arena lore"}},{q="Why do people fight here now?",a="Local pirates use the arena for illicit entertainment. Every few hours, a pirate captain drags a treasure chest into the center of the sands, prompting a bloody free-for-all brawl among anyone daring enough to step into the ring and claim it.",al={"why fight in gurubashi","gurubashi chest","booty run lore"}},{q="Who is Short John Mithril?",a="Short John Mithril is a pirate who oversees the arena and the regular chest deliveries. He rewards combatants who consistently survive the chaotic brawls and recover his arena treasures.",al={"short john mithril","arena overseer"}},{q="Why can members of my own faction attack me here?",a="The floor of the arena operates under complete lawlessness. Once you cross onto the sands, all faction treaties and military alliances are suspended—only those standing together in your immediate battle party are spared your blade.",al={"why is gurubashi free for all","friendly fire in gurubashi","arena pvp rules"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For trolls, the arena is sacred ground rather than simple pirate sport, a monument of the old Gurubashi Empire where champions once shed blood upon the sands.",["class:Warrior"]="The sands offer one of the purest martial crucibles in Azeroth, stripped bare of grand war politics and reduced entirely to personal grit and raw survival."},kw={"arena","booty run","chest","gurubashi","short john mithril","stranglethorn","the great arena"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","topic:pirate","subzone:booty-bay"},src={"Gurubashi Arena"}}
E["subzone:jaguero-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Jaguero Isle",z="stranglethorn",s="Jaguero Isle is an isolated, jungle-covered island resting off the eastern coast of Stranglethorn Vale's Wild Shore. Dominated by fierce wild panthers and gorillas, it is infamous as the domain of the colossal silverback gorilla known as King Mukla.",h="Jaguero Isle is an isolated, jungle-covered island resting off the eastern coast of Stranglethorn Vale's Wild...",sec={{t="A Primal Domain",b="Situated off the southeastern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, Jaguero Isle stands well apart from the mainland pirate camps and troll ruins. The island is entirely overrun by untamed fauna, mainly panthers and aggressive gorillas. Looming over them all is the gargantuan ape King Mukla, whose rule over the rocky interior is absolute and territorial. Few sailors willingly approach its reefs, though occasionally washed-up bottles along the mainland beaches carry desperate pleas for rescue from those unfortunate enough to be stranded ashore.",sp=0},{t="The Captive Princess",b="The island's most peculiar and perilous situation involves Princess Poobah, a shipwrecked tauren held captive by King Mukla. Cast adrift and marooned on the predator-choked island, she managed to send out distress notes sealed in bottles across the tides of the Wild Shore, hoping a passing adventurer might brave Mukla's wrath and help secure her escape.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Jaguero Isle located?",a="Jaguero Isle is situated in the Great Sea off the southeastern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, just east of the Wild Shore.",al={"jaguero isle location","where is jaguero","find jaguero isle"}},{q="Who is King Mukla?",a="King Mukla is a gigantic, powerful gorilla who reigns over Jaguero Isle. Territorial and aggressive, he dominates the island's interior.",al={"mukla","king mukla gorilla","ape boss stranglethorn"}},{q="Who is Princess Poobah?",a="Princess Poobah is a stranded tauren trapped on Jaguero Isle far from her home. She casts messages in bottles into the sea in hopes of being rescued.",al={"tauren captive","who is poobah","princess poobah"}},{q="How do you start the quest to visit the island?",a="Adventurers often discover her plight by finding half-buried bottles washed ashore along the mainland beaches of the Wild Shore, containing a carefully folded note requesting aid.",al={"message in a bottle quest","jaguero island quest","how to get to jaguero"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Finding a fellow tauren trapped so far from Kalimdor among hostile beasts makes securing Princess Poobah's release a matter of personal honor.",["class:Hunter"]="The exotic predators of Jaguero Isle, from stalking panthers to the mighty King Mukla himself, present an irresistible tracking challenge for seasoned hunters."},kw={"gorilla","jaguero","jaguero isle","king mukla","panther","princess poobah","stranglethorn","wild shore"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:wild-shore","topic:tauren"},src={"Jaguero Isle"}}
E["subzone:janeiro-s-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Janeiro's Point",z="stranglethorn",s="Janeiro's Point is a small, rocky island situated just outside the harbor of Booty Bay in southern Stranglethorn Vale. It is crowned by a colossal stone statue of an unknown goblin welcoming incoming maritime traffic with outstretched arms. The island's waters and shores are dominated by the menacing sea giant known as Mok'rash the Cleaver.",h="Janeiro's Point is a small, rocky island situated just outside the harbor of Booty Bay in southern...",sec={{t="Beacon of the Bay",b="Standing as the monumental gateway to Booty Bay, Janeiro's Point greets every vessel charting a course into the southern seas of Stranglethorn Vale. Atop the crag looms an immense stone effigy of a goblin, arms spread wide in a grand gesture of welcome and unbridled mercantile ambition. Though visible to sailors and corsairs for miles around, landing on the island's shores is a perilous prospect due to Mok'rash the Cleaver, a terrifying sea giant who has claimed the outcrop as his territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Janeiro's Point?",a="Janeiro's Point is a small rocky island just off the coast outside Booty Bay's harbor in Stranglethorn Vale. It serves as a visual landmark for ships approaching the goblin port.",al={"janeiro point","what is this island","booty bay statue island"}},{q="Who is the giant statue on the island?",a="The colossal statue portrays an unknown goblin with outstretched arms. It was raised to welcome trade ships and weary sailors to the commercial haven of Booty Bay.",al={"statue identity","who is the goblin statue","who is depicted"}},{q="What dangerous creature lives on Janeiro's Point?",a="The island and its surrounding shallows are the domain of Mok'rash the Cleaver, a formidable sea giant who poses an extreme danger to any adventurous mariners or swimmers attempting to approach the statue.",al={"sea giant island","who lives on janeiro point","mokrash"}}},kw={"booty bay","goblin statue","janeiro's point","mok'rash","sea giant","stranglethorn"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin"},src={"Janeiro's Point"}}
E["subzone:kurzen-s-compound"] = {t="subzone",n="Kurzen's Compound",z="stranglethorn",s="Kurzen's Compound is a heavily fortified human settlement tucked into the hills of northern Stranglethorn Vale. Established by an expedition dispatched from Stormwind under Colonel Kurzen, the outpost has devolved into a rogue camp of cutthroats and wild beasts following their commander's descent into madness.",h="Kurzen's Compound is a heavily fortified human settlement tucked into the hills of northern Stranglethorn...",sec={{t="Heart of Darkness",b="What began as an official expedition into the untamed jungles of Stranglethorn turned into a nightmare when Colonel Kurzen lost his mind. Rather than fulfilling Stormwind's mission, the garrison broke away from the kingdom's authority, cutting ties with the crown and descending into tyranny. Today, the compound operates like a mercenary stronghold, complete with a functional lumber mill, stables for training captured Stranglethorn panthers and tigers as weapons of war, and an extensive cave complex known as the Stockpile where the rogue soldiers stash their plundered supplies.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Regiment",b="Not all of the expedition's original members followed their commander into savagery. When Kurzen's madness took hold, a faction of his men mutinied and fled west to form the Rebel Camp, sparking a bitter and bloody feud within the dense canopy. From their fortified compound, Kurzen and his loyal men ruthlessly hunt down the deserters, treating any outsider who steps into their jungle domain as an enemy of the expedition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Kurzen's Compound?",a="The settlement is occupied by the rogue remnants of Kurzen's Expedition. These human soldiers, jungle fighters, and mercenaries follow Colonel Kurzen and his lieutenants rather than the laws of Stormwind.",al={"who is here","kurzen soldiers","who lives in the compound"}},{q="Why are the humans here hostile?",a="Colonel Kurzen descended into madness deep in the jungle and abandoned his original allegiance to the Alliance. He and his men now view all trespassers—including Alliance forces and the deserters at the nearby Rebel Camp—as mortal threats.",al={"why do they attack","kurzen hostile","are kurzen friendly"}},{q="What is the cave in the back of the camp?",a="The cave system behind the compound is known as the Stockpile. Kurzen's men use it as a fortified supply depot to store weapons, provisions, and contraband away from jungle scavengers and rebel raids.",al={"cave in kurzen compound","the stockpile","kurzen cave"}},{q="Why are there caged tigers and panthers here?",a="The fighters capture native Stranglethorn tigers and panthers and keep them near the stables. They train these predators into vicious Kurzen War Panthers and War Tigers to defend the compound and patrol the surrounding jungle.",al={"kurzen animals","caged panthers","war tigers"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Kurzen's expedition was sent under the banner of the Alliance, making the outpost's descent into madness a shameful scandal that neighboring rebels desperately seek to rectify.",["class:Hunter"]="The compound showcases crude and violent attempts to domesticate wild Stranglethorn panthers and tigers into frontline beasts of war."},kw={"colonel","compound","kurzen","rebel","stockpile","stranglethorn"},rel={"npc:colonel-kurzen","subzone:rebel-camp","zone:stranglethorn"},src={"Kurzen's Compound"}}
E["subzone:lake-nazferiti"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Nazferiti",z="stranglethorn",s="Lake Nazferiti is a sprawling freshwater lake nestled in the dense jungle of northern Stranglethorn Vale. Fed by a vast river system stretching far north into the mountains, its waters are infested with ferocious crocolisks and snapping frenzies, while its shores host an industrial encampment operated by the goblin Venture Company.",h="Lake Nazferiti is a sprawling freshwater lake nestled in the dense jungle of northern Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="Heart of the Jungle Waterway",b="Lake Nazferiti sits along the Nazferiti River, one of the longest continuous waterways across the southern Eastern Kingdoms. The river traces its origins deep into the northern heights, tumbling down waterfalls from the Redridge Mountains and possibly originating as far inland as Deadwind Pass. Within Stranglethorn, the water widens into this murky lake, teeming with vicious predators like snapping river frenzies and ambush-hunting crocolisks that make casual swimming deadly.",sp=0},{t="Venture Company Encroachment",b="The natural balance of Lake Nazferiti is under siege by the goblins of the Venture Company. Setting up heavy operations along the lake's banks, these ruthless profiteers exploit the jungle's timber and resources with mechanical saws, drills, and clear-cutting crews. Their sprawling base pollutes the waterways and constantly clashes with local wildlife and wandering hunters braving the vale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Lake Nazferiti get its water?",a="The lake is fed by the Nazferiti River, an extensive river network originating high in the northern mountains. Its confirmed source is a waterfall pouring down from the Redridge Mountains, with unconfirmed headwaters reaching as far inland as the crags of Deadwind Pass.",al={"nazferiti river source","where does lake nazferiti come from","water source lake nazferiti"}},{q="Who controls the shores of Lake Nazferiti?",a="The goblin-run Venture Company occupies a major base along the lake's borders. They use the foothold to strip the surrounding jungle of wood and mineral resources, deploying armed overseers and goblin machinery along the water's edge.",al={"who is at lake nazferiti","goblins at lake nazferiti","venture co lake"}},{q="Is it safe to swim in Lake Nazferiti?",a="Swimming in the lake is hazardous. The murky waters harbor packs of aggressive river frenzies and lurking crocolisks, both quick to attack anyone stepping away from the shallows.",al={"lake nazferiti monsters","what lives in lake nazferiti","creatures in lake nazferiti"}},{q="Where is Lake Nazferiti located?",a="Lake Nazferiti is situated in northern Stranglethorn Vale, just south of the border with Duskwood and west of the Zul'Gurub ruins along the main river highway.",al={"lake nazferiti location","where is lake nazferiti","find lake nazferiti"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The shores and depths of Lake Nazferiti offer abundant game, from aggressive river beasts to dangerous crocolisks prowling the reeds.",["race:NightElf"]="The industrial scars left by the Venture Company along Lake Nazferiti demonstrate the raw environmental devastation wrought by unrestrained goblin greed."},kw={"crocolisks","frenzies","lake nazferiti","nazferiti","river","stranglethorn vale","venture company"},rel={"topic:venture-company","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin","zone:redridge","zone:deadwind"},src={"Lake Nazferiti"}}
E["subzone:mizjah-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Mizjah Ruins",z="stranglethorn",s="The Mizjah Ruins are ancient stone remains nestled in northern Stranglethorn Vale, situated just southeast of Grom'gol Base Camp. Long abandoned by their original troll architects, the crumbling structures have been seized by the brute-strength Mosh'Ogg ogres. From this vantage, the ogres launch disruptive ambushes against passing supply caravans traveling toward the Swamp of Sorrows.",h="The Mizjah Ruins are ancient stone remains nestled in northern Stranglethorn Vale, situated just southeast of...",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres",b="Like many of the ancient stone ruins scattered throughout Stranglethorn Vale, the Mizjah Ruins were built by the Gurubashi Empire long before modern empires rose. Today, the moss-choked arches and cracked flagstones are occupied by the Mosh'Ogg clan, primarily brute warriors and crude witch doctors. Far from keeping to their stolen perimeter, these ogres routinely raid nearby supply convoys bound for the Horde settlement of Stonard, transforming ancient history into a persistent, bloody thorn in the side of Grom'gol's commanders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Mizjah Ruins?",a="Like the majority of stone architecture scattered across northern Stranglethorn Vale, the Mizjah Ruins were originally constructed by the jungle trolls of the Gurubashi Empire before centuries of warfare and ruin left them empty.",al={"who made mizjah","mizjah origins","troll ruins mizjah"}},{q="Who lives in the Mizjah Ruins now?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by the Mosh'Ogg ogres, specifically Mosh'Ogg Brutes and Mosh'Ogg Witch Doctors, who have fortified the stone structures as a local encampment.",al={"who lives here","mizjah mobs","mosh'ogg camp"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in clearing the ruins?",a="The Mosh'Ogg ogres dwelling in Mizjah actively prey upon Horde supply lines, ambushing convoys traversing between Grom'gol Base Camp and the outpost of Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"why kill mosh'ogg","grom'gol defense","stonard caravan quest"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Mosh'Ogg presence at Mizjah directly threatens critical Horde logistics, forcing Grom'gol Base Camp to deploy warriors to protect the supply route to Stonard."},kw={"brute","grom'gol","mizjah","mizjah ruins","mosh'ogg","stonard","stranglethorn","witch doctor"},rel={"subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:stonard"},src={"Mizjah Ruins"}}
E["subzone:mosh-ogg-ogre-mound"] = {t="subzone",n="Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound",z="stranglethorn",s="The Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound is a fortified cavern complex in northern Stranglethorn Vale, situated just south of the ruins of Zul'Gurub. It serves as the primary stronghold for the brute Mosh'Ogg tribe in the jungle, dominated by their ruthless ogre mage chieftain, Mai'Zoth.",h="The Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound is a fortified cavern complex in northern Stranglethorn Vale, situated just south of...",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres",b="Carved into the rugged jungle ridges south of Zul'Gurub, the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound swarms with brutish Mosh'Ogg maulers, shamans, and warmongers. The ogres seized the cavernous network as an ideal redoubt against hostile jungle trolls and prowling beasts.",sp=0},{t="Mai'Zoth and the Mind's Eye",b="Deep within the twisting interior of the mound presides Mai'Zoth, the formidable two-headed ogre mage who commands the Mosh'Ogg clan. In his possession is the Mind's Eye, a potent and dangerous arcane relic that enhances his mental and sorcerous grip over his followers. Mai'Zoth's mastery over magic and raw brute force makes entering the deepest reaches of the mound a peril for any traveler braving northern Stranglethorn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound?",a="The mound is inhabited by the Mosh'Ogg ogre tribe, including their warriors, maulers, shamans, and warmongers. They are ruled from deep within the cavern by their two-headed ogre mage chieftain, Mai'Zoth.",al={"who is in the mound","mosh'ogg inhabitants","ogre mound monsters"}},{q="What is the Mind's Eye?",a="The Mind's Eye is a potent magical artifact held by the ogre mage Mai'Zoth within the mound. Its strange arcane power fuels his sorcery and leadership over the local ogres.",al={"what does mai'zoth have","mind's eye relic","minds eye"}},{q="Where is the mound located?",a="The mound is situated in northern Stranglethorn Vale, nestled in the hills just south of the entrance to the troll city of Zul'Gurub.",al={"where is mosh'ogg ogre mound","ogre mound location","how to find ogre mound"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The ogre mage Mai'Zoth wields the Mind's Eye deep within the mound, possessing raw arcane energy unusual for brute ogres."},kw={"mai'zoth","mind's eye","mosh'ogg","mound","ogre","stranglethorn","zul'gurub"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:zul-gurub"},src={"Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound"}}
E["subzone:nek-mani-wellspring"] = {t="subzone",n="Nek'mani Wellspring",z="stranglethorn",s="Perched high in the cliffs above the Southern Savage Coast, the Nek'mani Wellspring holds a fountain of remarkably pure holy water. It is renowned as the only pristine source of fresh water found south of Duskwood. However, this sacred site has recently been overrun by hostile naga explorers who jealously guard its flow.",h="Perched high in the cliffs above the Southern Savage Coast, the Nek'mani Wellspring holds a fountain of...",sec={{t="A Sacred Basin",b="The Nek'mani Wellspring sits tucked away in the jagged coastal heights of western Stranglethorn Vale. Dispensing the only untainted freshwater south of Duskwood, the spring is hailed by various scholars and pilgrims as holy. Because differing cultures and traditions each claim its divine waters were blessed uniquely for their own kind, it remains a subject of intense theological fascination. Despite its spiritual renown, peaceful contemplation here is impossible: a vicious contingent of naga has recently seized the basin and guards the waters against all intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes the Nek'mani Wellspring special?",a="The wellspring produces exceptionally pure holy water, known to be the only untainted, completely fresh water source in the wilderness south of Duskwood. Many religious scholars consider its waters divine, though different faiths squabble over whose people it was originally intended for.",al={"why is nek'mani important","what is holy water of clarity","holy spring stv"}},{q="Where exactly is the wellspring located?",a="It is perched high along the cliffside overlooking the Southern Savage Coast on the western shores of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is nekmani wellspring","how to find nek'mani","nekmani location"}},{q="Who controls the Nek'mani Wellspring right now?",a="An expedition of hostile naga has recently advanced inland from the ocean to claim the sacred basin, viciously attacking anyone who approaches the water.",al={"who is at nek'mani","nekmani monsters","naga at nekmani"}},{q="Why are adventurers sent to this spring?",a="Travelers and researchers seek out the holy water of the spring for powerful enchantments, purifications, and alchemical mixtures that demand absolutely pristine water.",al={"nekmani quests","holy water quest stv","clean water stv"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="The claims of divine provenance surrounding Nek'mani's waters make it a curiosity for priests, though the squabbling over which faith it belongs to is an enduring scholarly dispute."},kw={"holy spring","holy water","naga","nek'mani","savage coast","stranglethorn","wellspring"},rel={"subzone:southern-savage-coast","zone:stranglethorn","topic:naga","subzone:savage-coast","zone:duskwood","topic:troll"},src={"Nek'mani Wellspring"}}
E["subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition"] = {t="subzone",n="Nesingwary's Expedition",z="stranglethorn",s="Nesingwary's Expedition is a rustic hunting encampment situated in northern Stranglethorn Vale, just north of Lake Nazferiti. Established by the famed dwarven marksman Hemet Nesingwary, the outpost serves as a staging ground for hunters seeking to test their mettle against the jungle's fiercest predators.",h="Nesingwary's Expedition is a rustic hunting encampment situated in northern Stranglethorn Vale, just north of...",sec={{t="A Hunters' Outpost in the Jungle",b="Tucked alongside the river north of Lake Nazferiti, this remote encampment is a bustling haven for big game hunters, trackers, and marksmen. Hemet Nesingwary established the camp to stalk the legendary beasts of Stranglethorn Vale, surrounded by seasoned peers like Sir S. J. Erlgadin, Ajeck Rouack, and Barnil Stonepot. Guarded by hired marksmen and supplied by neutral vendors, the camp welcomes anyone capable of handling a rifle or bow, regardless of their allegiances, uniting them under the singular pursuit of tracking down the deadliest predators the jungle has to offer.",sp=0},{t="Pages and Predators",b="Life in the expedition camp revolves around intense competition and grand tall tales. Hunters are continually challenged to master the tracking and slaying of the jungle's native panthers, raptors, and tigers, culminating in hunts for apex beasts. Aside from the thrill of the chase, the camp contends with its own small logistical disasters, notably the scattering of Nesingwary's sprawling manuscript across the wilds, leaving camp scholars eager to recover every missing chapter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who runs Nesingwary's Expedition?",a="The camp was founded and is led by the legendary dwarven big game hunter Hemet Nesingwary, alongside a circle of veteran marksmen.",al={"who leads this camp","nesingwary camp leader","who is in charge here"}},{q="Why is the expedition here in Stranglethorn Vale?",a="The expedition traveled to Stranglethorn to hunt the dense jungle's most dangerous wildlife, including prowling panthers, aggressive raptors, ferocious tigers, and legendary trophy beasts.",al={"what are they doing here","why nesingwary stranglethorn","purpose of camp"}},{q="Is Nesingwary's Expedition friendly to both Alliance and Horde?",a="Yes. The camp operates as a neutral hunting outfit. Nesingwary's hired guns maintain peace so long as visitors respect the camp, welcoming both Alliance and Horde hunters who wish to prove their tracking skills.",al={"is nesingwary neutral","can horde visit nesingwary","can alliance visit nesingwary"}},{q="What is the story behind the missing manuscript pages?",a="Hemet Nesingwary authored an extensive hunting memoir titled 'The Green Hills of Stranglethorn.' Unfortunately, the manuscript's loose pages were lost throughout the wilderness, prompting camp archivist Barnil Stonepot to enlist travelers to recover them.",al={"green hills of stranglethorn story","why are pages scattered","barnil stonepot book"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For marksmen and beast masters, this camp is a proving ground where you can hone your tracking skills against the deadliest predators of Stranglethorn Vale.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing Hemet Nesingwary and fellow Khaz Modan mountaineers carving out a thriving camp amidst the humid tropical wilds is a familiar sight of dwarven grit and love for the hunt."},kw={"camp","expedition","green hills","hemet","hunters","nazferiti","nesingwary","stranglethorn"},rel={"quest:5762","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:lake-nazferiti"},src={"Nesingwary's Expedition"}}
E["subzone:old-port-authority"] = {t="subzone",n="Old Port Authority",z="stranglethorn",s="The Old Port Authority is a bustling, multi-vendor warehouse nestled along the boardwalks of Booty Bay. Beneath its roof, travelers browse everything from exotic pets and firearms to hearty rations and finely crafted weapons.",h="The Old Port Authority is a bustling, multi-vendor warehouse nestled along the boardwalks of Booty Bay.",sec={{t="Commerce on the Boardwalk",b="Perched inside the pirate haven of Booty Bay, the Old Port Authority serves as an indoor marketplace divided into distinct stalls, and its interior buzzes with brisk commerce. Merchants hawk general adventuring supplies, firearms, bows, food, and weapons to scoundrels and privateers alike. It also houses exotic imports, offering colorful birds and nautical oddities straight off the docks to anyone with coin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Old Port Authority?",a="It is a prominent commercial warehouse in Booty Bay partitioned into several market stalls. Adventurers and buccaneers visit it to purchase food, ammunition, weapons, and trade sundries.",al={"what is this building","booty bay warehouse","port authority booty bay"}},{q="What shops are found inside?",a="The warehouse contains five distinct merchant stalls: Nautical Needs, Good Food, Swift Flights, Boomstick Imports East, and Cuts-N-Bruises Incorporated, covering rations, weapons, pet birds, and basic provisions.",al={"vendors inside","shops in port authority","what can i buy here"}},{q="Can you buy pets here?",a="Yes. Inside Nautical Needs, travelers can acquire exotic avian companions such as cockatiels and Senegal parrots, popular sidekicks among the local sailors and privateers.",al={"pet vendor booty bay","parrots booty bay","nautical needs vendor"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The merchants at Boomstick Imports East make this building a dependable stop to restock shot and powder before setting out into the deep jungles of Stranglethorn.",["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary travelers can stop by Good Food to pick up regional cooking ingredients and provisions brought in by passing trading vessels."},kw={"blackwater cartel","boomstick imports","booty bay","cuts-n-bruises","nautical needs","old port authority","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin"},src={"Old Port Authority"}}
E["subzone:rebel-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Rebel Camp",z="stranglethorn",s="Tucked just off the road in northern Stranglethorn Vale, the Rebel Camp serves as a fortified refuge for Alliance soldiers who broke away from Colonel Kurzen. Led by Lieutenant Doren, these troops refused to surrender to the madness gripping their commander's expedition and now fight to survive and undo his descent into tyranny.",h="Tucked just off the road in northern Stranglethorn Vale, the Rebel Camp serves as a fortified refuge for...",sec={{t="A Stand Against Madness",b="When Colonel Kurzen's expedition pushed deep into the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale on behalf of Stormwind, things rapidly fell apart. Afflicted by the dark jungle magic and the curse of the ogre mage Mai'Zoth, the Colonel and his core loyalists succumbed to madness, turning rogue and terrorizing the wilds. A handful of sound-minded soldiers led by Lieutenant Doren refused to participate in the atrocities. Breaking away from Kurzen's Compound, they established this hidden camp in the north to stage a desperate guerrilla campaign against their former comrades.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Perched precariously near the Duskwood border, the Rebel Camp operates under constant threat. Cut off from regular Stormwind relief, Doren relies on covert supplies and defensive armaments—including goblin explosives brokered through Booty Bay—to hold the perimeter against Kurzen's raiding parties. For Alliance travelers venturing south into the savage jungle, the encampment provides a vital first foothold of sanity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the rebels at the Rebel Camp?",a="They are former Stormwind soldiers who were part of Colonel Kurzen's expedition into Stranglethorn Vale. When Kurzen and his inner circle fell into madness and tyranny, Lieutenant Doren led this faction in mutiny to escape and oppose them.",al={"who lives at rebel camp","who are these soldiers","rebel camp alliance"}},{q="Why is it called the Rebel Camp if they are loyal to Stormwind?",a="They are considered rebels only against Colonel Kurzen's command structure. Kurzen was their commanding officer, so defying his orders was technically mutiny, even though they remain loyal to the Alliance and Stormwind.",al={"why rebel camp","are they traitors","who did they rebel against"}},{q="How does the camp survive without official Stormwind support?",a="Operating far from official supply lines, Lieutenant Doren relies on resourceful back-channel connections, including trade with contacts like Krazek down in Booty Bay, who supplies land mines and vital gear to fortify the camp's defenses.",al={"rebel camp supplies","where do they get food","rebel camp logistics"}},{q="Where is Colonel Kurzen located?",a="Kurzen and his deranged followers occupy Kurzen's Compound, a fortified base situated directly southeast of the Rebel Camp.",al={"kurzen location","where is kurzen","kurzens compound"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Rebel Camp is your primary staging ground and safest haven when crossing south over the bridge from Duskwood into Stranglethorn Vale.",["race:Human"]="Watching fellow Stormwind regulars unravel in the jungle is a sobering sight, and Lieutenant Doren desperately needs fellow subjects of the kingdom to help put an end to Kurzen's disgraced outfit."},kw={"colonel kurzen","doren","kurzen","kurzen's compound","mai'zoth","rebel camp","stranglethorn","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"subzone:kurzen-s-compound","npc:colonel-kurzen","npc:doren","zone:stranglethorn","zone:duskwood","subzone:booty-bay","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Rebel Camp"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-aboraz"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Aboraz",z="stranglethorn",s="The Ruins of Aboraz are ancient Gurubashi stone ruins nestled along the southeastern cliffs of Stranglethorn Vale. Once part of the sprawling jungle troll empire, the crumbling terraces now serve as the secluded redoubt for the renegade witch doctor Zanzil the Outcast and his mind-addled thralls.",h="The Ruins of Aboraz are ancient Gurubashi stone ruins nestled along the southeastern cliffs of Stranglethorn...",sec={{t="A Witch Doctor's Domain",b="Perched on the bluffs southeast of the Ruins of Jubuwal and south of the Crystalvein Mine, the weathered masonry of Aboraz has been transformed into an alchemical testing ground. Zanzil the Outcast was banished by the local tribes and the mainlanders alike, retreating here to brew potent mind-altering concoctions and toxic elixirs. Within the stone courtyards, Zanzil exerts total control over an unsettling menagerie of servitors, including shambling undead ghouls, corrupted troll thralls, and even co-opted coastal naga.",sp=0},{t="Pawns and Captives",b="Zanzil's strange potions do not simply poison the body—they shatter the will. Among the lost souls pacing the terraces is the enthralled Darkspear youth Yenniku, whose mind remains locked under Zanzil's sorcery. Joining him in aimless wandering is Chucky 'Ten Thumbs', a pirate debtor fleeing the collection efforts of Booty Bay's 'Sea Wolf' MacKinley, reduced by Zanzil's draughts to an oblivious guardian of the compound.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules over the Ruins of Aboraz?",a="The ruins are controlled by Zanzil the Outcast, an exiled witch doctor infamous throughout Stranglethorn Vale for his dark alchemy and powerful mind-controlling brews.",al={"who leads aboraz","aboraz boss","who is in ruins of aboraz"}},{q="Why are there naga and ghouls together here?",a="Zanzil's unique mixtures allow him to dominate minds and animate corpses. He has bound troll outcasts, risen jungle ghouls, and ensnared coastal naga to serve as unquestioning guards for his terrace.",al={"why are naga here","aboraz ghouls","aboraz mobs"}},{q="Where are the Ruins of Aboraz located?",a="They lie on the high bluffs in southeastern Stranglethorn Vale, south of the Crystalvein Mine and just southeast of the Ruins of Jubuwal overlooking the eastern sea.",al={"aboraz location","where is aboraz","how to get to ruins of aboraz"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, Aboraz is an affront: an outcast using perverted voodoo to enslave fellow trolls and hold young Yenniku hostage in the ancestral lands of the Gurubashi.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance privateers and mercenaries frequently run into Zanzil's affairs when chasing debts or bounties tied to the goblins and pirates of Booty Bay."},kw={"aboraz","chucky","jubuwal","stranglethorn","witch doctor","yenniku","zanzil"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-jubuwal","subzone:crystalvein-mine","zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","topic:naga"},src={"Ruins of Aboraz"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-jubuwal"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Jubuwal",z="stranglethorn",s="The Ruins of Jubuwal are the crumbling remnants of an ancient Gurubashi settlement located just east of the Gurubashi Arena in Stranglethorn Vale. Once a place of empire and ritual, the ruins have fallen under the sway of the rogue witch doctor Zanzil the Outcast and his bizarre retinue of minions.",h="The Ruins of Jubuwal are the crumbling remnants of an ancient Gurubashi settlement located just east of the...",sec={{t="A Refuge for the Exiled",b="Situated off the primary thoroughfare cutting through Stranglethorn Vale, Jubuwal was once part of the grand Gurubashi civilization. Today, stone carvings and ivy-draped masonry have been overtaken by Zanzil the Outcast, an eccentric witch doctor known for his potent concoctions and foul voodoo. Zanzil has filled the ruins with an unnatural menagerie of followers, including enthralled ghouls, subjugated naga, and renegade trolls. Desperate fugitives also lurk among the stone arches, such as Jon-Jon the Crow and Maury 'Club Foot' Wilkins, both hiding from the ruthless debt collector 'Sea Wolf' MacKinley back in Booty Bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Ruins of Jubuwal located?",a="The ruins lie in central Stranglethorn Vale, just east of the Gurubashi Arena and immediately adjacent to the main dirt road connecting northern and southern Stranglethorn.",al={"ruins of jubuwal location","where is jubuwal","jubuwal map"}},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Jubuwal?",a="The ruins are held by Zanzil the Outcast and his minions. His eclectic followers include brainwashed trolls, reanimated ghouls, allied naga, and miscellaneous scoundrels seeking shelter from outside law.",al={"who lives in jubuwal","jubuwal enemies","who controls jubuwal"}},{q="Why are ghouls and naga working together here?",a="Zanzil the Outcast uses toxic voodoo mixtures and mind-altering potions to subdue and command those around him. Through these mixtures, he binds risen undead, naga, and trolls into an obedient fighting force.",al={"why are there ghouls in jubuwal","zanzil minions"}},{q="Why are outlaws like Jon-Jon and Maury hiding here?",a="Both Jon-Jon the Crow and Maury 'Club Foot' Wilkins fled to Jubuwal to escape the wrath of 'Sea Wolf' MacKinley, a notorious debt collector operating out of Booty Bay.",al={"jon-jon the crow","maury club foot wilkins","mackinley debtors"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Jubuwal represents both the tragic collapse of Gurubashi heritage and the twisted perversion of ancestral voodoo practiced by rogues like Zanzil.",["class:Rogue"]="The shadows and crumbling masonry of Jubuwal make ideal cover for ambushing outlaws hiding from Booty Bay's bounty hunters."},kw={"gurubashi","jon-jon","jubuwal","mackinley","maury club foot","stranglethorn","zanzil"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:gurubashi-arena","topic:troll","topic:naga"},src={"Ruins of Jubuwal"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-zul-mamwe"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Zul'Mamwe",z="stranglethorn",s="Tucked away in a mountainous pocket south of the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound, the Ruins of Zul'Mamwe serve as a heavily fortified stronghold for the Skullsplitter troll tribe. Enclosed by steep cliffs on almost all sides, the ancient stone platforms now teem with fierce jungle trolls under the rule of their ruthless chieftain, Ana'thek the Cruel.",h="Tucked away in a mountainous pocket south of the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound, the Ruins of Zul'Mamwe serve as a...",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Skullsplitters",b="The Ruins of Zul'Mamwe represent one of the primary seats of power for the Skullsplitter tribe in central Stranglethorn Vale. Cradled within a natural mountain amphitheater, the site has only a single open approach from the north, making it an exceptional defensive redoubt. From atop its weathered ziggurats and stone terraces, Chief Ana'thek the Cruel directs his warriors and witch doctors, defending their territory fiercely against both intruding adventurers and rival jungle troll tribes.",sp=0},{t="Remnants of an Ancient Empire",b="Like many of the stone settlements dotting the jungle, Zul'Mamwe is a relic of the ancient Gurubashi Empire that once held undisputed dominion over the southern reaches of the continent. Although the grand empire splintered long ago into squabbling, hostile factions, modern Skullsplitters fiercely guard these ancestral stones, continuing age-old tribal rituals amid the overgrown masonry and broken monoliths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Ruins of Zul'Mamwe?",a="The ruins are held by the Skullsplitter troll tribe, one of the two dominant and aggressive jungle troll tribes in Stranglethorn Vale. They are commanded on-site by their chieftain, Ana'thek the Cruel.",al={"who lives here","zul'mamwe trolls","who owns zul'mamwe"}},{q="Where is Zul'Mamwe located?",a="Zul'Mamwe is located in central Stranglethorn Vale, just south of the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound. The encampment is enclosed by towering mountains on nearly every side, accessible primarily through a valley pass to the north.",al={"how to get to zul'mamwe","zul'mamwe location","where is it"}},{q="Why are the Skullsplitters hostile to travelers?",a="The Skullsplitter tribe is fiercely isolationist and hostile to outsiders, seeing all other races and rival troll tribes as trespassers on their ancestral lands. Led by the merciless Ana'thek the Cruel, they attack anyone who approaches their jungle sanctuary.",al={"why do trolls attack","skullsplitter hostility"}},{q="What is the history behind these ruins?",a="The stone structures of Zul'Mamwe date back to the height of the Gurubashi Empire. Following the empire's collapse into warring splinter factions, the Skullsplitters claimed the site as an inland base of operations, preserving its ancient stone terraces.",al={"ruins history","who built zul'mamwe","zul'mamwe lore"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls aligned with the Horde, Zul'Mamwe stands as a sobering reminder of the savage, insular ways of their jungle kin who refused to abandon bloodthirsty traditions and adapt to the wider world."},kw={"ana'thek","ana'thek the cruel","gurubashi","jungle troll","skullsplitter","stranglethorn","zul'mamwe"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:mosh-ogg-ogre-mound","topic:troll"},src={"Ruins of Zul'Mamwe"}}
E["subzone:salty-sailor-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Salty Sailor Tavern",z="stranglethorn",s="The Salty Sailor Tavern is the beating heart of Booty Bay's social life, serving as the port's primary inn and watering hole. Run by the goblin Innkeeper Skindle, it welcomes scoundrels, mercenaries, and travelers from both factions seeking respite from the perils of the jungle.",h="The Salty Sailor Tavern is the beating heart of Booty Bay's social life, serving as the port's primary inn...",sec={{t="A Safe Haven in the Jungle",b="Perched amidst the wooden tiers of Booty Bay, the Salty Sailor Tavern offers warm beds and strong drinks under the watchful eye of the Blackwater Raiders. Behind the bar stands Innkeeper Skindle, keeping glasses filled while a menagerie of buccaneers, traders, and adventurers mingle on neutral ground. Outside the establishment hangs a massive, curious curio—a Zul'Gurub Protector Stone—serving as a strange trophy in this bustling den of commerce.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who runs the Salty Sailor Tavern?",a="The tavern and its inn services are managed by Innkeeper Skindle, an industrious goblin who caters to the assorted sailors, mercenaries, and adventurers passing through Booty Bay.",al={"innkeeper","who is the innkeeper","skindle"}},{q="What is that large stone hanging outside the tavern?",a="Suspended outside the building is a Zul'Gurub Protector Stone, an ominous relic brought back from the ancient troll ruins deep within the jungle.",al={"stone outside","zul'gurub stone","protector stone"}},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde stay here?",a="Yes. As with the rest of Booty Bay, the Salty Sailor Tavern operates under the neutral authority of the Steamwheedle Cartel. So long as patrons mind their manners and do not draw weapons, both Alliance and Horde travelers are free to rest here.",al={"is it neutral","alliance and horde allowed","can horde use the inn"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The crowded, smoky floor of the Salty Sailor makes it the ideal place to swap rumors, listen for pirate chatter, and keep your purse guarded."},kw={"blackwater raiders","booty bay inn","protector stone","salty sailor","skindle"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:zul-gurub"},src={"Salty Sailor Tavern"}}
E["subzone:savage-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Savage Coast",z="stranglethorn",s="The Savage Coast is the rugged western shoreline of northern Stranglethorn Vale, stretching from the southern border of Westfall down toward Grom'gol Base Camp. Prowled by river crocolisks, shore basilisks, and hostile troll tribes, the strand earns its brutal name with every tide.",h="The Savage Coast is the rugged western shoreline of northern Stranglethorn Vale, stretching from the southern...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Strand",b="Running from the cliffs bordering Westfall south toward Grom'gol Base Camp, the Savage Coast marks the perilous western edge of northern Stranglethorn Vale. The sandy banks offer little hospitality: snapjaws, crocolisks, and stonestalkers roam freely among the tide pools and drift logs. Just inland lie territorial jungle troll encampments, making any casual walk along the beach a fight for survival. Offshore, the waters dip toward the submerged dangers of the Vile Reef, ensuring that danger lurks both on the sand and under the waves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Savage Coast?",a="The Savage Coast lines the western ocean edge of northern Stranglethorn Vale. It begins near the border of Westfall in the north and extends southward past the waters near the Vile Reef, reaching down toward Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"savage coast location","where is savage coast","savage coast map"}},{q="What creatures live along the Savage Coast?",a="The shore is overrun by dangerous wildlife, most notably aggressive crocolisks and basilisks that sun themselves on the sand. Just beyond the waterline and along the nearby jungle bluffs, hostile troll tribes maintain encampments overlooking the surf.",al={"savage coast mobs","what is on savage coast","savage coast beasts"}},{q="Is the Savage Coast safe for travelers moving south from Westfall?",a="Not at all. While entering Stranglethorn Vale along the coast bypasses the dense canopy, the Savage Coast is packed with vicious amphibious predators and local troll warriors that quickly overwhelm unwary travelers.",al={"can you walk to stranglethorn from westfall","westfall to savage coast path"}},{q="What landmarks are near the Savage Coast?",a="Directly offshore lies the sunken Vile Reef, while further down the coastline sits the fortified Horde outpost of Grom'gol Base Camp. To the north, the bluffs rise toward the farmlands and coast of Westfall.",al={"savage coast points of interest","what is near savage coast"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The northern stretch of the coast lies just above Grom'gol Base Camp, serving as a perimeter buffer against wildlife and aggressive troll bands near the Great Sea.",["class:Hunter"]="The beaches offer an abundance of crocolisks and basilisks for tracking, skinning, and beast-taming along the shoreline."},kw={"basilisk","crocolisk","grom'gol","savage coast","stranglethorn","vile reef","westfall"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:vile-reef","zone:westfall","topic:troll"},src={"Savage Coast"}}
E["subzone:southern-savage-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Southern Savage Coast",z="stranglethorn",s="The Southern Savage Coast encompasses the long strand of beaches and tidal waters hugging southwestern Stranglethorn Vale. Flanked by the treacherous depths of the South Seas, these shores are home to prowling wildlife, hostile naga, and the ever-present threat of coastal raiders.",h="The Southern Savage Coast encompasses the long strand of beaches and tidal waters hugging southwestern...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Shoreline",b="Stretching down the western edge of the southern jungle, the Southern Savage Coast marks where the mainland gives way to the warm currents of the South Seas. Divided from the northern Savage Coast by the submerged ruins and perils of the Vile Reef, this coastline skirts inlets near the Gurubashi Arena and Nek'mani Wellspring before tapering off past Booty Bay and Janeiro's Point. While the beaches offer open ground compared to the suffocating interior jungle, travelers must contend with aggressive reptilian predators, predatory naga hunting the shallows, and passing corsairs scanning the strand for easy prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Southern Savage Coast begin and end?",a="It covers the southwestern shoreline of Stranglethorn Vale, beginning below the Vile Reef and extending south along the coast past Booty Bay and Janeiro's Point, where it transitions into the Wild Shore.",al={"southern savage coast location","where is southern savage coast","savage coast borders"}},{q="How is it different from the northern Savage Coast?",a="The two stretches of coastline are separated by the Vile Reef. The northern Savage Coast runs along northern Stranglethorn's Great Sea waters, while the Southern Savage Coast lies along the lower cape bordering the South Seas.",al={"difference between savage coast and southern","why two savage coasts","vile reef border"}},{q="What threats can travelers expect along the beach?",a="The open sands are heavily populated by vicious basilisk lizards, snapping crocolisks, hostile naga slithering out of the shallows, and patrols of territorial pirates.",al={"is southern savage coast dangerous","mobs on southern savage coast","threats along the coast"}},{q="Does Booty Bay control this coastline?",a="No. The Blackwater Raiders and the Steamwheedle Cartel maintain control strictly over Booty Bay's harbor and immediate approaches. The wild beaches to the north and south remain lawless, untamed territory.",al={"does booty bay own the beach","steemwheedle control of coast","goblin territory"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The wide open beaches provide ideal tracking ground for amphibious game, coastal cats, and basilisks, offering clear sightlines far preferable to the claustrophobic brush inland."},kw={"booty bay","janeiro's point","savage coast","south seas","southern savage coast","stranglethorn vale","vile reef"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:savage-coast","subzone:vile-reef","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:janeiro-s-point","subzone:nek-mani-wellspring","subzone:wild-shore","topic:naga"},src={"Southern Savage Coast"}}
E["subzone:tkashi-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Tkashi Ruins",z="stranglethorn",s="The Tkashi Ruins are ancient stone remnants situated southwest of Nesingwary's Expedition in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Overrun by hostile Bloodscalp trolls, the site remains a stronghold of the tribe.",h="The Tkashi Ruins are ancient stone remnants situated southwest of Nesingwary's Expedition in northern...",sec={{t="Stones of the Bloodscalp",b="Perched southwest of Hemet Nesingwary's hunting camp, the crumbling stone masonry of the Tkashi Ruins marks the ancient domain of Stranglethorn's jungle trolls. Today, the encampment is heavily occupied by the Bloodscalp tribe, who aggressively defend the territory and practice their shamanistic rituals among the vines and decayed stone. While Hemet Nesingwary noted passing through the ruins without trouble in his hunting memoirs, modern travelers find the trolls far less accommodating, guarding valuable tribal relics buried among the rubble.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Tkashi Ruins?",a="The ruins are occupied by the Bloodscalp tribe, a hostile faction of jungle trolls that aggressively defends the crumbling compound against outsiders and rival tribes.",al={"who is here","tkashi ruins mobs","trolls at tkashi"}},{q="Where are the Tkashi Ruins located?",a="They lie in northern Stranglethorn Vale, just southwest of the river crossing near Nesingwary's Expedition.",al={"tkashi location","where is tkashi","find tkashi ruins"}},{q="What is mentioned about Tkashi in Hemet Nesingwary's writings?",a="In chapter three of his memoir, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn (specifically page 21), Nesingwary records that he and his hunting party managed to traverse the Tkashi Ruins without incident during their early days in the jungle.",al={"nesingwary tkashi","green hills tkashi"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, sites like Tkashi are grim reminders of the ancient tribal ruins left behind by their hostile Gurubashi kin, now fiercely defended by savage Bloodscalp holdouts."},kw={"bloodscalp","nesingwary","stranglethorn","stranglethorn vale","tkashi","tkashi ruins","troll ruins"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","topic:troll","subzone:kurzen-s-compound","topic:alliance","quest:5762"},src={"Tkashi Ruins"}}
E["subzone:venture-co-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Venture Co. Base Camp",z="stranglethorn",s="Tucked away in the dense jungles of northern Stranglethorn Vale, the Venture Co. Base Camp serves as a forward foothold for the notoriously greedy goblin syndicate. Here, hired overseers and laborers exploit the lush wilderness, focusing their efforts on harvesting timber, hunting local wildlife, and extracting valuable tumbled crystals from the nearby waterways.",h="Tucked away in the dense jungles of northern Stranglethorn Vale, the Venture Co.",sec={{t="Industrial Encroachment",b="The Venture Company is infamous across Azeroth for ruthless profiteering and complete disregard for the natural world. At this jungle base camp, steam-powered equipment and makeshift goblin shacks chew into the ancient canopy. Guarded by armed mercenaries, foremen, and field workers, the camp coordinates resource extraction throughout the surrounding valleys, paying particular interest to valuable tumbled crystals found nearby while clear-cutting any jungle that stands in their way.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Venture Company doing in Stranglethorn Vale?",a="The Venture Company operates as an opportunistic mining, logging, and engineering syndicate. In northern Stranglethorn, they have set up camp to log the dense jungle, build heavy operations, and harvest valuable mineral deposits—chief among them the tumbled crystals found around local watercourses.",al={"why are goblins here","venture co purpose","venture company stranglethorn"}},{q="Are the goblins here affiliated with the Steamwheedle Cartel in Booty Bay?",a="No. The Venture Company is a separate, predatory enterprise completely distinct from Baron Revilgaz and the Steamwheedle Cartel. Unlike Booty Bay's merchant princes who cultivate lucrative trade relationships, the Venture Company relies on ruthless exploitation and acts hostile toward nearly anyone who interferes with their bottom line.",al={"is venture co booty bay","are they friendly to booty bay","venture co steamwheedle"}},{q="What lies beyond the base camp?",a="Adjacent to the base camp lies the Venture Co. Operations Center, a more deeply entrenched outpost housing heavy logging apparatus, lumber supplies, and higher-ranking company managers who direct the regional clear-cutting effort.",al={"where does this camp lead","what is adjacent to base camp","venture co operations center"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Venture Company represents unchecked industrial despoilment, tearing into pristine jungle habitats and unsettling the local balance of nature for crude mechanical enterprise.",["profession:Mining"]="The camp serves as an industrial hub for prospecting the jungle, where company prospectors seek raw materials and rare tumbled crystals."},kw={"goblin lumber","operations center","stranglethorn vale","tumbled crystals","venture co base camp","venture company"},rel={"topic:venture-company","zone:stranglethorn","topic:goblin","quest:764"},src={"Venture Co. Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:vile-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Vile Reef",z="stranglethorn",s="The Vile Reef is a submerged, vibrant coral shelf lying off the western coast of Stranglethorn Vale near Grom'gol Base Camp. Beneath its waters, aggressive murlocs make their home among ancient sunken troll ruins, giant clams, and coastal shipwrecks.",h="The Vile Reef is a submerged, vibrant coral shelf lying off the western coast of Stranglethorn Vale near...",sec={{t="Sunken Stones and Coral Beds",b="Stretching beneath the waves of the Great Sea just offshore from Grom'gol Base Camp, the Vile Reef is known for its vivid marine growth and perilous inhabitants. The seabed is dotted with the weathered stonework of submerged troll ruins alongside the enigmatic Altar of the Tides. Flocks of territorial murlocs lurk among the coral shelves and shattered timbers of passing vessels, fiercely defending the shallow waters and preying upon any diver who braves the deep in search of giant clams and rare blue pearls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Vile Reef located?",a="The Vile Reef sits in the Great Sea off the western shores of Stranglethorn Vale, situated directly northwest of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"vile reef location","where is vile reef","how to find vile reef"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Vile Reef?",a="The reef is heavily infested with hostile murlocs that swim among the coral and sunken structures, alongside giant clams resting across the sea floor.",al={"vile reef mobs","monsters in vile reef","who lives in vile reef"}},{q="What ruins are found underwater here?",a="The sea floor contains the remnants of ancient troll ruins and the Altar of the Tides, relics of troll civilization that were long ago swallowed by the ocean.",al={"vile reef ruins","sunken ruins stranglethorn","altar of the tides location"}},{q="Why do adventurers dive into the Vile Reef?",a="Divers risk the murloc-infested waters to explore coastal shipwrecks, investigate the Altar of the Tides, and harvest the giant clams that sometimes conceal precious blue pearls.",al={"why go to vile reef","vile reef treasures","blue pearls stranglethorn"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Resting just offshore from Grom'gol Base Camp, the reef poses a lingering maritime threat to Horde supply vessels and coastal patrols in Stranglethorn Vale.",["race:Troll"]="The sunken stonework and ancient Altar of the Tides serve as a somber reminder of the long-lost coastal territory once commanded by the jungle trolls."},kw={"altar of the tides","blue pearls","giant clams","grom'gol","murloc","stranglethorn vale","vile reef"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:murloc","topic:troll"},src={"Vile Reef"}}
E["subzone:wild-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Wild Shore",z="stranglethorn",s="The Wild Shore is the southernmost coastline of Stranglethorn Vale, where the jungle meets the waves of the South Seas. It serves as a staging ground and anchorage for the Bloodsail Buccaneers, whose ships lie moored along the shallows.",h="The Wild Shore is the southernmost coastline of Stranglethorn Vale, where the jungle meets the waves of the...",sec={{t="Edge of the South Seas",b="Stretching along the bottom tip of the continent, the Wild Shore marks the border where Stranglethorn Vale plunges into the South Seas. To the northwest lies the fortified inlet of Booty Bay, while a shallow ocean strait separates the mainland beach from Jaguero Isle to the east. The beach continues northeast toward the Crystal Shore. Because of its secluded position away from the Blackwater Raiders' direct cannons, the coast has become a hotbed of piratical activity and wild perils.",sp=0},{t="Pirates and Giants",b="The shore is heavily occupied by the Bloodsail Buccaneers, who anchor their wooden ships in the surf and pitch camps along the sand. These swashbucklers use the beaches to stage operations, store illicit cargo, and plan strikes against their goblin rivals. Travelers must also contend with natural hazards of the shore, including prowling beasts and Gorlash, a colossal sea giant who stomps through the surf, crushing anyone caught lingering along the tide line.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Wild Shore located?",a="The Wild Shore forms the very southern coastline of Stranglethorn Vale in the Eastern Kingdoms. It sits south of Booty Bay, looking out across the South Seas toward Jaguero Isle.",al={"wild shore location","where is wild shore","wild shore map"}},{q="Who controls the Wild Shore?",a="The Bloodsail Buccaneers dominate the coastline. They moor several of their ships in the shallow waters and maintain encampments along the sandy beaches.",al={"who lives on the wild shore","wild shore factions","wild shore pirates"}},{q="Who is Gorlash?",a="Gorlash is an enormous sea giant who prowls the shallows along the Wild Shore, threatening both unwary sailors and pirates walking the beach.",al={"gorlash giant","who is the giant on the beach","gorlash wild shore"}},{q="How does the Wild Shore relate to Booty Bay?",a="A rocky point separates Booty Bay from the Wild Shore. Booty Bay serves as the stronghold of the Blackwater Raiders and the Steamwheedle Cartel, making the nearby Wild Shore a natural staging ground for their sworn enemies, the Bloodsail Buccaneers.",al={"booty bay connection","wild shore booty bay"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The Bloodsail camps and anchored vessels offer pickpocketing opportunities and a chance to study rival swashbucklers operating outside the Steamwheedle Cartel's law."},kw={"bloodsail buccaneers","booty bay","gorlash","jaguero isle","pirates","south seas","stranglethorn","wild shore"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:jaguero-isle","subzone:crystal-shore","subzone:southern-savage-coast","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:south-seas"},src={"Wild Shore"}}
E["subzone:yojamba-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Yojamba Isle",z="stranglethorn",s="Yojamba Isle is a cluster of small tropical islets off the northwestern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, near the waters leading up to Westfall. It serves as an offshore encampment for the scholarly Zandalar Tribe, who have established a foothold here to observe the growing crisis in the jungle. From these shores, the Zandalari seek willing champions from both the Horde and the Alliance to confront the ancient horrors awakening in Zul'Gurub.",h="Yojamba Isle is a cluster of small tropical islets off the northwestern coast of Stranglethorn Vale, near the...",sec={{t="The Emissaries of Zandalar",b="While most trolls encountered across Stranglethorn Vale are hostile to outsiders, the Zandalar tribe dwelling on Yojamba Isle maintain an uneasy neutrality. As the ancient priests and lorekeepers of troll civilization, the Zandalari have watched with mounting dread as the Gurubashi trolls within Zul'Gurub turned to Hakkar the Soulflayer. Knowing the world-ending danger a fully summoned blood god represents, the Zandalari have ventured far from their ancestral home to establish this staging ground, calling upon any capable adventurer—regardless of faction—to aid in curbing the threat.",sp=0},{t="Guarded Waters",b="The island rests quietly along the coastline northwest of the Vile Reef and the ruins that haunt the mainland beaches. To the north lies the massive hidden sea-gate of Ironclad Cove, while the surrounding shallows are frequented by wandering sea beasts. Despite its precarious location, the Zandalari camp functions as a tranquil sanctuary where exotic rituals, sacred altars, and ancient knowledge provide solace and power to those preparing to march deep into the jungle's darkest ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the trolls on Yojamba Isle friendly?",a="These trolls belong to the Zandalar Tribe, the revered caste of priests and historians of the troll race. Unlike the territorial Bloodscalp or Skullsplitter tribes inland, the Zandalari have come on an urgent mission to stop Hakkar the Soulflayer in Zul'Gurub, and they recognize that they need the help of outside champions from both the Horde and the Alliance to achieve it.",al={"friendly trolls yojamba","why don't yojamba trolls attack","zandalar friendly"}},{q="Where is Yojamba Isle located?",a="Yojamba Isle is situated in the far northwestern sea of Stranglethorn Vale. It lies just off the coast northwest of the Vile Reef, near the maritime boundary where the southern sea borders Westfall.",al={"yojamba isle location","how to get to yojamba","where is yojamba"}},{q="What is the Zandalar Tribe doing out here?",a="They have established a forward camp to monitor the dangerous resurgence of Hakkar the Soulflayer within Zul'Gurub. From Yojamba Isle, their emissaries recruit, supply, and reward powerful adventurers who are willing to enter the ancient troll city and defeat the corrupted priesthood before Hakkar's full power is unleashed upon Azeroth.",al={"zandalar purpose","what do zandalari want","why are zandalar here"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, meeting the Zandalari is an encounter with the ancient ancestral root of troll civilization, whose traditions, prestige, and demands command deep cultural reverence.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers might be startled to find a peaceful troll encampment so close to Westfall, but the Zandalari put politics aside in the face of the cataclysmic threat of the Soulflayer."},kw={"blood god","hakkar","stranglethorn","vile reef","yojamba island","yojamba isle","zandalar","zandalari","zul'gurub"},rel={"subzone:zul-gurub","zone:stranglethorn","subzone:vile-reef","subzone:ironclad-cove","zone:westfall","topic:troll","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Yojamba Isle"}}
E["subzone:zul-gurub"] = {t="subzone",n="Zul'Gurub",z="stranglethorn",s="Zul'Gurub is an ancient temple city nestled deep in the jungles of northeastern Stranglethorn Vale. Once the glorious heart of the sprawling Gurubashi Empire, it now stands as a perilous stronghold where jungle trolls scheme to summon an ancient, terrible entity into the world.",h="Zul'Gurub is an ancient temple city nestled deep in the jungles of northeastern Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="Heart of the Fallen Empire",b="Thousands of years ago, Zul'Gurub reigned supreme as the vibrant capital of the entire Gurubashi Empire, uniting the jungle troll tribes under its grand stone ziggurats. That golden age shattered roughly fifteen hundred years before the opening of the Dark Portal when a vicious civil war tore the empire apart. A radical sect of priests, the Atal'ai, sought to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer—a bloodthirsty ancient god—to seize absolute power. Though loyalist tribes banded together to defeat and banish the Atal'ai northward into the Swamp of Sorrows, the devastation broke the empire's spine, leaving Zul'Gurub a violent shadow of its former grandeur.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Shadow of the Soulflayer",b="Though exiled, the fanatical worshippers of Hakkar never abandoned their dark devotion. They eventually realized that their dread deity's physical avatar could only be brought forth from the ancient ritual seat of Zul'Gurub itself. Inside the city, dark sorcerers like Jin'do the Hexxer have sought to enslave Gurubashi high priests to conduct blood rituals in Hakkar's name. The jungle surrounding the ruins crawls with hyper-aggressive Gurubashi trolls, driven into a murderous frenzy, making the temple city an epicenter of dread for anyone brave or foolish enough to tread near its borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Zul'Gurub?",a="Zul'Gurub is an ancient temple city in northeastern Stranglethorn Vale. It served as the capital of the great Gurubashi Empire thousands of years ago, but today it is a dangerous, ruined stronghold inhabited by the hostile Gurubashi tribe.",al={"zg history","what is zg","about zulgurub"}},{q="Who is Hakkar the Soulflayer?",a="Hakkar the Soulflayer is an ancient and terrible blood god. Worshipped by the fanatical Atal'ai troll sect, Hakkar demands endless blood and sacrifice, and his cultists have long plotted to bring his physical avatar into Azeroth through dark rituals in Zul'Gurub.",al={"hakkar","blood god","who is the soulflayer"}},{q="Why did the Gurubashi Empire collapse?",a="Roughly fifteen hundred years before the Dark Portal opened, the empire was torn apart by a devastating civil war. The radical Atal'ai priests tried to summon Hakkar, and while the other trolls successfully drove them into exile, the conflict left the empire permanently shattered.",al={"why gurubashi fell","gurubashi civil war","fall of zul'gurub"}},{q="Can adventurers safely explore the ruins?",a="No. Zul'Gurub is exceptionally hazardous. The Gurubashi trolls inhabiting the ruins are violently aggressive and driven by bloody fervor. Treasure hunters and artifact seekers regularly disappear within the stone walls, with very few ever returning.",al={"is zg safe","zg treasure","exploring zg"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear tribe, Zul'Gurub represents both a tragic monument to their ancestors' fallen grandeur and a terrifying warning about the ruinous price of serving Hakkar.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde keeps a wary eye on Zul'Gurub's dark rituals, recognizing that the blood god's return poses an existential threat to the safety of nearby settlements and tribes across Stranglethorn."},kw={"atal'ai","gurubashi","hakkar","jin'do","soulflayer","stranglethorn vale","troll capital","zul'gurub"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","topic:troll","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:dark-portal","topic:horde","quest:2300","npc:mathias-shaw"},src={"Zul'Gurub"}}
E["zone:stranglethorn"] = {t="zone",n="Stranglethorn Vale",z="stranglethorn",s="Trolls, goblins, pirates, and soldiers contest Stranglethorn Vale. South of Duskwood, the old Gurubashi heartland has become a maze of ruins, beasts, and rival camps.",h="Trolls, goblins, pirates, and soldiers contest Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="Ruins of an Empire",b="Zul'Gurub once ruled the vale as the Gurubashi Empire's capital. That rule ended when radical priests summoned Hakkar the Soulflayer, and civil war tore through the region. The Zandalari crushed the blood god's uprising, but the empire never recovered. Now successor factions fight across the jungle. The Bloodscalp hold the northwest, while the Skullsplitter occupy the east. Both tribes slaughter outsiders as they fight to reclaim their ancestral home.",sp=0},{t="Pirates and Profiteers",b="Booty Bay fills the vale's southern tip with trade and sea traffic. The Steamwheedle Cartel carved out the port, and the Blackwater Raiders run it under Baron Revilgaz. Bloodsail Buccaneers anchored along the coast keep the port under constant threat. Farther inland, the Venture Company cuts timber and mines the hills for rare singing crystals.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Wilderness",b="Rival powers meet across the vale's dangerous borderland. The Horde holds Grom'gol Base Camp on the western coast, and goblin zeppelins link it to Durotar and Tirisfal Glades. Alliance loyalists at the Rebel Camp hunt for the rogue Colonel Kurzen. In the thick jungle, famed hunter Hemet Nesingwary leads big-game expeditions. Wanderers drawn to his hunts face prowling panthers, enormous apes, and enemy soldiers.",sp=0},{t="The Madness in the Jungle",b="Colonel Kurzen led a Stormwind expedition into the northern jungle, then went mad and built a tyrannical mercenary redoubt. The Mind's Eye, wielded by Mai'Zoth, an ogre mage from the nearby Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound, ensnared Kurzen's mind with sorcery. The expedition fell into madness, and Kurzen's former men broke away to form the Rebel Camp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Stranglethorn Vale?",a="No single power controls Stranglethorn Vale. Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter trolls, Kurzen's Compound, the Venture Company, and Horde and Alliance military posts hold rival ground. Booty Bay is the largest settlement, governed by Baron Revilgaz and the Blackwater Raiders.",al={"who owns stranglethorn","who rules stv","stranglethorn factions"}},{q="What is Booty Bay?",a="Booty Bay is a port city on the southern bluffs of the Cape of Stranglethorn. Once the human settlement of Blackwater Cove, it was captured by trolls and later secured by the Steamwheedle Cartel. Baron Revilgaz and Fleet Master Seahorn run it as a neutral trading port, linking travelers with Ratchet across the Great Sea.",al={"what is booty bay","booty bay port","who runs booty bay"}},{q="Why did Colonel Kurzen go rogue?",a="Colonel Kurzen went rogue after Mai'Zoth, an ogre mage wielding the Mind's Eye, ensnared his mind. Kurzen had led a Stormwind expedition into the jungle, but grew erratic and despotic. Lieutenant Doren and loyal soldiers broke away to form the Rebel Camp and stop him.",al={"why is kurzen evil","what happened to kurzen","kurzen backstory"},sp=1},{q="What is Zul'Gurub?",a="Zul'Gurub is the ruined capital of the Gurubashi Empire in northeastern Stranglethorn. Fifteen centuries ago, radical priests summoned Hakkar the Soulflayer there, starting the civil war that ended the empire. Vines and ruins cover the abandoned city, but dark rituals still threaten its halls.",al={"what is zg","zul gurub history","capital of gurubashi"}},{q="What was the Stone of the Tides?",a="The Stone of the Tides is a legendary relic from ancient Gurubashi history, found on the coast by a troll warrior. It gave its bearer control over water and elemental summons like a powerful mage, earning the name Tidebearer. Its curse slowly drew each bearer from the physical realm until they walked into the sea and vanished.",al={"stone of the tides","tidebearer legend","gurubashi water stone"}},{q="How do I travel to Stranglethorn Vale?",a="You can walk south from Duskwood across the river border into northern Stranglethorn. Horde zeppelins link Grom'gol Base Camp with Durotar and Tirisfal Glades. From Kalimdor, take the merchant vessel that sails between ratchet in the Barrens and booty bay.",al={"how to get to stv","getting to stranglethorn","stv travel"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, your ancestral homeland is the jungle troll cradle of Stranglethorn. Civil war followed the Gurubashi Empire's worship of Hakkar the Soulflayer, driving tribes like the Darkspear across the seas.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you can rely on Grom'gol Base Camp as a strategic stronghold on the southern continent, supplied by zeppelins from Durotar and the Undercity.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Alliance, you inherit Stormwind's costly efforts to conquer and pacify the jungle. Now hard-pressed mutineers at the Rebel Camp defend the kingdom's interests.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can meet famed big-game hunter Hemet Nesingwary on the northern riverbank. He challenges marksmen to track the jungle's fiercest raptors, panthers, and crocolisks.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can search the humid canopy's riverbanks and coastlines for Wild Steelbloom, Fadeleaf, Goldthorn, and Purple Lotus."},kw={"bloodsail","booty bay","grom'gol","gurubashi","kurzen","nesingwary","revilgaz","stranglethorn","venture co","zul'gurub"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","subzone:zul-gurub","npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:colonel-kurzen","quest:5762","subzone:nesingwary-s-expedition","subzone:rebel-camp"},src={"Stranglethorn Vale (Classic)","Stranglethorn Vale"}}
